// Book · E Comments: every comment of the code, one entry a code, written once. The code carries only the code (// E12); 4. COMMENTS shows them, 5. MASTER ties each to its code, laws and citations. Edit here only.
BOOK("comments", {
 "E687": {"text": "past the lane beside a building, the next ring a pace further out, as many rings as the most people need (Mid's spot further out): every paid unit stands somewhere"},
 "E688": {"text": "a computer's soldier holding a choke whose time is up, or sent to help an ally and still there D285's stay s, goes back to the pool for the next wave (Mid's state 'home', 17-ai and assist)"},
 "E689": {"text": "the tops are made again when a building is finished or lost: a building blocks sight only once it stands finished (N23, Gemini audit 2: a site counted at its built share, so while anything was being built anywhere the whole map's tops were made again every beat)"},
 "E690": {"text": "the dice can tell and set where they are, so a save opened rolls on as it would have"},
 "E691": {"text": "a captive is taken alive: gone from the field with no corpse, no killer and no blow to anyone's nerve; who aimed at it looks again"},
 "E693": {"text": "the arguments the cells point at are made again with each render, so the table holds only what is on the screen"},
 "E694": {"text": "a unit's row of numbers with its side's research applied, kept until the research changes: code reads the stats through here, never the raw table"},
 "E695": {"text": "at rest (paused, a full-screen page, the end) the world draws D340's idle frames a second, as SoRen does; paused, time stands still"},
 "E696": {"text": "the screen stays awake while a match runs; let go when paused, at rest or hidden; a browser without the lock plays on"},
 "E697": {"text": "the page hidden, the sound engine is suspended and resumed on return (was closed, as SoRen's sound.off, which left the game silent until the next touch); it wakes on the finger lifting as well as landing, Safari's rule (Base 26-input; the Nov 7 sound audit)"},
"E698": {"text": "a draw-level change redraws the canvas at its new sharpness; only a real change of the window's size refits the camera, so the view never jumps out to the whole map mid-match (the Nov 7 flow study)"},
"E699": {"text": "the ghost carries its own label on the map, as Base and Mid: its name and price where it fits, else why not; the player never has to look down at the card to know"},
"E700": {"text": "only a touch on or near the ghost moves it; a touch away from it falls through to the camera, so the player can look around while placing (Mid's nearGhost, 26-input.js); before the ghost is set down, the first touch places it; a still tap on a set ghost builds, a move past D.touch.move drags it (N409)"},
"E701": {"text": "the top bar's cells by the Screen book: pause and the small map are live controls; a cell that does nothing is not shown (Base's bar had none)"},
"E702": {"text": "pause stops the clock and opens the Pause menu right under the top bar, by the pause button (N419); the same cell resumes"},
"E703": {"text": "New game asks twice, so a stray tap cannot end a match; then the Start sheet"},
"E705": {"text": "a hazard switched on adds its points to the level (the measure book's hazards.pts); the Start sheet's picks are a setting, copied into the match's own set when it begins, as Base (SET.hz into G.hz): a toggle after Start is the next match's (Albert, Nov 7 19:35)"},
"E706": {"text": "as Base (Albert, Nov 7 20:48: all Base): a pause has no page, it drops the speeds, New game and the volumes under the pause button and says Paused · tap to carry on, and a tap on the open map carries on; the Start sheet and the Welcome back card hold the world paused behind them; a saved game opens behind Welcome back with Resume and New game; the Yard shows only in the test field"},
"E707": {"text": "while a tall sheet (the Start page) is open, messages wait in the post and come out when it closes, so none covers the sheet (Base's land card came after Start)"},
"E708": {"text": "a shell's ticks as a Set, built once from the Shells book: has() is asked hundreds of thousands of times a second, and a Set answers in one step where a list walks"},
"E2180": {"text": "ticked(cap) lists the shells that tick a capability, in book order; the shells never change in a match, so each list is made once, on first ask, and kept (TICKED): bought() asked ticked('Seat') once per shell it looked at, and the trade stop asked for the Post shell every frame. Callers only read the lists, never change them"},
"E709": {"text": "the buildings as their own list, a derived index of things rebuilt only when things change (TV, the things version): buildings are a few dozen among ten thousand things, and most scans want only them"},
"E710": {"text": "a new building slides into the things list at its depth instead of re-sorting ten thousand things, which was a felt hitch every time anyone built"},
"E711": {"text": "the pocket as Mid's (QCS): zone 1's need from the age's price and the first villagers and houses, the home finds by their piles and amounts; Z1 lays Mid's pile counts, each pile carrying its share, and Z3's finds scale from the same totals"},
"E712": {"text": "the computers' first buildings (D342), standing and free when the match begins: Mid's handicap for a player that plays worse than a person; placed by the same site rules the computers always use, so the lanes and the gap from finds hold"},
"E713": {"text": "visibility by CALVIS alone (QK): rain and snow enter as water content, rain by Marshall–Palmer, snow by its fall speed, so the three haze terms come from one source"},
"E739": {"text": "research, as Base's techBtn: its name and cost; a step that cannot start says why on the button in place of its price (its age, the step before, the line busy or full, its building; N17 #18), or its shortfall when only the cost stops it; the first tap on a step tells what it does on the help line and arms it, the second buys it, any other tap disarms (Albert, Nov 8 20:49). A step of your age that waits on another step: the tap also takes you to that step (the first one in the chain that is not itself waiting): its building's card opens with the step ringed thick, or, when no such building stands, the Build page opens on it, marked blue (locked; Albert, Nov 14, N369). The ring: blue, lit when the step can start now, dim when it cannot, green and receding while it runs"},
"E740": {"text": "a building's lines, each as its next step to learn (none when the line is done); another people's lines are left out"},
"E748": {"text": "the ground painted once into the whole picture: tiles, faces, contours, reeds; its grass also onto the season sheet, which is the blades' mask"},
"E749": {"text": "the cache budgets for what is drawn once and kept"},
"E751": {"text": "the ground: nothing before the land is made, then its shapes replayed under the camera at every zoom"},
"E753": {"text": "a figure that moved this step walks; it swings its tool only standing at its work"},
"E754": {"text": "a drawing's size in the world comes from its body's real height in the Mass book: the art is measured once and drawn so it stands that tall"},
"E755": {"text": "how tall a drawing is: from its first to its last painted row"},
"E756": {"text": "the figures' scale: a villager's body height over its drawing's, one for every figure (riders, animals and engines are drawn at the same art scale)"},
"E757": {"text": "a find's scale: its body's height (tree, bush, outcrop) over its own drawing's; a find with no body is drawn as the figures are"},
"E758": {"text": "a tile's flat colour by what lies there; its light is the meadow layer's (D353), smooth across the tiles (N11: a marsh is shallow water; the woods' floor is grass; no rim colour)"},
"E759": {"text": "the shore and the strata as contours: between four tiles' middles the lowest band is laid, then each higher band above its level, so the coast and the sand, dirt and grass edges cut across the tiles instead of stepping; foam on the water's edge; a cliff or a wood keeps its tiles"},
"E760": {"text": "a stone wall laid course by course, each stone with its own faint tint"},
"E761": {"text": "damp moss rising from a wall's foot, fading upward"},
"E766": {"text": "the ring at a unit's feet, full and bright: green picked, blue working, yellow idle (yours); a foe's its side's colour, the wild white (the Colours book's foot, C24)"},
"E767": {"text": "a grid cell's key is a number, row times the land's width plus column, not a string: no text built on every lookup"},
"E768": {"text": "the board point of each tile's middle stepped across the square, not turned afresh for every tile (a stamp of a tower's reach turned a thousand points a beat)"},
"E769": {"text": "a research's needs worked out once and kept: the Tech book does not change in play"},
"E770": {"text": "the pace meter: frames a second and the ms a frame spends on logic and on drawing, averaged over tau s, shown with the Yard's P"},
"E772": {"text": "every tap on the map sounds once, by what it did: a pick the unit's voice, an order the go, a double tap the open chime, a wall's point the place, a wall off the land the err, else the tap"},
"E773": {"text": "the trees as a cast: twelve kinds from the Sprites book (PT1), each a few variants by its own seed; a crown is leaf dabs inside its outline, lit by where each sits; bare limbs grow by twig; evergreen tiers fade light to shade across the tree; drawn once a leaf stage (and snow) and kept"},
"E774": {"text": "which kind a tree is: weighed by where it stands (wet low ground, the plain, the hills), one roll picks the kind and its variant"},
"E776": {"text": "water cells traced like the land: each depth band of the water drawn along its contour, so the shallows and the deep meet in curves, not tiles"},
"E777": {"text": "a tree's leaf stage: the year's place in seasons, each tree a little later or earlier by its own seed (lag)"},
"E778": {"text": "every leaf a tree could hold is placed first, each with its own draw; the ones under the share kept are drawn, so a crown fills in spring and thins in fall, leaf by leaf, never reshuffled"},
"E779": {"text": "the contours painted band by band over the whole piece of land, lowest first, so a band laid in one cell is never painted over by the lower band of the next; then the ice masks filled once each"},
"E780": {"text": "the ice masks, one a step of depth: a lake's water of depth d belongs to step d ÷ the lake's depth (D27) of D350's steps"},
"E781": {"text": "the ice drawn: the mask of the deepest step frozen so far, over the water"},
"E782": {"text": "each water cell adds its shallow part to every step's ice path and its land part to the land path; one fill each, so no seam shows"},
"E784": {"text": "the ice's thickness on a tile by Stefan's law from the degree-days past that tile's onset (or past the day a hole broke it), thinner growth under snow; what it holds at failure by Gold's formula"},
"E785": {"text": "who may step on ice: yours unless told to go around; the computer and the wild only where the ice holds several of them at the safe load"},
"E786": {"text": "your crossing for a unit: its own, else the one you chose to remember for this winter or this game, else normal"},
"E787": {"text": "stepping from land onto the ice keeps the crossing: wait for an answer; one at a time waits while others of yours are on the ice; file and thin out wait while one of yours is on the ice within the gap"},
"E788": {"text": "the thinnest ice on the way of the units asked about, what it holds safely, and what the units weigh (each its own mass: body, mount and kit, the Mass book)"},
"E789": {"text": "clear off: everyone of yours on the ice goes to the nearest land"},
"E790": {"text": "each beat the ice under every loaded tile of deep water is weighed (a thaw leaves them on ice too thin to hold anyone): over the safe load it cracks (heard and seen), and after the warning it breaks at a chance growing with the square of the overload, at once past failing; the tile's people fall through, those near at a chance"},
"E791": {"text": "the holes and the cracks drawn over the ice: a hole open water ringed with broken edge, a crack's rays growing over the warning"},
"E792": {"text": "the ice card's answers: a way to cross for the units asked about, remembered for this winter or this game if picked; go around orders them again off the ice; clear off"},
"E794": {"text": "an order whose way crosses ice asks how to cross, unless a remembered answer stands; they wait at the shore meanwhile. Nov 13 (N359): the woods are asked about for soldiers only, whose line and arrows the trunks break; a villager just walks through, slower, and is never stopped at the trees to be asked how an army should go"},
"E795": {"text": "ice cracking under yours: the warning said and a clear-off button beside it until all of yours are off the ice"},
"E796": {"text": "one who falls through the ice is lost, as any death, and leaves no body on the ice (under); a crack, or one of a side drowning, takes that side's people off the ice and keeps them off it a season (iceShy, E1017)"},
"E797": {"text": "a frozen lake under snow: white as the land, with wind-scoured streaks of ice and a rim line at the shore, so it still reads as a lake; made once per ice step and snow step"},
"E763": {"text": "a figure's lines in its own darker shade, never black: while a figure is painted (RIM), a stroke asked in ink takes the fill's shade, or a soft ink under a gradient, and a thinner line (the Sprites book's cut, PF2)"},
"E764": {"text": "the person's cut: anchors at the shoulder, hip, hem, ground and face; the tunic, robe, armour, apron, hair and coif drawn as curves from them; sleeves as bowed strokes with a rim, ending in a hand"},
"E762": {"text": "a person in true proportion: long legs, a torso, a small head, a slim build, from the Sprites book; the head and its helm drawn smaller about the neck"},
"E741": {"text": "an event's knobs (damage, speed) while it runs, and how far through it is"},
"E743": {"text": "the mirage: an army seen on the small map ahead of your Town Center toward the middle, told with its square; at its end, told it was not there"},
"E744": {"text": "the circus crosses the land like the wagon; a villager near a performer is cheered and gathers more for a while"},
"E745": {"text": "the aurora: curtains of green and violet over the top of the glass, swaying unless motion is stilled"},
"E746": {"text": "an event with its own picture draws it over the map"},
"E747": {"text": "the mirage's dots on the small map, in the colour of what is coming"},
 "E735": {"text": "the hammer carries the receding brown ring for every site going up (the mean of their progress; Albert, Nov 10, #21: the Build button is the aggregator of all builds), People the green ring while the seat trains, and People is ringed blue while anyone stands idle (Base, items 19 and 20); with no hazard ticked each is drawn by lot at D309 lot odds, Base's HZ_ODDS, and the first message says the level (item 5)"},
"E734": {"text": "a yield's first age is the earliest age of anything that costs it (units, buildings, research, the ages themselves), Base's firstAge; a job is locked until then and a tap on it says when it opens (the Nov 7 re-read, item 21)"},
 "E731": {"text": "the Controller's parts (Albert Nov 11, N325): its words J50, its sizes SN41, its thin icons SN42, its tints C37; 'soldiers' are the picked that are armed; a pad cell is one button, dimmed when its verb says why not. Before N25 the war station's middle was the small map with five pages (Train, Squad, Set up, Direct, Field): parked, see Parked.md"},
"E730": {"text": "the Build card as Base's: opening it reads the middle of the view and opens the tab of what fits there, marked blue with Fits here; a second tap on the Build tab closes it; each row is the name, built/limit (limitOf), the price in green or the lock (its age, research, need) in grey; tapping the picked building again cancels the ghost"},
"E729": {"text": "the sky's washes (the dusk glow, the night blue, fog, rime, the flash, the visibility veil) are composed into one colour and laid in one pass, exactly as the six would have painted in turn (each over the last: c = cᵢaᵢ + c(1 − aᵢ), a = aᵢ + a(1 − aᵢ)); the top bar's height is measured once, not read from the layout every frame (SoRen 70-render; the Nov 7 read); with no top bar (a full card open) the sky's band starts at the top of the glass"},
"E728": {"text": "a close bolt startles as Mid's did: the picture whites to its flash (D113 flash), the ground shakes (the jolt, D113 shake), the thunder follows by the real delay; a sheet flash is the far one"},
"E727": {"text": "a blow from beyond melee reach (D.flanking.melee, the combat book's own line) is a missile: its hit is the arrow's sound, as Base's (the Nov 7 sound audit); research done is heard as a build done"},
"E726": {"text": "the place bar says what Base's said (J34): where to press, then the name with 'tap Build, or drag it to move', the pieces of a line; Build and Cancel"},
"E725": {"text": "the finger's target is lift px a zoom ABOVE the figure's foot, its body; the sign was turned, so the target sat below the feet and a tap on the figure fell on the ground (the sword): Albert, Nov 7 20:30"},
 "E723": {"text": "the sound engine is woken the moment it is made: a phone makes it asleep until a gesture resumes it, so the first taps were silent"},
"E721": {"text": "the path search keeps its working memory between searches (typed arrays stamped by a search number, a heap in two arrays): no Maps, Sets or objects made per step, so a search costs its steps and nothing else; the answer is the same path"},
"E720": {"text": "the forest is Mid's (D345, N249): a jittered lattice scored by an organic field, thicker away from home, the best trees kept, three winding paths out; the wall band round a home and the zones' tree shares (D50, Z1–Z4 trees) are gone with their circles"},
"E719": {"text": "rain and snow are drawn on the glass, as Mid's: the biggest drop crosses the screen at glass px/s whatever the zoom, the rest by their real ratios (Atlas); drawn in the world's metres a far view left them hanging as hairs (Albert, Nov 7 20:01); weather is information, never switched off: a phone shedding motion draws a share of the drops, Reduce motion holds them still (SoRen's; Albert, Nov 9)"},
"E718": {"text": "the Start sheet as Base's: the Start button one slot tall, the people's blurb two lines (the unit and its wonder; the history stays in the Guide), so the sheet fits a phone with the browser's bars (Albert, Nov 7 19:40: ridiculously tall); the speeds ×1 ×2 ×3 drop under the pause button while the match is paused, as Base's spdPop; a speed picked resumes the match"},
"E717": {"text": "the eye sees the ground's light, not the sky's: the lux × the albedo of what covers the ground, snow four times grass (D117 albedo, N248), by the snow's share of full cover"},
"E716": {"text": "the guide lines, Base's PDF guides (Build 63; Albert, Nov 8: locked): a dashed line along the board's rows (the land turned a little, so they read level and upright) wherever the ghost lines up with one of yours within guide: centre to centre, edge to edge, or flush (D206 align: the ghost's side, then its), so two or three can show at once; counted in half tiles (a middle may sit on a half); drawn pad past both"},
"E715": {"text": "the loop as Mid's (41-boot frame): the world steps at a fixed rate (D343) however the frames come, catching up at most catchup steps; a frame between two steps draws each figure the fraction of the way, so walking is smooth at any frame rate and a slow phone does half the work it did at 60 steps a second; lvx, lvy are where it stood before the step"},
"E714": {"text": "the glow's gradient is the inverse-square law itself (QCU), sampled at falloff stops, instead of two guessed stops"},
"E1": {"text": "First Keep v100 · the world reads its numbers from the Books (books/*.js), never from here: one home each."},
 "E2": {"text": "A Book entry is { key, value, name, cite, law } under its code; the game sees each book as one object by key (D, A, C, W, G), and a shell's slot points at a code (D53, D86.walk)."},
 "E3": {"text": "every code in every book"},
 "E4": {"text": "a slot's pointer, read"},
 "E5": {"text": "S the shells (books/shells.js): a row names its layer, ticks its capabilities (SC) and points each slot at a book. has() is the one way the code asks what a thing can do."},
 "E6": {"text": "The frames (QBD). The grid is square in its own frame; the board frame is the grid turned A1 about the site's middle; the view foreshortens depth by sin A2 and shows height by cos A2."},
 "E7": {"text": "QBE: the most a tile may step up or down over its own width and still be a slope"},
 "E8": {"text": "QBK the art frame: a building is painted with its front along x and sheared by SKEW so that edge follows the grid; its depth is ART_T a unit of width, the back standing ART_S of that to the right"},
 "E9": {"text": "QBF the dice (N65): one seed, Mulberry32. Every roll names Who, What, Where, When, Why and How beside it (L13)."},
 "E10": {"text": "two streams from the map's seed, dealt fresh at makeUnits: the rules' (M1), so the same seed plays the same game, and the looks' (D187), so a look never shifts a rule roll"},
 "E11": {"text": "QAZ a fractal line (N60): K waves, the k-th of amplitude k^(−H), H = 2 − Dim; a coast's Dim is about 1.25. Returns a function of the way along, in radians, giving −1 to 1."},
 "E12": {"text": "QAZ as a surface: K plane waves in rolled directions, the same amplitudes; scale is the longest wave in units. Returns a function of (x, y) giving about −1 to 1."},
 "E13": {"text": "The coast (L2 Cut at the board's edge; L4 Edge). Where it stands out it is a headland and a cliff, where it bends in a bay and a beach (QBG)."},
 "E14": {"text": "The roll: Who the map · What how far the coast wanders in and out · Where the coast only; within D3's Z3 of every corner the same wander (L12), blending over D7 into one free along the middle of each side · When the map is made · Why no two maps share a coast, and every home gets the same one · How QAZ on the dice."},
 "E15": {"text": "pos: the way along the side from its start; returns [wander, cliffness]"},
 "E16": {"text": "−1 bay to 1 headland"},
 "E17": {"text": "The ground: one height a tile. Depth is the way in from the coast (negative at sea). Land stands at D13; a beach falls to the water over D16, a cliff over D17 (L4); the sea deepens with distance. The stratum a tile shows is whichever its height reaches (L1)."},
 "E18": {"text": "height, depth from the coast, the four drawn corner heights, the forest floor"},
 "E19": {"text": "marsh (TW1): always wet (KI1)"},
 "E20": {"text": "the way in from the coast at a board point, and the coast's cliffness there"},
 "E21": {"text": "the drawn corners (QBE): at every grid corner the tiles round it are sorted by height and split where a step passes the angle of repose; each group shares one height, so a slope meets without a crack and a face stands where it should"},
 "E22": {"text": "Floor 2, terrain (layer 90): every piece is a Cut or a Raise on the one height field (L2, L3); the layer that shows follows (L1), a step past the angle of repose is a face (QBE)."},
 "E23": {"text": "a spot in a corner's own frame (u along one edge, v along the other), the frame turned with its corner, the same in all four (L12)"},
 "E24": {"text": "the four roads: corner to middle"},
 "E25": {"text": "every tile whose middle lies within r of a board point: fn(k, d, dx, dy)"},
 "E28": {"text": "a channel: discs along a line; w the half-width, deep the bed; the bank falls over D32"},
 "E30": {"text": "The home cove: every corner · the pond, a channel to the sea, a ford midway (his 'bridges', N407)"},
 "E31": {"text": "The land's shape: the seed's relief; the same plain at every home (Z3); the pocket and the middle graded flat (D380). Lakes: each joined hollow, its deepest point and inner reach"},
 "E32": {"text": "Water from the shape, once: Priority-Flood from the sea (N402), flow to the lowest neighbour, rivers from A·S^1.27 (N403) 2 tiles wide and up, marsh by wetness (N404), banks at D32"},
 "E33": {"text": "Fords (TC4): where a river crosses a lane from a home to the middle, and once along each river"},
 "E38": {"text": "Forest (TF1): Who the map · What where the trees grow (the trees themselves come on floor 3) · Where a wall round every home at D50 with the road through it (the same for all, L12); elsewhere each zone's tree share (D63–D66): none in Z1 and Z2, thickening across Z3 to Z4's own (QCP); never on water, slopes or roads · When the map is made · Why woods to cut, to hide in, to go round, and room to build out near home (Albert, Nov 6) · How QAZ as a surface, scale D48, ranked so each zone holds its share (QCP)"},
 "E39": {"text": "the wood's edge keeps one tile from any slope or water"},
 "E40": {"text": "Floor 3, non-movables (layer 100): shells with no Walk, an Amount and a Yield (S). Each stands on one flat tile of land; a big one takes the tiles under it. Nothing here moves; floor 5 takes from the amounts."},
 "E41": {"text": "the finds (layer 100), from their shells: kind → code, yield, amount, the ground kept clear"},
 "E42": {"text": "QBJ the pocket's store, one age up calculated (D62: the age's price, the villagers and the buildings at their costs, with the margin); a kind's finds in a zone are its pockets' worth (D63, D65), at least one"},
 "E43": {"text": "what stands on each tile, and the shells themselves"},
 "E44": {"text": "the free tile nearest a spot"},
 "E45": {"text": "a shell on a tile; its stand wanders within the tile by D82 on the dice, so no wood is a grid"},
 "E46": {"text": "the n free tiles nearest a spot: a grove (marked as woods, the trees follow) or a berry patch"},
 "E47": {"text": "The home finds: Who every corner · What the pocket's berries, grove, gold and stone at D70's spots, sized by QBJ, the home cluster alone laid with its count and amount times D62's near (bushes half again, each as full as before: Albert, Nov 14, N369); Z3's finds (D65) at three pockets' worth, laid by the Randomizer in the ring between Z2 and Z4, off the road; the land's specialty once more · Where the corner's own frame, the same in all four (L12) · When the map is made · Why every player starts with the same ground and the same means to the next age · How one home dice (QBF), restarted at each corner, so the corners match"},
 "E48": {"text": "Z4's finds: Who the map · What piles of gold, stone and iron, berry patches, and the gifts: ruins, cemeteries, campfires, treasure · Where Z4, on flat free land, off the roads, the middle and the play edge · When the map is made · Why the game beyond the homestead is to be found, not known · How counts D73–D81, places uniform until one is clear, each a roll"},
 "E49": {"text": "The trees: Who every tile of woods (TF1, and the groves) · What one tree, its stand, size and shade · Where its tile · When the map is made · Why the woods are what is cut for wood (R1) · How three rolls a tile"},
 "E50": {"text": "drawn back to front"},
 "E51": {"text": "a tree with trees on all eight sides is deep: nothing can stand between it and its neighbours, so the deep woods are painted once a chunk (see the woods cache)"},
 "E52": {"text": "0 water, 1 sand, 2 dirt, 3 grass; bare dirt again high over the land (D23)"},
 "E53": {"text": "the first band is what can be waded (D24) (N11: three sheets of water, shallow to deep)"},
 "E54": {"text": "the forest floor: the grass, shaded; the marsh: the grass, toward the water (N11: the paper sheets from the waterline up: wet sand, sand, the dirt lip, grass; grass is a light neutral the season colours, E902)"},
 "E55": {"text": "what a face shows between two heights (L1): the grass is the land's top skin; anything raised above it shows bare earth"},
 "E56": {"text": "Drawn once in the view frame: every tile a lifted quad, a face where it steps down toward the camera. Then every frame is one picture, moved and scaled."},
 "E57": {"text": "the masks at a quarter scale: the land in white and in shadow, the inland water"},
 "E58": {"text": "a quad a, b, c, d (top-left round to bottom-left on the screen) grown half a pixel right and down, so the next tile's edge lands on solid paint and no seam shows"},
 "E60": {"text": "the ground is painted flat; the light stands high to the left and in front and the meadow layer lights it (D353 lit): ground leaning that way warm, ground leaning away cool"},
 "E61": {"text": "runs: flat tiles of one colour in a row drawn as one quad (no seams, few fills)"},
 "E62": {"text": "faces: the +y edge and the +x edge face the camera (the turn is under 45°)"},
 "E63": {"text": "The view (layer 140): one camera, drag to pan, pinch or wheel to zoom; the overlays are drawn each frame over the one picture."},
 "E64": {"text": "(the Pace meter starts on when the page is opened with ?fps, so a phone can show it: Albert, Nov 10 20:02) one flag a layer code (the panel, floor 8) and Fast"},
 "E65": {"text": "The door (floor 8): the modules (menu, econ, combat, ai) hang on these hooks and read the world through FK; nothing else of theirs touches this file"},
 "E66": {"text": "the hooks: every named moment one part fires (FK.fire) and others answer (FK.on), from tick and draw to save and load; event: a named happening (a blow, a drop, a raise) that the sound and the feel answer, by the names in books/sound.js HE1; befell: something first befalls an order (E1296); ended: an order has no one left"},
 "E67": {"text": "a slow beat's turn (D182–D184): the step whose seconds played cross it, its phase in Mid's frames (D98)"},
 "E68": {"text": "the screen jolts with a heavy impact (QBT)"},
 "E71": {"text": "The brushes (preview 49, 18-figures.js): a polygon, an ellipse, a line, two gradients; g is the canvas being painted"},
 "E72": {"text": "The building art (preview 49, 19-building-art.js; Nov 3, the last build before the camera turn): every piece drawn from its own point lists, in units, feet at (0, 0), the front edge along x, the back up and to the right. A building's level and its research footing are skins (PB3, PB4, PB6, PB12); civs, seasons and flags are cut."},
 "E73": {"text": "a building picture's height, from its look"},
 "E74": {"text": "The node art (the same file): six trees, three bushes, stone, gold and iron; r is a dice for the leaf blobs"},
 "E75": {"text": "The figures (preview 49, 18-figures.js): people and beasts drawn from data, feet at (0, 0), facing right, a person about 21 tall; fr 0–3 the walk, 10 and up at work (the tool, two poses). One look a code; the soldiers' looks are Mid's own (F18), the rest of the roster stays in preview 49 as skins."},
 "E76": {"text": "the brushes: one drawing routine a shape; a look in books/sprites.js names its brush and the brush's settings ($side the owner's colour, $side*0.6 a tint of it, any colour*0.6 a tint of that)"},
 "E77": {"text": "a figure's frame, from its look"},
 "E78": {"text": "B the buildings (layer 110; shells without Walk): the size in tiles (D8–D11; a wall piece is one tile, D12), Open or Closed (S Styles), the picture it wears. Health, prices and times come with the Content pull."},
 "E79": {"text": "the buildings (layer 110), from their shells: name, size in tiles, Open, the picture, what it takes in"},
 "E80": {"text": "a building stands on n × n flat free tiles from (i, j); Closed takes them (OCC 2), Open leaves them walkable (OCC 3)"},
 "E81": {"text": "The Town Center: Who every corner · What one · Where Z2 on the road at D84, the same in all four (L12) · When the map is made · Why the game starts with a hall to gather at · How no roll: fixed"},
 "E82": {"text": "Floor 5, movables (layer 120): U units and M moveables are shells that walk. Each stands at a board point, walks tile to tile along a path (QBL), and does one thing at a time."},
 "E83": {"text": "one a corner (C5–C8); the player is 0"},
 "E84": {"text": "the units and moveables (layer 120), from their shells: name, look, pace (a D86 key)"},
 "E85": {"text": "the tool a villager works a find with (WORKTOOL): axe, hands, pick, from the Sprites book (PN1 tool), the one home econ.js reads"},
 "E86": {"text": "walking (L5, top rules): land or a ford is walked; a thing, a closed building or a step past the angle of repose is not"},
 "E87": {"text": "inland water bearing ice (QQ): walked as if flat; ice bears where its depth step is behind the walking front (K.iceOn)"},
 "E88": {"text": "the pace's books (QCB): its states and Pandolf's coefficients (D224), the friction a step needs (G9), slipping (G10); the player's side, told when its people slip"},
 "E89": {"text": "QBL A* over the tiles, the eight ways of D198, straight 1 and diagonal √2, the heuristic the octile distance (N74). goal(k) says when a tile will do; returns the tiles to walk, or null. Each open entry keeps the priority it was pushed with; a tile reached again by a shorter way is pushed again, and the old entry is skipped when it comes up (lazy deletion: the heap's order never changes under it)"},
 "E90": {"text": "most: the tiles it may open before giving up The search is weighted (f = g + D.tries.weight × h, N446): it opens far fewer tiles for a way that is at most that many times longer than the best, so a long way round through woods is found within the budget"},
 "E91": {"text": "the tiles one step from a tile, by the eight ways of D198, that a walker may step to (walkable, within the slope); no cutting a corner; the pathfinder and the reach both step by it"},
 "E92": {"text": "a unit on a tile; its stand wanders in the tile (D82)"},
 "E93": {"text": "a path of one tile (already there) walks to its middle: no step past the end"},
 "E94": {"text": "to a tile"},
 "E95": {"text": "to a tile beside one"},
 "E96": {"text": "the one distance and the one nearest search; the drop-off for a yield is the side's nearest building that takes it in (SC Drop-off, B's fifth field), a find the nearest of its kind within reach"},
 "E97": {"text": "to a tile along a building's edge (the ring of tiles round it, byB)"},
 "E98": {"text": "a find used up is gone; its tile is free again"},
 "E99": {"text": "one tick for every unit"},
 "E100": {"text": "walking: toward the next point at the walker's pace (QCB) over the ground it steps onto; true when it gets there"},
 "E101": {"text": "metres walked, which turn the stride (QBU); its speed now, which a blow carries (QBT)"},
 "E102": {"text": "wildlife wanders: after a Poisson wait (QM, mean D94) it walks to a free tile within D95"},
 "E103": {"text": "M3 the grids (a spatial hash): units by squares of D185, refiled after each step's walking, buildings by D186; a new unit is filed as it comes. A search looks only nearby"},
 "E104": {"text": "every unit within r of from (a square), never itself"},
 "E105": {"text": "the buildings within r of (x, y) by their squares, a little beyond on the edges; refiled when one comes or goes (Mid's rule); stops when fn says true"},
 "E106": {"text": "the rules' dice and the looks', from the map's seed but not its stream"},
 "E107": {"text": "The villagers: Who every side · What D67 villagers · Where round its Town Center · When the game starts · Why hands to gather and build · How the free tiles nearest the hall"},
 "E108": {"text": "The wildlife: Who the map · What herds of deer and packs of wolves · Where Z4, on walkable ground · When the map is made · Why food to hunt, teeth to fear · How counts D90–D93, places uniform until one walks"},
 "E109": {"text": "which walkers, how many groups and how big: the book's (D181)"},
 "E110": {"text": "what carries a walker: its mount, else its own body (W)"},
 "E111": {"text": "The body's laws (Book 1): mass from what a shell is made of (W), the blow that sends a body off (QBT), the slide to rest on the ground under it (G), the sway of the wounded (QBS)"},
 "E112": {"text": "QBT: the whole striker when it moves, else its weapon; the struck one is sent off at v = m·v ÷ (m + M)"},
 "E113": {"text": "QBT: friction slows it by μ g a second until it rests; anything it cannot stand on stops it"},
 "E114": {"text": "the mean speed over the step, so the slide ends where v² ÷ 2μg says"},
 "E115": {"text": "QBS: none while the body holds (classes I, II); grows over class III to the tipping angle; there in class IV. Its rhythm the body's pendulum"},
 "E116": {"text": "a unit's picture: its look at its frame, its rank and its side's armour kit, facing right, painted once per look, colour, rank, kit and frame (LOOKBOX gives the box); a look marked elite carries the gold pennant at a rank (Mid's sprite)"},
 "E117": {"text": "The things, drawn each frame back to front, only those on the screen. A picture is painted once per look and zoom step, then stamped (the sprite cache); far out (D83) a node is a dot. The gifts are drawn direct, as tints of C."},
 "E118": {"text": "W × H units, the art's origin at (tx, ty), its anchor (the point stamped at the thing's stand) at (ax, ay)"},
 "E119": {"text": "the node art's own small dice, seeded by the variant, so a tree's leaves fall the same each paint"},
 "E120": {"text": "each drawn at its stand (x, y on the screen), s pixels a unit"},
 "E121": {"text": "a find far out, from its look"},
 "E122": {"text": "Floor 6, climate (layer 130): one sky over the whole board (185 m across: one weather), acting on everything below (L7). The clock is Y: a day D20, a season D21, a year D22."},
 "E123": {"text": "QA the sun: sin a = sin φ sin δ + cos φ cos δ cos H; φ D99, δ swings ±A7 over the year from the spring equinox, H turns with the day (noon at the day's middle)"},
 "E989": {"text": "the picked bar acts on the picked soldiers only and says what it did (Mid's phold, precall; Albert, Nov 11)"},
 "E990": {"text": "the clock reads the sun: the day's noon (D341) shows 12:00 (Albert, Nov 11)"},
 "E991": {"text": "the light between the ramp's points: a cubic Hermite with Fritsch-Carlson slopes, flat at both ends, so dusk and dawn fade without a corner (D369)"},
 "E992": {"text": "a computer's side sees in a plain circle of its sight: it knows what is there, no rays through woods and hills (Albert, Nov 11; the late game spent 43% of its logic casting rays for four sides)"},
 "E993": {"text": "the save lives in the phone's IndexedDB (hundreds of MB, the browser's own big store), mirrored in STORE so reading is instant; the small localStorage (about 5 MB for the whole site, shared by every folder) is no longer used (Albert, Nov 11: one save, kept)"},
 "E994": {"text": "an old save left in localStorage moves to IndexedDB once, and every First Keep key there is cleared to free the site's small store"},
 "E995": {"text": "the newest tab owns the save: a tab told another has opened pauses and stops saving, so two tabs never write over each other (Albert, Nov 11)"},
 "E996": {"text": "the Stores card (Have, In, Out, On it over the last minute) and the Score card (each side's parts), opened from the top bar's stores and score (Base's; Albert, Nov 11)"},
 "E997": {"text": "a book over each of your finished, idle buildings with research you can start now, looked for once a second (Base's mark; Albert, Nov 11)"},
 "E998": {"text": "shedding (fewer drops, then 30 fps, then a lower resolution) is timed on the drawing alone: logic time had pushed his phone to half resolution, a blurry picture that saves no logic (Albert's screenshots, Nov 11 10:07, 10:14: 29 fps, logic 7.2 ms, draw 3.3 ms)"},
 "E124": {"text": "light by the sun's height, the twilights at −6, −12, −18 (SoRen's ramp, QD)"},
 "E125": {"text": "QP the one first-order lag, x to its level L over τ: x(t) = L + (x0 − L) e^(−t/τ) (N16; Mid's relax: wetness here, and the market, nerve, healing, loyalty to come)"},
 "E126": {"text": "QH the rain: a two-state chain, drawn once a game hour (a day's 24th): P(wet | dry) and P(wet | wet) are D102; a wet spell draws its intensity and the wind's sign once, from the rules' dice (QCL), a storm from D103. Snow falls instead when the air is at or under 1 °C (QI)"},
 "E127": {"text": "the season's mean, eased into the next"},
 "E128": {"text": "what falls in a wet hour: snow at or under 1 °C, else rain; nothing in a dry hour; on each new hour the sky's word is told if it turned (turned, E554)"},
 "E129": {"text": "rain and snow come and go over tens of seconds (SoRen), toward the spell's intensity"},
 "E130": {"text": "QP settle: wet in D104, dry in D105; melting snow soaks the ground as rain does (Mid: what melts goes into the ground's water; nothing vanishes)"},
 "E131": {"text": "QO degree-day melt, rain on snow twice as fast"},
 "E132": {"text": "QQ: lake ice grows with the freezing degree-seconds (D350, by Stefan's law); ice on the ground grows the same way while the ground is wet, full at D225"},
 "E133": {"text": "fog by the atmosphere (QK, QCL): the air keeps its dew point (D229 fog); falling rain or snow saturates it; past the fog's water the rest settles as dew and lowers the dew point (Magnus inverted)"},
 "E135": {"text": "(Albert, Nov 10 16:58: never saw a bolt; a storm strikes all through, not only in its heaviest rain, which had halved the strikes of a storm already rare) QL, QM: strikes on Poisson waits in a storm"},
 "E136": {"text": "a strike: on the ground in view when close, a sheet flash when far; the flash never comes within D112 of the last (QL, WCAG 2.3.1), and the bolt is pinned to the ground it hits"},
 "E137": {"text": "a far flash: its thunder from beyond the screen"},
 "E138": {"text": "the rain's fall speed (QJ, Atlas's fit to Gunn & Kinzer); how many of the pool are falling: the strength"},
 "E139": {"text": "on the ground, under everything: snow whitens the land (screen), wet darkens it (multiply), ice whitens the inland water"},
 "E140": {"text": "over everything: what falls, the strikes, the flash, the night, the white of low visibility and the fog"},
 "E141": {"text": "SoRen's bolt: a channel from the top of the sky to the ground with a fork or two, three strokes from a soft glow to a bright core; its foot lights the ground round it"},
 "E142": {"text": "the channel wanders but leans home to its foot"},
 "E143": {"text": "the light: the sun's by the ramp, the horizon's warmth within 8° of it; rain no longer washes the whole picture grey nor darkens the wet ground (Mid tints only the sky band; Albert, Nov 7 20:11: gloomy, dismal), the weather's visibility (E381) remains; the night's wash is the eye's own darkness (D117's light on a log scale, QAL), one home with sight: moonlit snow is bright on the screen as it is to the eye"},
 "E144": {"text": "KW7: Koschmieder's reach (QK) limits sight on the Display floor; here the haze"},
 "E145": {"text": "Marsh (TW1): the wet ground E32 found, less what the fords and roads made water"},
 "E146": {"text": "Floor 7, display (layer 140): what each side sees, now and nothing else (Albert, Nov 6: no fog of war; the land is always drawn). Every tick of D117 each side's eyes, its units and finished buildings, look at every other side's unit and building: seen when within the eye's range (QAL) and the line clears (QAM); the computers by the same rule (QAN)"},
 "E147": {"text": "a thing's height: a building's from its look (D312), a person's from D117"},
 "E148": {"text": "each tile's top: the ground, a standing tree's height, a finished building's; worked out again when a thing is felled, lost or finished"},
 "E149": {"text": "the line of sight (QAM): from the eye's height to the target's top, tile by tile along the grid line (Bresenham), its own footprints aside; blocked where a tile's top stands above the line"},
 "E150": {"text": "QAT the shadow: length = height × cot(the sun's height), capped at D120 heights, thrown away from the sun; the sun rises on the right, stands over the bottom of the screen at noon (the camera looks north), sets on the left"},
 "E151": {"text": "left at sunrise, up at noon, right at sunset"},
 "E152": {"text": "under the buildings and units: a building's footprint thrown by its height, a unit's foot by its own; none under the trees (the woods are their own shade)"},
 "E153": {"text": "the box's shadow: its top thrown, joined to its foot along every edge, one fill so the overlaps stay one shade"},
 "E154": {"text": "The woods cache: the deep trees (eight tree neighbours) are painted once per chunk of the board and zoom step; the rest of the things are stamped each frame. Cutting a tree wakes its neighbours and repaints the chunk."},
 "E155": {"text": "chunks of CS × CS tiles"},
 "E156": {"text": "a tree cut: its chunk is stale, and its neighbours stand at an edge now"},
 "E157": {"text": "each chunk's box in the view frame, with room above for the trees' height"},
 "E158": {"text": "the woods' picture: every untouched tree in a chunk on or near the screen, back to front, drawn once into one sheet the size of the screen and its margin, as the land is (Albert, Nov 10 21:08-21:10: things that do not move are not redrawn)"},
 "E159": {"text": "the woods' sheet slides with the camera and is painted again only past its margin, on a zoom, when a tree is baked or woken (DEEPV), or when the season turns the leaves"},
 "E160": {"text": "a wounded one sways about its feet (QBS)"},
 "E162": {"text": "Touch: one finger pans, two pinch; a wheel zooms about the pointer; a held finger picks more, drags the crosshair or draws a box (F21)."},
 "E163": {"text": "the camera rule: the board never leaves the screen's middle; past its edge the camera may show what the bars cover there and a little more (D315 sea on the sides and below, sky above), so nothing of the board need stay under a bar; a board smaller than that sits centred"},
 "E164": {"text": "what is under the finger: the tile at the land's height and the nearest unit it may see (yours, or one in sight and not hidden), within the larger of D246 hit and hitZ a zoom (Mid's hitAt); the menu answers the tap"},
 "E165": {"text": "The seed of the day (QBF): the date as YYYYMMDD, the same map for everyone that day; a seed in the address overrides it."},
 "E166": {"text": "the door: what the modules may touch"},
 "E167": {"text": "the test hook"},
 "E168": {"text": "First Keep v100 · menu.js (floor 8): everything on the glass. Lives alone; it reads the world through one function, read(), and acts through one, act(verb, arg), backed by VERBS, where every verb carries its own whyNot. A dim button never runs: it says why."},
 "E169": {"text": "Its shape lives in the Screen book (books/screen.js): the mold, the Build tabs, the card's rows and the subject's ticks that pick them, the pages and which are Tall. Nothing of it is typed here."},
 "E170": {"text": "its numbers live in books/measure.js (D); nothing is typed here"},
 "E172": {"text": "the Screen book: the Build tabs are its; a building shows priced once econ prices it, else Later"},
 "E173": {"text": "the seat, and who it trains first: asked of the books, never named"},
 "E174": {"text": "the classes War's Train box offers (D133), each as the first kind of it open at this age (Mid's kindOf)"},
 "E175": {"text": "a page that keeps its own height (SC20)"},
 "E176": {"text": "the new game's choices: the first is the label's row in Albert's template; built ones set the game, the rest wait (dim, they say why)"},
 "E177": {"text": "which choices are floors yet"},
 "E178": {"text": "the base's columns, Albert's template: the five stores in the top bar's order, read from SN5's top (no copy), the one order the Stores table, the log and every price follow (N560)"},
 "E179": {"text": "the base's icons: one 24-unit box each, line icons in the cell's colour, finds in their own"},
 "E181": {"text": "the colours: the menus read every colour from the Colours book (C38 the menus' own, the rings, Gold (on) and gunmetal), set once on :root with the page behind the board; nothing below uses a colour that is not in the book (the map's and the brushes' own paint excepted, C header)"},
 "E182": {"text": "the glass's own state, nothing of the world's"},
 "E183": {"text": "60f 60w, as Albert's Build menu: each part's amount (through fmt: 1k at a thousand, 1.5k) and its store's first letter, in the top bar's order (ORDER), anything outside it last (N560)"},
 "E184": {"text": "read: the one window onto the world the glass draws from"},
 "E187": {"text": "a channel's volume, a step a tap (HX10)"},
 "E189": {"text": "a cell for what is drawn but not yet built: Albert's reminder"},
 "E190": {"text": "the new game: the bell (D134), fog, the day's map or a fresh one"},
 "E191": {"text": "tap a yield: new villagers go there (the ring)"},
 "E192": {"text": "tap picks, slide places the ghost, tap again builds. N61 (N384): a place holds the name, the count, then the price; the count reads n/max when the building has a max (a build-once too: 0/1, then 1/1, no more Built) and n when it has none; no price once the count is full (Albert's design pass, Nov 21, N560)"},
 "E193": {"text": "the cells: one mold; a verb's cell is dim when its whyNot says so, and a dim cell only says why"},
 "E194": {"text": "a cell's object arguments live here by key, since the DOM holds strings (the hold verbs are gone: one tap does everything, Albert, Nov 8)"},
 "E195": {"text": "the mold: a ribbon is an optional label and a strip of n equal cells; seg puts them in one frame with one lit. Every screen is a list of ribbons"},
 "E196": {"text": "the mold: every screen is rows on one six-column grid (the Formation). A row holds cells and parts; a part is an optional label and a strip of choices, seg puts them in one frame with one lit"},
 "E201": {"text": "war mode: Albert's War rows. Left the people's orders, the middle box (map, squads and their dials, orders, kinds), right the army's"},
 "E202": {"text": "the top bar: Albert's two ribbons. The stores, sound, play, mail; the age, the clock, people, idle, records, rank, army"},
 "E203": {"text": "Relations and Misfits: one row a people: who and where they stand, (a bribe for misfits), the three stances, ✓. Drawn now, built with diplomacy (Later)"},
 "E204": {"text": "the five stores, sound, play, mail (SN5)"},
 "E205": {"text": "a page or a card is a bottom sheet: it opens from the bottom edge over the base's rows and hides them while it is open, as tall as its own rows (Albert, Nov 9: no fixed height); the card waits behind a page"},
 "E206": {"text": "the ghost: press and slide on the map moves it; the tile under the finger is its middle. Build confirms. Nothing of this reaches the canvas's own pan while a ghost is up"},
 "E207": {"text": "the tap: the glass answers first. A ghost takes it; aiming takes it; a unit or a thing under it becomes the subject, and a picked villager or soldier is sent at it"},
 "E208": {"text": "one height for every page but the Tall ones: each is laid out once, the tallest sets the panel, the others fill it (Albert: menus never move)"},
 "E211": {"text": "the game opens on the player's hall"},
 "E212": {"text": "the version, said once (D171)"},
 "E213": {"text": "First Keep v100 · econ.js (floor 9): the economy. Lives alone; touches the world only through FK. Costs, homes, training, sites, ages, upkeep, and the villager as one state machine: idle, walk, gather, carry, build, repair, wait."},
 "E214": {"text": "seconds played, and when the bell rings"},
 "E215": {"text": "gone: marked when it leaves the map (below)"},
 "E216": {"text": "paying: a side pays all of a cost or none of it (SB Cost)"},
 "E217": {"text": "a site: a building paid for and placed at done 0; villagers raise it. canPlace mirrors build's rule without building"},
 "E218": {"text": "training, research and the age: one queue at the building, as long as the mold's six and what research adds (QCA); the head trains, is learned or rises, in its own time after research (D124, the step's own, or the age's, D129); a price is the book's after research (QCA), an age's D129; a new unit stands on a free tile beside and takes the side's rally job; a step or an age in the queue is no person"},
 "E219": {"text": "the age (Mid's ageUp): the next age, never the hidden sixth until the peace opens it; paid at its price (D129, the ages of D130) and queued at the seat, which trains nothing else while it rises; the side's aging is its time left"},
 "E220": {"text": "the jobs (SM Gather): a villager's job is the yield it works; counts are read, not kept"},
 "E221": {"text": "QV: the find of a yield whose rate of return R is best (the walk out, the walk home and the crowd counted), of those not full (D195), not left alone for no path (D137), in the box it was sent to cut, and within the look (D197) of the point given; the straight line under-counts the walk home, so finds are weighed by it first and walked (wayLen) best first until none can beat the best"},
 "E222": {"text": "a find no path reaches, or with no spot free on its ring, is left alone a while (D137), and the next beat chooses again: one walled in tries one find a beat and waits, never every find on the map at once; sent to a building she drops the standing spot she held (Nov 13, N343: the spot of her last find or of the Town Center kept pulling her off the building, so she walked back and forth and worked under half the time); a post she is set to counts as told (N437)"},
 "E223": {"text": "assign: + sends an idle or waiting villager (else the one earning least, QV, on another job, never one posted to a field) to the yield's best find; − sets one of the job's villagers idle"},
 "E224": {"text": "a stroke of work (gathering or raising) faces its work and sounds on every other beat; the tick: training and research, ages, upkeep, the villagers, the bell"},
 "E225": {"text": "a new game: the book's stores (D172); the bell stays as Start set it"},
 "E226": {"text": "the score (QBR): what a side holds, cost ÷ D135, everything it gathered ÷ D135, and what it paid for research and ages (the ledger's research, Mid's spent) ÷ D135"},
 "E227": {"text": "First Keep v100 · combat.js (floor 10): health, the blow (QBO, QBT), the foe (QAG, QAF), nerve and the rout (QAI, QAO, QBQ), a soldier's day (its yard, kiting, healing at a shelter), squads, shapes and tempers, towers' reach (QAJ), the missile, sparks and standards. Lives alone; touches the world only through FK. A soldier's jobs: idle (at home, guarding its yard), march (to a point, fighting what it meets), hold (standing at that point), fight, rout (broken and running, or called home)"},
 "E228": {"text": "tiles from a unit to a thing: to a building's footprint, in the grid's frame"},
 "E229": {"text": "gone: pulled down (econ marks it) or dead (die marks it)"},
 "E230": {"text": "the blow's strength (Mid's dmgOf): its blow after research, blades worn by frost, rain or snow (D234, its research a share), a mounted shape's edge, its temper, its side's hunger"},
 "E231": {"text": "a blow lands (QBO); it shakes the struck one's nerve by where it comes from (QAI), sends it off by the impact (QBT), throws sparks and, from a shooter, a missile; a kill steadies the striker"},
 "E232": {"text": "QAF and QAG the foe (Mid's unitPower, groupPower, canBeat, foeValue): one its group can beat first (Lanchester: its side near summed against the foe alone, with the counters both ways), then the most harm the foe does a second for the time to kill it and reach it; wildlife picks the most worth among what bites it"},
 "E233": {"text": "the best foe in reach (Mid's bestFoe), the nearest one (nearestFoe, round any point), the nearest foe building (nearestFoeBld; the widest one's reach, D11, added to the grid's search)"},
 "E234": {"text": "to within reach of a thing, with a short search (D147); a soldier on the target he was ordered at searches as far as it takes (findPath's far search, N447)"},
 "E235": {"text": "a wave falls back to its seat, else to any building of its side"},
 "E236": {"text": "a side's wave in the field: its soldiers at the start, so nerve can be read (QBQ)"},
 "E237": {"text": "to a tile, or near one that cannot be stood on (a building's); no way there, it strikes a foe building that blocks it"},
 "E238": {"text": "QAF a group's power: each one's health × its blow (Mid's dmgOf), the blow at least D194, over D193 per, a building-only kind at D193's bonly (Mid's unitPower and powerOf, one home)"},
 "E239": {"text": "a soldier's nerve (QAI): at rest it settles back (QP), faster by its own wall or tower; outnumbered it drains; at nothing it breaks and runs (QAO), the player told once in a while"},
 "E240": {"text": "the bars: a unit's or building's health, when it is hurt and in sight; the crosshair of the player's wave"},
 "E241": {"text": "First Keep v100 · ai.js (floor 11): one brain for every computer's side, three personalities (D303: Raiders, Rivals, Fortress), Mid's think. Lives alone; acts only through ECON and WAR, the same doors as the player; it sees the whole map, as Mid's computers did (Albert, Nov 5)."},
 "E242": {"text": "the seat, and the hands it trains"},
 "E243": {"text": "the shells a side can pay for that tick a capability"},
 "E244": {"text": "each yield's camp: the drop-off that takes it in"},
 "E245": {"text": "a spot: the nearest free footprint to a point, searched in rings, kept off the home's own ring so the roads stay open"},
 "E250": {"text": "First Keep v100 · sound.js (beside the stack): one player for every recipe in books/sound.js (H). Lives alone; hears the world only through FK's 'event' hook."},
 "E251": {"text": "The ear is the camera, at a height (QAX); a struck thing rings by its material (QAY); snow lowers the air's top and rain masks the quiet (QBX). No sound is typed here."},
 "E252": {"text": "each channel's volume steps, the one in use first (HX10)"},
 "E253": {"text": "a phone opens its audio only on a touch"},
 "E254": {"text": "the Ring/Silent switch silences the game; the player's music plays on (HX8)"},
 "E255": {"text": "a battle's many blows never clip a phone speaker"},
 "E256": {"text": "QAY: each mode dies with time constant tau ÷ Hz, to 80 dB down"},
 "E257": {"text": "QAX: the ear sits over the screen's middle at the height a lens of HX1's field of view needs to see the screen; a sound d along the ground is √(d² + h²) away,"},
 "E258": {"text": "full within the closest zoom's height, then falling as 1 ÷ distance (the inverse-square law in amplitude), less the air's loss"},
 "E259": {"text": "the camera's height in metres: half the view's width (the screen's width over the zoom, halved) over the tangent of half the ear's field of view (the Sound book's ear fov), units to metres by D85's upm"},
 "E260": {"text": "QBY: a sound with a reach is full within floor × reach"},
 "E261": {"text": "the air is full: an alert never waits"},
 "E262": {"text": "thunder comes after its flash by the distance ÷ the speed of sound"},
 "E263": {"text": "QBX: rain drowns the far and quiet first"},
 "E264": {"text": "the player's volume for this channel"},
 "E265": {"text": "ambience as events: a bird from a tree in view by day, a cricket in the dark, never in winter; when one sings is a Poisson process (HX4)"},
 "E266": {"text": "QBX: the air's top falls with snow cover, on a log scale"},
 "E2220": {"text": "one panner for a whole sound, not one for each of its parts (a knock is up to four): fewer nodes made a blow in a big fight, the same sound, since a panner is linear on one channel; a part with its own pan (the new age's chord) still gets its own"},
 "E267": {"text": "a side's economy, fresh: its age, the steps it knows, its gathered total, the rally, and the stores' flow (this minute's in and out, the last minute's, each by reason) and the ledger of the whole game"},
 "E268": {"text": "earn and spend: every store in or out goes through these two, the one home for the stores, the minute's flow (by resource and by reason) and the ledger of where it came from and went (its words in the Words book, J1); a gain from gathering counts toward the score's wealth"},
 "E269": {"text": "what was paid comes back the way it went out: the store, the minute's spending and the ledger step back, so a cancel is as if the order never was"},
 "E270": {"text": "the stores' flow a minute: the last full minute, or before there is one the minute so far scaled up (from at least D189 seconds); net is in less out; a store's velocity runs −1 to +1 by tanh, and falling with under two minutes left is the worst there is (D189)"},
 "E271": {"text": "each minute (D188) the minute's in and out become the last minute's"},
 "E272": {"text": "the words helpers: numbers shortened (1.2k, 12k), plurals, 'a, b or c', a percent slower, a place as its lettered square, a ledger line; their words in the Words book (J), their numbers in D191"},
 "E273": {"text": "the first ending in the Words book (J5) that fits the name"},
 "E274": {"text": "how much slower a full cover of mud or snow makes a march, in percent, from its terrain factor f: 1 − 1 ÷ (1 + f) (QN)"},
 "E275": {"text": "a place as the map's lettered squares, measured from the board's corner: D190 units a square, letters across, numbers down (A1 to V22); off the board, the nearest square"},
 "E276": {"text": "a ledger line: its reasons largest first, each in its word and shortened, apart by a dot; under half a unit is left out"},
 "E277": {"text": "QCA, the effects: what each side has learned, and each side's numbers worked out once until its learning changes; a new game forgets both"},
 "E278": {"text": "a thing's keys, the names an effect may reach it by: every head of its code's letters (B, BR for BR1), its code, its ticks and a soldier's class"},
 "E279": {"text": "a number's base, from its one home: the pace (D86), a building's health (D139) or a unit's (D138), a find's or a field's rate, a price (D123, or the step's own), a step's time (its own), a unit's training (D124), a site's raising (D125), a queue's length (the mold's six, SN1), a load (D87), a home's room (D127), mud's and snow's cost (D106, how deep it sinks), studs (none), a soldier's share of a blow before armour (D228); any other key is the unit's D138 entry"},
 "E280": {"text": "the one window for a kind's number after research (QCA): flat adds first, then the boosts summed and applied once to that, then each cut on what is left (Albert, Nov 5 18:07), then the lowest kept; a price rounds each yield to the whole unit"},
 "E281": {"text": "learning a step puts its effects in force for that side; every unit and building of the side keeps its share of health as the most it can have moves"},
 "E282": {"text": "who counters whom (Mid's vsMul): the most of the striker's counters (D138 vs, its ranks' added) over the struck one's kind, class and tags; the one home the blow (QBO), the foe (QAG) and the odds (QAF) read"},
 "E283": {"text": "QAF the odds an army gives itself against a side, the one home the computers read, counting only the foe's soldiers and towers its side has seen (E624; Albert, Nov 8: the all-seeing was a crutch of the live test): the counters summed both ways over the first of each army, their ratio held in D193 (Mid's matchup) bending my power"},
 "E284": {"text": "against theirs: its soldiers, its towers (not its seat) at D177 each, its people at D192 (Mid's powerFrom); the square law as odds, p² ÷ (p² + q²), which is r² ÷ (1 + r²) with r = p ÷ q"},
 "E285": {"text": "the Sides book (I) and the stances made in play, each pair's own; a new game forgets them"},
 "E286": {"text": "who belongs (the kind decides): a side's own are no group; an animal (I4) is a beast; a kind of the wild in a group's list (I3) is that group's; the rest of the wild is the Natives' (Mid's gangOf)"},
 "E287": {"text": "a stance is the pair's own, or the book's start (I2); a treaty sets it both ways between its signers only, never for a third (pacta tertiis, N159)"},
 "E288": {"text": "the one hostility test (Mid's isFoe): never one's own; an animal is everyone's foe; one of a wild group is a foe when the side is at war with that group; between sides, war"},
 "E289": {"text": "the wild looking at a side: an animal fights everyone; a group fights a side at war with it, but starts nothing with a computer (decision 4b: a camp fights a computer only once struck on its ground, which comes with the camps)"},
 "E2200": {"text": "war and friendship are the Sides book's own words (I1), read once, never written in the code"},
 "E2201": {"text": "the Relations card's wild rows are the Sides book's group names (I5), in its order; whoOf reads each back to its group by that name"},
 "E2202": {"text": "each kind's wild group, read from the Sides book (I3) once at load instead of searched at every look of the hostility test; a kind in two lists keeps the first, as before"},
 "E290": {"text": "the Research book (O) by code and by key"},
 "E291": {"text": "a find's or a field's rate after the side's research (QCA): the one window, D88 or the row's own rate as the base"},
 "E292": {"text": "Mid's research lines: a line is the steps of one line at one building, in the book's order; a step waits on the one before it and on its needs (by key; a need not yet in the book is never met); the next is the first unknown step of the line"},
 "E293": {"text": "research (Mid's researchWhy and research): a step is refused when known, before its age, before its needs, already queued, with no finished building of its row, the shortest queue there full, or not paid for (the reason as a word for the menu); else paid and queued at that building; learned when it leaves the queue, its effects applied once (FK.learn)"},
 "E294": {"text": "research shows on its building (Mid's UP, PB12): the steps learned of those its row names, none, some, or half or more; a building's level (PB3, PB4, PB6): the side's age against the look's, or how many steps that raise it the side knows; the footing drawn under the walls"},
 "E2401": {"text": "a building's level is drawn every frame: the two counts that read the side's learned steps (how many of its row's steps are learned; for a tower, how many steps of its tier) are kept per side and building (E2400), not counted again each frame, and the tower count no longer copies the side's whole learned set each time; same numbers"},
 "E295": {"text": "the keep at its level: the bastion from its points in the Sprites book (PB13)"},
 "E296": {"text": "the walked length (QBL) from a tile to beside a building: a straight step one tile, a diagonal √2; no way, infinitely far"},
 "E297": {"text": "QCI standing spots: everyone stands on a spot of its own a pace (D196) apart. A point's spots lie on the hex lattice, nearest first, rings enough for D128 people and D196's spare"},
 "E298": {"text": "a find's working ring (Mid's WORK_R, D196): as many spots as fit a pace apart round it, ⌊2π·r ÷ pace⌋ (Mid's findCap), laid on a ring wide enough that the chord between two is a pace, and clear of the ground the find keeps (D169)"},
 "E299": {"text": "spot i of c: round a find on its ring; round a building on its outline, the lane of tiles beside it, k a side, at least a pace apart, corners too, clockwise from the top-left (Mid's spotAt, in tile coordinates); round a point on the lattice; null past the last"},
 "E300": {"text": "a spot is free when its tile is walked and nobody stands on it or has claimed one within a full pace, 3 ft (D196, OSHA 1910.142(b)(3), N166); at less, neighbours overlapped, the push moved them and the walk back returned them: the twitch (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #16, found against the rule)"},
 "E301": {"text": "the spot u keeps at c, else the free one nearest u (round a point, the nearest the point)"},
 "E302": {"text": "walk to a spot of its own at c: the path's last tile becomes the spot itself; false when none is free or none is reached"},
 "E303": {"text": "a path's last point is reached within near-enough (D196), any point within a pace when the crowd has pushed it this step: a walker held off its way by people takes the next point"},
 "E304": {"text": "QCJ separation, neighbours only (the M3 grid): two closer than a pace part to a pace, each moved by the other's share of their mass (the Mass book, QBT's bodies), the lighter further; two on one point part along a direction fixed by their places in the roll; nobody is pushed into a tree, a wall or water"},
 "E305": {"text": "a find drawn smaller as it is used: PN1's left share and the rest by what is left (Mid's nodeScale)"},
 "E306": {"text": "the forager (QV, QX): a find takes D195's cap (a tree one feller, a field one worker) or as many as its ring has spots; the others on it crowd its rate by D195's hold; span: how far a find or a building reaches, so the straight line less both spans never over-counts the walk"},
 "E307": {"text": "QV R = c / (c/g + 2d/v + w·c/(A·v)): c the load, g the rate crowded (QX), v the walk, d the walked length to the drop-off (cached per find), w the straight walk out, A what is left up to a field's life (a tree begun counts as worth finishing); low: d by the straight line, a bound. A find with no free spot pays nothing"},
 "E308": {"text": "a lost find (Mid's decision 1): it delivers what it carries, then looks from where the find ran out within the look (D197), widening over tau; nothing found, it waits on a spot at its drop-off and looks again every few seconds, with no end; a box that is done sends it back to its work"},
 "E309": {"text": "builders who finish a place of work take it up (Mid's startWork): a field if nobody works it; a camp (a drop-off that takes fewer than every yield) sends them to the best find it takes"},
 "E310": {"text": "a box over finds (Mid's boxCut): n villagers, idle first then the nearest, cut the finds in it, from the nearest open one outside when none inside is open, then go back to the work they left; Send out: the last villager on a field goes idle; posted: on a field; idlePost: a finished field nobody works"},
 "E311": {"text": "a trained unit steps out onto the free spot of its building's outline nearest the middle of its south side, the side that faces the player (Albert, Nov 14, N369: \"make them spawn facing me. So south\"; was the first free spot, the north side, behind the building); none free, the queue waits; with your rally flag up, a soldier marches to it (Mid's rally0, F21)"},
 "E312": {"text": "nudged off its spot, it gives way while pushed and steps back once the crowd lets go: no tug of war with a walker, no shuffle between two on their spots (a push moves each less than near-enough)"},
 "E313": {"text": "how many of a building a side may have now: its age's limit with research added (D199), none before its age (D200); why not, in Mid's words (capWhy)"},
 "E314": {"text": "why a building may not stand here, Mid's rules in order: the edge, the limit, the ground under it (a gate may take its owner's wall piece), the gap from every building (gapOf: two squares, a house one from another house, none between two fields of the touch list; walls and gates may touch; Albert, Nov 19 21:29, N421: the space is back; Nov 21, N438: houses closer, fields side by side), and never touching one that trains (canPlace); capped: the limit already checked; apart: the computers' own looser rule, their fields may touch anything (ai.js spot: their towns are laid as before N52; still to be put to Albert, N438)"},
 "E315": {"text": "two squares from every find too, measured from the footprint's edge to the find's middle (Mid's nodesNear)"},
 "E316": {"text": "the ghost snaps to the nearest spot that fits beside one of yours (its own gap from that one, N438, or a lane apart; edges or middles in line; N421) or in line with one farther off; else it stays where the finger is (Mid's snapGhost)"},
 "E317": {"text": "taking a building down pays back half its price, all of it early in the build; its line is paid back in full first (Mid's shellBack, refundOf, demolish)"},
 "E318": {"text": "a wall dragged from corner to corner: a straight run of tiles, four-connected so nothing slips through a diagonal (Mid's wallLine); laid piece by piece while the stores last, each sent a builder; the seal is a foe's walk out from the Town Center over the tiles not yet built too (Mid's sealPath, by v100's A*)"},
 "E319": {"text": "the walk starts on the Town Center's own floor; walls being laid count as built; everything is put back after"},
 "E320": {"text": "a builder remembers the work it left (its find and yield, and whether it was pulled off it) so it can go back (Mid's sendBuilder); one already beside the site stops the walk it was on, so its arrival cannot turn it back to that walk's work"},
 "E321": {"text": "a new site gets the nearest free villager; with none free, your nearest worker is pulled off and goes back after, a computer's lowest earner keeps building (Mid's autoBuilder and pickVil); a line of wall gets two at most, who work down it"},
 "E322": {"text": "back to the very find it left if it still stands, else the best of its yield, else idle (Mid's backToWork)"},
 "E323": {"text": "the next site for a builder done: a wall piece close by, else a site nobody raises (Mid's repairTick)"},
 "E324": {"text": "a builder done (Decisions Nov 11, #16): his queued sites first; then, if he raised this building, its own work (a camp's finds, a field's post); then the next unbuilt site near; then the last resource building he raised in this run (house, mill, gold, house: back to the gold); then the job he was pulled from; else idle and counted"},
 "E325": {"text": "mending, Mid's: three times the build time for a whole building, a quarter of its price paid as it goes; short of any part, it stops (QCK)"},
 "E326": {"text": "a crew of n raises a site at n^0.7 (QAC), counted once a tick; frost slows stone work; the site's health rises with it"},
 "E327": {"text": "of the buildings that can take an order, the one with the shortest line (Mid's shortest)"},
 "E328": {"text": "a gate is walkable only to those its owner does not count a foe: asked of combat.js by the shut hook, for the walker on the path in hand; none in hand, it is shut"},
 "E329": {"text": "a gate is shut to a foe of its owner, and to an unknown walker (the seal's foe)"},
 "E330": {"text": "the computer's wall ring: from its age, with stone, a few pieces a round, gates first, while it keeps its stone (Mid's decide)"},
 "E331": {"text": "an arc of wall round the Town Center facing the middle, four-connected; its two squares nearest the middle are the gate (Mid's wallPlan)"},
 "E332": {"text": "who trains a kind: the building with the shortest line; walls are laid as lines; walls and gates show the seal"},
 "E333": {"text": "the ghost to the finger, lifted above it on a phone, snapped beside yours; the reason it may not stand is kept for the label"},
 "E334": {"text": "a wall's next corner snaps flat or upright when nearly so; its tiles from its corners (Mid's wallSnap, wallSet)"},
 "E335": {"text": "a finger on a wall's corner moves it, on its line slides the whole wall; elsewhere it looks around and a tap adds a corner (Mid's wallHit, wallDrag)"},
 "E336": {"text": "Build: a wall line laid while the stores last, said in one toast; a building sent its nearest free villager (or the one picked), then, for a building that ticks Repeat, the ghost waits on the next spot beside it until the limit or the purse says no (Mid's commitPlace; N17 #17)"},
 "E337": {"text": "while placing, the finger moves the ghost (a wall's corner or line), not the map; the drag holds only its own finger: a second finger, and the first one's lift, stay the map's, so the map never keeps a finger that has left"},
 "E338": {"text": "the ghost's own art tinted green where it fits and red where not, one tinted copy a sprite and colour (Mid's ghostTint)"},
 "E339": {"text": "while a wall or gate is placed: a red line where a foe could walk in, or Sealed over the Town Center (Mid's drawSeal)"},
 "E340": {"text": "the ghost: a wall's tiles green or red with its corners, the first ringed green; a building's guides to yours in line and its tinted art, no footprint box (Mid's drawGhost, drawGuides)"},
 "E341": {"text": "a tap on open ground while the Build page is open marks what fits there (Base: the suggestion is shown in blue with Fits here, never picked for the player; Mid picked it and dropped its ghost)"},
 "E342": {"text": "dragging the ghost near the screen's edge scrolls the map (Mid's edgeScroll)"},
 "E343": {"text": "what fits a spot: a drop-off for finds far from theirs, more of what stands round you, a wall in a narrow way (a gate beside your wall), a home when room is short; the best score wins (Mid's suggestAt)"},
 "E344": {"text": "fish round every lake: a spot every D218 per of its radius, walked out from the middle to the shore and set inset back into the water, each holding its share of the lake (Mid's layFish)"},
 "E345": {"text": "a find laid where something falls (game becomes a carcass where it stood); a lake near enough to stand a dock by, past its beach"},
 "E346": {"text": "a boar near every Town Center, at the book's spot in each corner (Mid's boar)"},
 "E347": {"text": "the gather beat: the field is worked now (its soil wears); a flock's food goes straight to the store; a plot with an amount runs down and its worker waits by it when it is cut out (Mid's replant wait); a famine weakens the work (hungerOf)"},
 "E348": {"text": "what a unit eats a second: its kind's shares (its Upkeep, with research) of a person's day; a famine past its grace weakens work and blows (Mid's shareOf, hungerOf); fish are worked only near a finished dock of the side (Mid's dockNear); food in reach is any find, field of one's own or game (Mid's foodInReach)"},
 "E349": {"text": "everyone eats, every moment: a villager working food eats from its find, not the store (a field and game for nothing, a shepherd from the store); the store empty is hunger, and with no food in reach a famine, timed from its start (Mid's upkeepTick, starveTick)"},
 "E351": {"text": "the year's work: everyone eats; a field's soil wears while worked and rests back, never under its floor (QAA, Mid's natureTick); each season's turn once"},
 "E352": {"text": "each season's turn: food in store spoils (QAD); in spring fish regrow (QY), lambs come (QY) and a tended flock is culled to half for mutton (QZ); wolves near a pasture take sheep every season; the harvest of the year is rolled in spring (Mid's seasonTurn)"},
 "E353": {"text": "a cut-out plot is replanted at D222's share of its price and is full again; from a drop-off, every cut-out plot of what it takes, nearest first, as many as can be paid for (Mid's replantWhy, replant, cutOut, replantAll)"},
 "E354": {"text": "send a hunter: the given villager, or the nearest idle one, else the nearest from other work (not a builder or a posted worker); it fights the game (Mid's sendHunt)"},
 "E355": {"text": "QBO the blow on a unit: × the counter; a villager's javelin on game × D221; on a soldier, an animal's at D231 wild, a runner's × routHit, × its armour share (D228), its shape's hit and against riders, from behind a blade × D141; roofed against missiles; on a building × the striker's bld (Mid's hurt); a stranger's blow is × (1 − D355 fight × (1 − its familiarity)) (Albert, Nov 8: the outsider pays)"},
 "E356": {"text": "a building that falls pays its destroyer D233 of its price (Mid's plunderBld); game falls as a carcass of its meat where it stood, and its hunters butcher it (Mid's kill); a death with no killer names its cause for the copy log (why: removed by you, drowned, sickness and the rest; N440), and a soldier under an order counts as dead on it"},
 "E357": {"text": "hunt a beast from its card; replant a cut-out plot, or every one a drop-off takes, from theirs"},
 "E359": {"text": "the town is told what food, the seasons and the flock do, in the Words book's news"},
 "E360": {"text": "the ground under a walker as it steps toward the tile to (QN, QR): its mud (the marsh always), its snow cover, its ice (D225), the friction its step needs by what steps (G9), what the ground offers off the ice (dry to mud to snow) and on it (G8 by the air, melting to hard; the studs' G10 if iron bites), the grade up to it, and which way it walks against the wind"},
 "E361": {"text": "QCB the pace: Pandolf's cost of walking solved for the speed, its power set by the walker's base (D86 with research, QCA) unloaded on flat firm ground in still air; the load, the ground's η, the grade and the wind change it; × each state (D224) and, after a slip, the shortened step on its share of ice (QR)"},
 "E362": {"text": "QR each second on ice: the step lands on the ice with the chance of its cover, else on the ground; it slips exactly when the friction it needs is more than that ground offers, and walks on wary (a shorter step) until it is off the ice"},
 "E363": {"text": "a slipped walker stands G10's seconds; which way it walks, for the wind"},
 "E364": {"text": "above freezing lake ice's degree-seconds fall four times as fast; ground ice thaws by the degree (D225) and its degree-seconds are set to match what is left; the freezing front and the walking front in depth steps (D350), from the freezing degrees"},
 "E365": {"text": "the share of the ground under ice: √ of its freezing degree-seconds over D225's full (QQ, Stefan)"},
 "E366": {"text": "the armour kit a side has learned (Mid's KIT): 0 to 3 steps of the Sprites book's kit, each turning a person's slots (mail and a steel helm, then plate, the great helm, its crest and a cape in the figure's own colours), with a shoulder guard of leather, mail or steel"},
 "E367": {"text": "one drawing list for every figure that is not a person or a beast (the engines, the chariot, the elephant, the riders, the elite pennant): each part a brush (P, E, L, Q, rect, wheel, planks, helm, horse, person), in a frame moved and turned (at), or drawn only in the blow's frame (atk) or out of it (rest); a value may sway with the stride or change in the blow's frame. The numbers live in the Sprites book"},
 "E368": {"text": "a look by its rank: level 0 the look itself, level n the nth of its rank list, past the list its last (Mid's LOOKS by tier)"},
 "E369": {"text": "the Unit shell's classes: a class's kinds in book order; what a building trains (D133: a shell, or a class's kinds); a kind is open from its age (D130); a side's civilisation trains its own kind in place of the common one it replaces (Mid's civKind), and no other side trains it"},
 "E2403": {"text": "the shells never change in a match, so a class's kinds (KINDS, in book order) and the kind each civilisation puts in place of each shell (CIVK, the first in book order) are listed once, at load: kinds() and civKind() looked through every shell on each call, and trains() calls them for the labels and the computer players; callers only read the lists, never change them; same answers"},
 "E370": {"text": "a kind's ranks (Mid's tiers): the steps whose rank names it, learned, in book order, give its level and its name; the kit is how many armour steps a soldier's side has learned"},
 "E2402": {"text": "every unit's picture asks its rank and kit every frame: both counts are kept per side and kind (E2400), not filtered again each time (two lists and an empty set for a side with no research, per unit per frame); same numbers"},
 "E371": {"text": "the army's ceiling: soldiers (a kind with a class), queued ones counted, against D226 (Mid's ARMYMAX; a fallen side's share, capA, joins it with M30)"},
 "E372": {"text": "the army: a side's soldiers, the kinds with a class (Mid's armyOf); BUSY names who keeps to its own work and armyFree leaves them out (the routed now; the spy, the shrine, the escort and the school with their modules)"},
 "E373": {"text": "why a kind waits: the age it opens in (Mid's trainWhy)"},
 "E374": {"text": "the load, the ground's η (QN, research cuts), and the wind's drag ½ρCdA v|v| (W1, by the mass to the ⅔, D224), v the walk against the wind (Pugh)"},
 "E375": {"text": "aV² + bV + c = 0: a the walking term, b the grade and the wind as a grade (100F ÷ g), c the standing and load terms less the walker's power; the positive root"},
 "E376": {"text": "QCL the weather of the moment: rates, wind and visibility from the strengths, fog's water in calm air the vapour above saturation (CALVIS: Kunkel's fog term beside rain and snow); fog's share of a km's contrast for its looks; the wind signed and gusting; a blizzard's hours counted while its three conditions hold, and the flag at the NWS's three hours"},
 "E377": {"text": "the weather's book (D229), a game hour, the gusts (a fractal of the day's dice, set at the start) and the particle pool (the looks' dice)"},
 "E378": {"text": "QCL rain and snow rates, the wind, its gusts and the visibility (QK: Koschmieder over rain's and snow's extinction); a blizzard by the NWS: snow, wind or gusts at 35 mph or more, visibility under a quarter mile"},
 "E379": {"text": "rain: Marshall–Palmer sizes at the rate (λ = N0 R^exp), each drop falling at its size's speed in metres a second on the screen, carried and slanted by the wind"},
 "E380": {"text": "snow: flakes falling slow to fast by size, carried by the wind and swaying"},
 "E381": {"text": "the white of low visibility: the contrast lost over the screen's width, 1 − e^(−3.912 d ÷ V) (QK)"},
 "E382": {"text": "a side knows a step of research by its key"},
 "E383": {"text": "the player's three squads (Mid's battalions): each one's plan by class, its shape, temper and intent (the dials), and the one picked for orders (none: the whole army); the computers keep Guard and the line"},
 "E384": {"text": "who is in which squad (Mid's rebattalion): each keeps its squad while its class has room in the plan, the rest fill the first squad with room; none before Battalions"},
 "E385": {"text": "a squad's plan by class (Mid's sqPlan): a step of one under ten, five above, the whole squad at most D227"},
 "E386": {"text": "what a squad lacks, by kind to train (Mid's musterGap): its plan less its soldiers and those mustering for it, each class as its first kind of the age"},
 "E387": {"text": "where a blow comes from (Mid's fromWhere): the cosine between the line's facing (its own and its comrades' near, D232) and the striker; the front whenever it can turn to meet it or a comrade covers that side"},
 "E388": {"text": "QAI a loss drains each armed soldier of its side within D231's crowd by 1 ÷ (D142 × n), n those near and the one lost; one winning his fight on a building is not drained (E1280) (Mid's died, Dupuy's break)"},
 "E389": {"text": "Lanchester's odds above a half is exactly the ratio above one"},
 "E390": {"text": "a soldier at home keeps to its yard: within D235 of its post or of its Town Center (Mid's nearHome)"},
 "E391": {"text": "a foe building in the way is struck (Mid's findBlocker)"},
 "E392": {"text": "a group dressed into its shape at a tile (Mid's formUp): facing from home to there, the squads in order, blades before shooters; a column three files, a square √n, a front one rank, a choke three, a line about twice as wide as deep, a wedge point first, support a ring of blades round the shooters; each walks to its own place, at the pace of the slowest that is not an engine; a drill (the War Director's) keeps the shape for its time"},
 "E393": {"text": "time to contact: a soldier in a drill fights where it stands when the nearest foe would reach it before it reaches its place (D242; Mid's drillOn, drillHold)"},
 "E394": {"text": "idle soldiers form up at the building that trained them, one block per squad, else one block per kind of soldier (Albert, Nov 10, #32: by type); at home an army stands in the yard of the building that trained it (or its Town Center), to its south, facing south (D241 face; Albert, Nov 14, N369; was toward the map's middle), a block a squad side by side, blades in front, shooters behind (Mid's formUp, homeSpot)"},
 "E395": {"text": "a broken soldier runs D231's run a step from the nearest foe (or toward home) at its own pace, for the run's seconds (research shortens it), then comes back at D231's after (Mid's routSecs)"},
 "E396": {"text": "a soldier's day (Mid's solTick): nerve, healing by a shelter (QP), its drill; it keeps its foe while in reach of its sight × D238 leash × its temper's chase; it looks for the best foe and keeps the one it has unless the new is D132 better or the old is at its blade; at home only near its yard; No pursuit and Buildings first; Hold fights only what comes within reach; a march arrived holds; at home it walks back to its post"},
 "E397": {"text": "QAJ the missile: projectile motion with quadratic drag (the arrow's, W10), loosed at A5's rise, stepped until it lands; its speed for a distance found by halving; a missile is its shooter's shot (the shell's look of what it looses: no shot, no missile), burning when its shooter's side has the stat fire, and it flies from where it was loosed, not from where its shooter stands now (N388); a tower reaches as far as the arrow that lands at its bow's ground reach would land from its height, plus its research"},
 "E398": {"text": "in reach: it faces its foe; a shooter reloading with a blade near steps back (Mid's KITE), then strikes when ready"},
 "E399": {"text": "the missiles in flight (N388): each is its look's picture from the Sprites book, drawn once a size and kept, at true size (zoom x D12 x the look's metres a unit) and turned along the last of its path; a look with a trail leaves it behind in dots, D245's share of the flight long; a look with no brush (the gun's ball) is its trail alone"},
 "E400": {"text": "a blow's sparks (Mid's sparkDraw)"},
 "E401": {"text": "the standards (Mid's drawStandards): a group of D sprites' least on the move carries its side's flag, a ring at its foot as full as its health"},
 "E402": {"text": "Muster (Mid's musterN, musterCost, musterWhy, muster): a squad's lack in one order at the War Council: D244's times the price, the slowest kind's time shared by the buildings that train it × D244's time; refused without the step, with nothing lacking, without a council, a kind's building, room in the army or the town, or the price (a reason as a word for the menu); it comes out together into its squad"},
 "E404": {"text": "the squads' words and the step each dial waits for (Engagement, Formations, Battalions)"},
 "E406": {"text": "the orders, missions and the War Director's measures and words; the groups on the march (ORD), the missions by squad or the whole army (MS), and the moves' waits (AT)"},
 "E407": {"text": "the archers' arc (Mid's dress 'arc'): each on a circle of the arc's radius round the foe, a rank's gap apart along it, facing in"},
 "E408": {"text": "a charge spent: the pace drops to D249 slow and settles back to the walker's own (QP, N16); while it lasts the pace is D249 spd times the charge's research"},
 "E409": {"text": "the orders' shared measures: a point of a tile, the tile of a point, the length between, a group's centre, a tile's straight steps"},
 "E410": {"text": "the walk over the straight line (Mid's routeK): the way by A* (QBL), its steps summed, held within D247 least and route"},
 "E411": {"text": "a group's order you can follow (Mid's march): its tile, label, start and walk ratio; each soldier carries it, and the player hears where they march"},
 "E412": {"text": "each soldier's one word (Mid's armyStatus): rout, fight, rally (sent home, walking to the flag, or away from its place), march, or hold once still for D247 still"},
 "E413": {"text": "the obvious order for what is picked (Mid's order, Albert Nov 2): a foe is fought, a beast hunted, a site raised or mended, a field or camp worked, a find gathered, the ground walked, each villager to its own spot; a side not at war is refused"},
 "E414": {"text": "missions: a mission's soldiers, the hostile soldiers a group sees near it, and the chance (QAF) of the group against them with the counters both ways"},
 "E415": {"text": "each beat: every order's centre, count, fight and time left, arrived once all have stopped (Mid's ordersTick); every mission goes, acts or is done, its chance eased, lost or losing said once (Mid's missionsTick)"},
 "E416": {"text": "Go (Mid's hudFire, hudGo): a squad's idle soldiers, else the army's, march on the crosshair as one order and one mission; every ready squad goes, else the army"},
 "E417": {"text": "who can still reach a fight in time, fastest first, until the fight is even (Mid's reinforcePlan); grouped into waves by arrival"},
 "E418": {"text": "the War Director: the soldiers of a kind that can go, the crosshair's tile, a move's wait in seconds; the charge's reason, the charge, fall back in order"},
 "E419": {"text": "the Director's three moves (Mid's DIRECTS): each returns what it says, a reason without its bang when nobody moved"},
 "E420": {"text": "a kind's move, one tap (Mid's direct): it says its word, tires the soldiers and sounds its event"},
 "E421": {"text": "the narrow at a tile: the open ground across the facing, a tile at a time each way until a wall, a tree or water; narrower than the widest choke it is a choke, held in as many files as it is wide (D.choke; Mid's chokeAt without the drag)"},
 "E422": {"text": "the nearest cover (Mid's coverNear): an open tile with forest within D252 cover, within D252 find of the crosshair"},
 "E423": {"text": "an ambush in place (Mid's ambushTick): once there it goes to ground (no foe sees it); a foe within reach or a blow springs them all with a charge"},
 "E424": {"text": "your groups on the march (Mid's drawOrders): a dashed line to where they go, a ring there, the time left; the rally flag (flagAt); leaves over a hidden soldier (leavesOver)"},
 "E425": {"text": "the finger's gesture: where it went down and is, when, and what a module made of it (a line, the crosshair, a box); a hold after D246 hold"},
 "E426": {"text": "the hold's ring once the finger plainly holds, and the box being drawn (Mid's drawTouch)"},
 "E429": {"text": "Albert's one rule for the finger (Build 40, Nov 2): a tap picks yours, a second tap opens the card; with yours picked a tap is the obvious order; on open ground with nothing picked, the sword and close (Nov 3); a group's ring picks the group; a cut-out plot replants"},
 "E430": {"text": "the crosshair (Mid's aimSpot, aimColor): a foe, a find or the ground under the tap; green yours, red a foe or a hostile near, blue an ally, white nature"},
 "E431": {"text": "the finger's holds and drags on the map: the crosshair dragged, yours picked to keep picking, a box picks yours in it"},
 "E432": {"text": "the crosshair (Mid's drawReticle): brackets, a sonar ring, turning chevrons, a scan line, the cross, the time and the square. (Nov 12, N29, list E1 and E2) With an action chosen and no spot tapped yet, no crosshair is drawn: before, it sat at its old place and looked like a set target while Execute was still dim. Its words (time and square) ride above it on the map's dark pill, so they read over troops and roofs"},
 "E433": {"text": "a tile on the board (the floor gives -1 off it)"},
 "E434": {"text": "the narrowest gap on the road to a foe (Mid's gapOnRoad): from D251 ai.from tiles out to half way, each ai.step tiles, the open width across the road, the narrowest of ai.min to ai.max"},
 "E435": {"text": "the computer holds a gap (Mid's chokeClaim): once each D251 ai.every, with enough idle foot, files deep across the narrowest gap on the road to its nearest foe, for ai.hold"},
 "E436": {"text": "the Alarm and the end (F23, Mid's 09-nav, 12-sim-core, 13-sim-civil, 16-sim-fight, 40-emergency): the danger map's and the alarm's measures (D253 to D255), the words (J12, J13), the sides fallen, the bell's warnings said, the best score's key"},
 "E437": {"text": "a threat (Mid's isThreat): alive, not inside, one that fights and is neither a villager, game hunted for meat, nor a soldier that strikes only buildings; the side's foe by the one hostility test"},
 "E438": {"text": "the danger map (Mid's dangerMap, stampDanger): each side's, drawn afresh each beat on the walking grid: foe level round every threat to it and inside every enemy tower's reach plus D253 reach; scare level round the frights remembered (they lapse)"},
 "E439": {"text": "why a spot is dangerous, nearest cause first (Mid's dangerWhy): a threat near (its side named), an enemy tower's reach, else a fright remembered there"},
 "E440": {"text": "a worker leaves a find that turns unsafe (Mid's vilTick): it drops the find and looks again, off the danger; your town is told why, once a look; a villager told to that find stays on it, since you chose it (N437)"},
 "E441": {"text": "going inside (Mid's vilTick, stepOut): a unit sent to a building with room walks to it and goes in, hidden and out of reach, at its middle; a building gone or not standing sends it back to idle; going in, a villager at her post or on a find she was told to keeps it in mind (stay) and goes back to it when she comes out (N437)"},
 "E442": {"text": "a villager's fright (Mid's vilTick, D254): soldiers near scare it, beasts or robbers when a pack comes or one hurt it; it runs into the nearest building with room if nearer than the Town Center, else the Town Center, and its side remembers the place when it was far from home; inside, it comes out when no threat is near the building, unless the Alarm holds it; a villager at a post (a farm, pasture, tree farm, quarry, mint, foundry and the like) is never scared off it: she stays and works, and only the Alarm or Garrison takes her in (N437)"},
 "E443": {"text": "the Alarm's ranking (Mid's shelterRank, roomIn, fillRank, threatDir): buildings with room, sturdiest first, then roomiest, each filled to its room with the nearest; the danger lies toward the foe coming, the nearest threat within D255 dir, else the middle"},
 "E444": {"text": "the Alarm (Mid's emgStart, townSquare, soldiersIn, villagersIn): its first order notes each villager's work for Work; Gather sets everyone round the Town Center, soldiers outside; Garrison fills the buildings with soldiers, shooters first, the rest a line toward the danger; Garrison and Shelter send each villager into the nearest building with room (E1501), the rest stand beside the Town Center under its arrows (E1502). Work (Mid's emgStop): every villager back to what it did; soldiers stay till sent"},
 "E445": {"text": "the warnings (Mid's incomingTick, watchHome, drawRadar): the nearest foe's soldier you see near your Town Center or marching on your buildings, its group counted and its time to arrive, for the marker; a soldier at the town warns, once each D255 again"},
 "E446": {"text": "a site nobody builds (F23, Albert's play test): one no villager of its side can reach says why once; else the nearest free villager who can reach it is sent; walls keep their crew (D203)"},
 "E447": {"text": "a side falls (Mid's fall): its killer takes its stores and D233 of what its buildings cost; its people and buildings go; its army room \u00d7 D258 share is split among those left"},
 "E448": {"text": "who wins (Mid's judge): your fall loses; every rival fallen wins; a Wonder standing D257 s wins for its side, the first finished first; a timed game warns at D259 and the top score wins at the bell"},
 "E449": {"text": "the end (Mid's finish): won or lost, the text and the score (Mid's level played comes with the hazards setting), the best won score kept on this device"},
 "E452": {"text": "the danger map's home on the walking grid (econ draws it) and each side's reach, cached by what changes the walkable tiles: WALKV counts every change to them (a find laid or spent, a building raised or taken down, a save opened)"},
 "E453": {"text": "the tiles a side's people can walk to: one flood fill over the walking grid (a queue, a typed array) from round its Town Center, by the same steps as the pathfinder (E91), gates as its own see them, a flood as its research lets it; made again only when the walkable tiles, the ice, the flood or a gate's answer change; a building's spot is reached when a tile round it is (F23: a spot nobody can walk to is refused)"},
 "E454": {"text": "the fallen, the hit glow and the marker (Mid's fallen, drawHitGlow, drawRadar; D258, D262, D261)"},
 "E455": {"text": "a figure that dies in sight topples back, away from the way it faced, and fades"},
 "E456": {"text": "something of yours hit: the screen's edge glows, red for a rival, the flame's for the wild, fading"},
 "E457": {"text": "foes near your Town Center out of view: a marker on the screen's edge points at them, their count in it and their time to arrive under it; a tap looks at them"},
 "E458": {"text": "Teach (Mid's teachTo, teachWhy, teach): an older soldier learns the newer kind its shell's teach slot names, if that kind is of a later age; it stands where it is for the lesson (D263), paid up front"},
 "E459": {"text": "the lesson's price: what the newer kind costs more than the old, in each yield, plus tuition gold for each age climbed (Mid's teachCost)"},
 "E460": {"text": "the lesson done: the soldier is the newer kind, its health the same share of its new most (Mid's graduate)"},
 "E461": {"text": "prisoners (Mid's takePrisoner, payRansom, prisonersTick): a runner caught is held for a ransom of its price; paid, it walks home from its hall; unpaid in D264's time, it serves the captor"},
 "E462": {"text": "Zeal (Mid's zealCost, zealWhy, zeal): the Temple blesses the squad for gold if a priest stands with them; their blows are stronger for a while, then the Temple rests"},
 "E463": {"text": "each tick: a lesson that is over graduates; a prisoner unransomed in time goes over to its captor"},
 "E464": {"text": "a spy by a foe's building reads that side: its stores, age, research and army, kept with the time (Mid's intel)"},
 "E465": {"text": "priests, medics and spies (Mid's 14-sim-troops, spyTick): the support troops' own work, the heal of the wounded, and a runner taken prisoner"},
 "E466": {"text": "a hand on a runner that did not get away: a prisoner, not a blow (Mid's soldier tick; riders catch the foot)"},
 "E467": {"text": "a student stands still; a spy keeps to its own work; a priest converts when sent, else priests and medics walk with the army"},
 "E468": {"text": "walk with the army: to the nearest soldier of the side out, a few paces behind it (Mid's followArmy)"},
 "E469": {"text": "a priest beside a foe for D265's time turns it; walking off lets the spell fade; with no room the spell stops; then it rests (Mid's priestTick)"},
 "E470": {"text": "the wounded heal by the best healer of their side in reach, a hospital or a medic, not the sum: the first-order lag (QP, Mid's healTick)"},
 "E471": {"text": "a shooting building watches for spies within its sight of one, more with research (Mid's watchtower, guarded, spySeen)"},
 "E472": {"text": "a spy is unseen unless a foe's soldier or watching building is near; by a foe's building it reads them"},
 "E473": {"text": "the computers' spy: it takes the first unguarded building it sees that can be sabotaged"},
 "E474": {"text": "sabotage (Mid's sabotage): a building burns a share of its health or stalls and loses the head of its line; the spy is spent; a fall by fire pays nobody"},
 "E475": {"text": "a support troop told: a priest at a foe converts, a spy at a foe building sabotages, else it walks there"},
 "E478": {"text": "the Market (Mid's marketTrade and its prices): a yield by the raw lot, a good by the good lot, sold at sell of its worth and bought at buy, both moved by the going price, P = P0 (Q/Q0)^(-1/eps) (QAE), and by debased coin; what is sold adds to the stock, what is bought takes from it; the goods' names for what a caravan says"},
 "E479": {"text": "sell or buy one lot at a finished Market: raw sold for gold is a swap, not gathered; a good sold counts"},
 "E480": {"text": "the Mint debases the coin once: its gold now, every Market price dearer for good (Rome's denarius)"},
 "E481": {"text": "a venture from the Market (the commenda): back in a year with the return or lost; only the profit counts as gathered (QCF)"},
 "E482": {"text": "a venture lost to robbers on the way"},
 "E483": {"text": "the stock settles back toward normal each slow beat (QP), spice toward dearer while one side holds a whole route"},
 "E484": {"text": "a shop (Make): what it makes now and from what; the choice changes its worker's work; Learning by doing adds a share for each other finished plot of its kind (QAB); its worker takes the inputs from the stores and puts the good straight in, as a shepherd's milk"},
 "E485": {"text": "trade: the stops on the two routes, held by the post standing on them; a good's price at a place is its base, more where wanted, × the going price, × the distance from its Market (QCE); a load is the best-paying goods first, of a yield only the surplus"},
 "E486": {"text": "a caravan walks to a building's side or onto a stop; a way it cannot walk ends its run, and it waits a beat"},
 "E487": {"text": "a caravan on a route: load at its Market, sell at the far end (a keeper's cut), buy spice at a stop if told, bring it home, again if it repeats"},
 "E488": {"text": "a caravan with no route runs to the farthest ally's Market or Town Center for distance² pay (QCE), then home; a run starts at home, where the cargo is loaded: away from home with no run it goes home first, and with no way home it is paid nothing (N422)"},
 "E489": {"text": "robbers leave a caravan alone near its side's trade post or tower, or with a soldier of its side beside it"},
 "E490": {"text": "each frame the caravans; each beat a stop's holder, an armed caravan's blow and a whole route's pay; each slow beat the prices settle and ventures come home; each minute the Bank's interest"},
 "E491": {"text": "a caravan taken by a side pays its cargo and goods to the taker; one killed by the wild is robbed (the robbers' hoard waits for their camps)"},
 "E492": {"text": "the trade stops (Mid's ROUTES, PLACES.stop): four on each of the board's two middle lines, each seated on its road (E1107) after the roads are laid, so every stop is on a road, wanting one of the wares in turn; open ground, so a trade post stands over one"},
 "E493": {"text": "guards (Mid's escortPick, guardsOf): soldiers told to escort a caravan or garrison a stop keep to it as their post, as many as the trade's guard; when it is gone they come home"},
 "E494": {"text": "The war camp (F25, Mid's 38-camps; Albert, Nov 5 11:16 (7)): a wagon of two sizes (D287) unpacks where it is sent; positions in tiles of the grid, facing the side's Town Center (the gate side), else south (D279)."},
 "E495": {"text": "A camp's pieces: each spot [code, across, along toward home] turned by the facing and snapped to a top-left tile as Mid's snapPos (round of the centre less half the size); the large camp's palisade ring first, its gate the two middle squares of the home side."},
 "E496": {"text": "Why a camp cannot stand here (Mid's campWhy): off the map's edge, on water, on a building, on a resource (trees are allowed: they burn), too near a gift; and v100's own ground rule for every building, one flat height under each piece (L5)."},
 "E497": {"text": "The wagon unpacks (Mid's campUnpack): the trees within D279's burn of the camp burn and their forest floor clears; the pieces come off as sites; a large camp's felled trees outside its square and off its home side are laid as abatis, built; the wagon is gone."},
 "E498": {"text": "How many camps of a size a side may have out (Mid's campCap, campsOut): none before its age, one in it, two after; the large needs Camp wagons and a Store standing; camps standing (by their tents, not a last palisade square), wagons on the road and in the line all count."},
 "E499": {"text": "Why a camp wagon cannot be trained (Mid's campWhyTrain): the queue and the Train cell ask it."},
 "E500": {"text": "Soldiers raise their camp (Mid's canRaise, campRaise): a soldier on foot, idle or holding, looks each D279 look beat for the nearest of its side's unraised or worn pieces, each hand already there counting D279's crowd tiles more; beside it, its hands (D279's build × campbuild) join the crew and raise it as a villager's would (D204), or mend it at the raising rate."},
 "E501": {"text": "A soldier by a medical tent that is badly hurt or sick walks home to the Hospital (Mid's campSendHome); with none it stays and is bound where it is."},
 "E502": {"text": "The depot feeds the camp (Mid's campEat, every second; here as the people eat): a soldier within D279's reach eats from its stock; with it empty the town feeds it but it is unsupplied, slowed as after a charge and not mended at a shelter, and the camp says so once a minute."},
 "E503": {"text": "A Market caravan with nothing to carry runs food to a depot under half (Mid's supplyRun): from the store, keeping D279's keep, and the carter's fee in gold by the distance; loaded at its Market, unloaded at the depot, home again."},
 "E504": {"text": "The camp's tick: soldiers raise and mend, wagons that arrived unpack, the hurt are sent home each send beat; each minute rain, snow or frost wears every camp piece (Mid's campWearTick)."},
 "E505": {"text": "Relations (F28, Mid's 11-orders diplomacy): one stance a pair of sides (combat.js treaty, the Sides book); war is given with D281's notice; peace and an alliance are carried by an envoy and answered by the odds (QAF); an alliance is one ally a side."},
 "E506": {"text": "Why a side cannot take a stance toward another, or a group, now (Mid's relWhy, envoyWhy): a group by its regard (D282); a court not your vassal or lord; war while notice runs."},
 "E507": {"text": "An envoy rides from the Town Center to the court (its Town Center) or the group (its nearest band), is heard there, and rides home (Mid's sendEnvoy, envoyTick); while out, no other goes."},
 "E508": {"text": "The answer (Mid's judgeEnvoy): at war and not asked for peace, the envoy is killed; the player answers its own; peace is taken free, or for a truce's gold when the court's odds are good (Mid's PEACE.truce); an alliance is refused to the weak, by the strong with no other war, and by one allied elsewhere."},
 "E509": {"text": "A wild group's regard for each side (Mid's gangState, regardOf, addRegard, gangSync): peace and war follow it; an envoy makes a friend at D282's allyAt, and the friendship ends a little under it."},
 "E510": {"text": "Gifts (Mid's giftGain, QCD): each gift in the window buys less regard than the last, as the Danegeld bought ever-dearer peace; the Natives' need their Throne standing (it waits for Albert)."},
 "E511": {"text": "Vassals and tribute (F28, Mid's 36-economy; Albert, Nov 5 11:16 (2): tribute, the tax rate parked; QCG): a vassal is an ally whose lord its stances follow; it pays tribute, shares its trade's gold when loyal, and may rise."},
 "E512": {"text": "A side becomes a vassal (Mid's makeVassal): by surrender, its army beaten and the lord's soldiers at its Town Center, or as an ally twice outmatched that asks for a lord (loyal from the start); its stances become the lord's."},
 "E513": {"text": "A lord's hand on a vassal (Mid's breakTies, demand, forceTribute, levy, releaseLevy): cut it loose (war, the others warier), demand a store (loyalty, dearer each time), force double tribute with soldiers at its town (unrest), or call up half its soldiers to march under the lord's colours."},
 "E514": {"text": "A rebellion (Mid's rebel): a share of its villagers take up arms as rebels and its army turns on its lord; with a coalition, the restless rise together."},
 "E515": {"text": "Each slow beat (Mid's vassalTick): a rebellion is crushed or wins its freedom; otherwise the vassal pays its tribute from what it gathered since, its loyalty settles toward what the lord has earned (QP), its unrest moves, a loyal one sends gifts, and at the top it rebels; each minute two or more restless vassals may rise together."},
 "E516": {"text": "A new map: no notice running, every group's regard at its start."},
 "E517": {"text": "A vassal's soldier lost under its lord's colours costs loyalty; a foe its lord kills near its town earns its thanks (protect)."},
 "E518": {"text": "A blow on a shooter's stake, or on one of a wild group (its regard falls)."},
 "E519": {"text": "Field traps (F25, Mid's trapsTick, trapShown): hidden from all but their side, its allies and a side whose scout found them; a foe who steps on one springs it (D280)."},
 "E520": {"text": "A trap sprung: caltrops spike each walker once a while and wear flat; the others go off once; a net takes a prisoner (not an engine); horses take the worst."},
 "E522": {"text": "The computer's relations (Mid's aiDiplomacy, allyDuty, peaceAll): its personality's bold and the difficulty's envoy, allyAt and gang (D304), the rest D285: losing, it asks peace; strong and at peace with no war on, it gives notice; with a war on (or on Hard against the leader) it courts an ally; an ally helps a friend's town under attack, never at the cost of its own"},
 "E523": {"text": "Dynamic Diplomacy (Mid's LEAGUE, leagueTick): when one side runs far ahead, the others (not the player, not the leader's vassals) ally and make war on it; it breaks up when the lead falls back."},
 "E524": {"text": "A hidden trap is drawn flat on the ground from the Sprites book, in its side's shade or the foe's red; a site as a dashed ring; caltrops show a spike for each tread left (Mid's drawBld for traps)."},
 "E525": {"text": "what a side stands, raises, trains and has queued, asked of the things themselves"},
 "E526": {"text": "the by-need plan's eyes (QCM, QV): the seconds to the bell, what one more hand earns at the best find from home (a probe walks from the hall; wild: no plot), whether a plot pays its price back, each yield's hands, rate, income, shortfall and time, and the reorder point (the store runs out before its income can be rebuilt)"},
 "E527": {"text": "the army a side keeps: its personality's ceiling plus D291's armyAge an age, at most D226; at peace with every side, D285's stand of it (Mid's armyCap, armyAim, peaceAll)"},
 "E528": {"text": "the counter (QCN, Mid's bestCounter): among the soldiers it can train now, the best answer to what its foes field for its price, mixed with the next best so an army is never one kind; with no foe in the field, each in turn"},
 "E529": {"text": "a computer's turn, every D304 react s (Mid's think), in Mid's order: a site nobody raises, homes, drop-offs, plots, the age and its saving, the town's growth by payback, a scout, its buildings, towers, walls, a Wonder, priests and Zeal, medics, engines, caravans, its economy, spies, research, Muster and soldiers, then the hands by need and the war"},
 "E530": {"text": "shelter before it is needed: a Home (an Apartment once it can) when the people come within D152 of the room; one it cannot yet pay for is due, and the hands work toward it"},
 "E531": {"text": "a drop-off where D291's crew work a yield whose nearest find stands far from one"},
 "E532": {"text": "the shift to plots: one at a time, never more than the hands on its yield, when it beats the wild find and pays its price back in the time left; one it cannot yet afford is due"},
 "E533": {"text": "the age: once the town is big enough (D176) it saves for the next; a save once begun holds until the age is bought, and spends freely only when it has stalled (D290)"},
 "E534": {"text": "the town grows while one more villager pays its price in the time left (QCM), and not while it saves for the age unless food runs over; growing is a steady draw on the stores: a villager and its share of a home over its training"},
 "E535": {"text": "its personality's buildings in order (D303 build); while saving, only the first; a second barracks or place to train when every line is full"},
 "E536": {"text": "faith and care: priests with an army, Zeal on the soldiers fighting, medics (Mid's think)"},
 "E537": {"text": "engines to break what soldiers cannot, by D291's cycle and the age's late engine"},
 "E538": {"text": "research while not saving: its personality's list in order, each through the first step it waits on; with the list done, any step every D291 research-th turn"},
 "E539": {"text": "the hands by need (QCM): the goal and what is due are the cost; the bottleneck is the yield with the longest time to afford it (food first when the famine runway is short)"},
 "E540": {"text": "a hand moves to the bottleneck from a yield the goal does not need whose store does not then run out, or from one whose time stays under the bottleneck's after the move"},
 "E541": {"text": "with nothing short, the personality's mix: no stone and less gold in the Stone age, no iron before the Classical, a Wonder-builder a little of everything"},
 "E542": {"text": "every waiting or idle villager goes to the first yield in need it can find work for, else the one paying most (Nov 13, N337: one who lost her find and found none nearby, or stood idle, was skipped and stood for ever); then the war and the relations"},
 "E543": {"text": "the computers' economy (Mid's aiEconomy, without surplus selling, Albert 11:16 (5)): staff an idle shop, ventures with gold to spare over the age, trade posts on free stops, a Market, a Pasture, a workshop (the Raiders brew), caravans and their routes"},
 "E544": {"text": "the war (Mid's decideWar, QAF): a wave out is judged by its progress (D289): a blow or a step nearer; it charges once on contact, and goes home beaten or stalled; at home, the foe whose odds, bent by the opportunist's eye, best clear the personality's nerve"},
 "E545": {"text": "the wave sets out, its guard kept home; a few riders go for the foe's nearest drop-off to draw the defence apart; you are told when it is you"},
 "E546": {"text": "the ground's memory (D299): a layer as big as the ground's picture, cleared with each map; the worn earth round every building standing is laid at once"},
 "E547": {"text": "the ground remembers (Mid's scarCv): marks painted once into a layer under everything, so they cost nothing a frame; at a board point on the ground's picture"},
 "E548": {"text": "bare earth worn by feet round a finished building (not a field, a wall or a trap)"},
 "E549": {"text": "the dark where someone fell, wider for a big body, a blade's cut for a soldier"},
 "E550": {"text": "burnt ground and rubble where a building fell (not a wall)"},
 "E551": {"text": "the moon (QB to first order, QC): it runs ahead of the sun by its phase on a declination that swings from the sun's at new to its opposite at full, so a full moon rises at sunset; its lit fraction (1 − cos i) ÷ 2"},
 "E552": {"text": "the sky told ahead, the sky's news, the flood and the ruts (D293–D295); the ground's marks laid when someone falls or a building falls"},
 "E553": {"text": "the chain (QH) rolled ahead a forecast step for each step of Weather signs, never less than an hour; when the last rolled hour turns, its sign is told"},
 "E554": {"text": "when the sky turns its news is told, with why in the chain's own odds (Mid's skyTurn and wxWhy)"},
 "E555": {"text": "water over the shore while the flood stands (KI4); the mud a step meets: the wetness, deeper by water (pooling) and by traffic, the ruts' depth (passes ÷ n0)^0.4 (QS, D294)"},
 "E556": {"text": "each land tile's distance to the inland water, once a map: the shore that pools and the land a flood covers"},
 "E557": {"text": "the flood harms a finished building whose middle stands within its rise, unless its side has Levees; you are told"},
 "E558": {"text": "marks on the water and the ground, and the sky band (D296–D298, Mid's drawLakeRipples, drawRainRings, drawSky)"},
 "E559": {"text": "ripples drift on the lakes, inside the shore; none on ice"},
 "E560": {"text": "rain rings sit on the ground, fixed to the world, fewer as the rain eases; only close up"},
 "E561": {"text": "the horizon: a band of sky along the top of the glass, coloured by the hour and the weather"},
 "E562": {"text": "clouds cross the band with the wind"},
 "E563": {"text": "the wind is heard as hard as it blows (HA4, HX4)"},
 "E564": {"text": "the dens and drifters' camps laid in Z4 on their own dice, so the map's other rolls stay as they were; a robbers' camp at each end of the two trade routes (Mid's layCamps)"},
 "E565": {"text": "a find's guards on a ring round it, each bound to it as its home; drifters in a row beside their fire (Mid's addFind)"},
 "E566": {"text": "a walker that leaves the land (no fall, no carcass), and a find taken away"},
 "E567": {"text": "the Challenge's hazards and the events: a hazard counts only off Easy; the level played multiplies the score"},
 "E568": {"text": "where an event comes in: a spot on one of the land's edges, its far side through the middle, or a free spot of the wild away from every town"},
 "E569": {"text": "an event comes only in its season, or in the rain; never the same twice running"},
 "E570": {"text": "a Poisson wait with a floor: least plus −(mean − least) ln U (QM)"},
 "E571": {"text": "what each event does when it starts, each second it runs and when it ends (Mid's EV)"},
 "E572": {"text": "a sinkhole's star of cracks, each arm bending as it goes, laid on the ground's memory from its place"},
 "E573": {"text": "once a second: the event running, else the warning ahead of the next, else its start; the horde and the travellers; a walker past its way out leaves (Mid's eventsTick)"},
 "E574": {"text": "the horde under the Outlaws hazard: told two seasons and one ahead, then it comes for the weakest side at war with the outlaws, growing with the age (Mid's hordeTick)"},
 "E575": {"text": "a wayfarer from the middle of each edge in turn, to the far one (Mid's wayfarers)"},
 "E576": {"text": "a bolt where it falls: drawn, the ground scorched, the thunder told"},
 "E577": {"text": "a running herd tramples who stands in its way and the soil of the fields it crosses (Mid's herdTick)"},
 "E578": {"text": "quicksand on the ground while it lasts"},
 "E579": {"text": "a falling star streaks down onto its spot"},
 "E580": {"text": "a find drawn as blobs from the Sprites book"},
 "E581": {"text": "flames on what burns, with its smoke, as strong as the fire"},
 "E582": {"text": "the wild's guards and travellers, the robbers' raids, the computers' detachments and the scout (Mid's wildTick, wayfarerTick, natRaid, lootRun, scoutTick)"},
 "E583": {"text": "a guard keeps to its home: it looks for a stranger near home (a raider, near its reach), lets go past its leash and walks home when far; a raid's band goes home when its time is out"},
 "E584": {"text": "a defender weighs a stranger now and then: it fights with probability V / C, C the stranger's strength over its own (QAH)"},
 "E585": {"text": "a traveller joins the first side to meet him, as villagers (on its rally job), or as food when the town is full"},
 "E586": {"text": "one weighted draw: p = w_i / Σw (QAR)"},
 "E587": {"text": "now and then the robbers send a band from the camp nearest a side at a villager or caravan of any side they can beat, drawn toward a load, away from a guard and back to a town robbed lately (D307), and call them back after a spell"},
 "E588": {"text": "a computer hires drifters it can pay for, and sends half its idle army at the nearest find while nothing else is on; home when it is taken"},
 "E589": {"text": "a scout left to itself goes for a find whose guards have fallen, else loops the land"},
 "E590": {"text": "the finds: the first side to touch one whose guards have fallen takes what it holds, once; the ruins a free research of its age. A find taken is marked taken, not with the taker's side (Nov 13, N347: the player is side 0, which read as not taken, so a fallen star paid again every beat a unit stood by it)"},
 "E591": {"text": "drifters fight for whoever pays, with a unit of the payer beside them and room in the army"},
 "E592": {"text": "fire: the ground's dryness by Rothermel (QT), the t² fire's heat across a gap (QU), and a chance in a step from a rate (QM)"},
 "E593": {"text": "a wooden building catches fire, and the nearest villagers of its side run with buckets (Mid's ignite)"},
 "E594": {"text": "a fire burns its building and, every few seconds, may light a wooden neighbour; a building that burns out falls (Mid's fireTick)"},
 "E595": {"text": "in a summer storm lightning strikes a wooden building now and then, and a forge throws sparks (Mid's lightning)"},
 "E596": {"text": "sickness: a town's people near its seat or a depot; more cases from outside in summer and winter, fewer with research"},
 "E597": {"text": "each health beat: cases from outside, the spread \u03b2 S I / N (QAQ), and each sick one cured by a healer near, dying, or well again (Mid's healthTick); who gets well is immune for good (SIR's R, N47, N397): only the susceptible catch it, over the whole town"},
 "E598": {"text": "the view's eyes, lights and stage: the light and each eye's range (real math, Albert Nov 6), the camera's glide, the lights after dark, the theatrics, the dressing, the small map and the draw budget (Mid's view, F33 and F34)"},
 "E599": {"text": "the light on the ground (D117): the sun's by its height, the moon's by its phase and height, the stars'; cloud dims it to the overcast night's share"},
 "E600": {"text": "a thing's range (QAL): the least of the horizon from its eye, the eye's range in this light (a lantern gives a building part of the dark back) and what the weather lets anyone see (QK)"},
 "E603": {"text": "another side's building shows only while your people see it"},
 "E604": {"text": "the player's Reduce motion, read from the phone; the draw budget's level; still: is motion off, by the setting or by load (Mid's lessMotion, DRAW, still)"},
 "E605": {"text": "a phone that falls behind sheds a level of drawing (tree shadows, then the moving extras, then half the pixels) and climbs back when fast again (Mid's shed); the whole frame is timed, the world's steps and the drawing (N23, Gemini audit 2: with the drawing alone timed, a phone slow in its steps never shed), against shares of the frame's real interval at the rate it runs, not a fixed 12 ms (SoRen's numbers were for 60 frames a second; Albert, Nov 9)"},
 "E606": {"text": "a cache held to a budget of pixels, its size kept as a running total: the least lately used go first (a picture used is moved to the back), their canvases emptied at once so the phone gets the memory back (N23, Gemini audit 2: the first made had gone first, so pictures in use every frame were thrown out and made again)"},
 "E607": {"text": "the camera glides on a critically damped spring (QAW): to a point, Home or the small map's tap; a finger takes over; still means a jump (Mid's spring, camGo, camStop)"},
 "E608": {"text": "Follow keeps the picked units in the middle until they are gone or a finger moves the map (Mid's followCam)"},
 "E609": {"text": "fire's colour from its temperature (QF, a black body), its life in the rain (an open flame dims, a covered one keeps), its glow fading as 1/r² (QAU) and the flame itself, leaning with the wind (Mid's kelvinRGB, flameLife, glow, flame)"},
 "E610": {"text": "a flame's light on the ground: a disc fading to a quarter at half its reach, added to the dark, only when there is dark to light"},
 "E611": {"text": "what burns after dark: a blazing or badly hurt building, a hearth in a home, a lantern at a lit door, a camp's fire, a caravan's lantern (Mid's drawLight, HEARTH)"},
 "E612": {"text": "theatrics: one pop curve (a finished building and a newborn swell and settle), ripples where you tap, three sizes of celebration (a building, an upgrade rolling through the army, a new age or a wonder) and the pale flash (Mid's popC, celebrate, ripple, ripDraw, drawFlash)"},
 "E613": {"text": "words on the map keep one size whatever the zoom, as the screen's own words; a label is a pill (Mid's mapFont, tag)"},
 "E614": {"text": "the dressing: a site staked out and rising with the work, a finished building's pop and fresh glow, its flags, piles and chimney smoke (Mid's drawBld)"},
 "E615": {"text": "a building site: the stakes round its footprint, the walls rising with the work between two posts, the bar, and z when nobody builds it"},
 "E616": {"text": "a building's flags, drawn live over its picture where its art put them, waving more in a strong wind (Mid's flagsOn)"},
 "E617": {"text": "a side's stores as piles by the camp that takes them in: a pyramid by log₁₀ of the store, drawn once per count and zoom (Mid's PILE, pileAt, pileArt)"},
 "E618": {"text": "a chimney's plume: rising ∝ x^(2/3) (QAV, Briggs) and widening ∝ x^0.9, leaning downwind (Mid's smoke)"},
 "E619": {"text": "a figure in motion: the woodcutter's lean into its tree (the view's own memory), the step's rise and fall, a lunge into a blow and a shooter's kick, the recoil, a hurt soldier's stagger; then its marks: nerve, rout, march, idle z and focus F (Mid's LEAN, drawUnit, idleMark)"},
 "E620": {"text": "the small map: the ground, the fog, buildings you know (a seat is a star), units you see, an army coming flashing red, and the screen's box; tap to glide there, drag to sweep (Mid's drawMini, miniIncoming, miniAt)"},
 "E622": {"text": "a banner on a building that flies live leaves its place to the view (Mid's FLAGS)"},
 "E623": {"text": "the shadows of the trees, bushes and rocks in sight, not the deep woods, cast like everything else (QAT, Mid's shadowPath); the draw budget sheds them first"},
 "E624": {"text": "is a thing in a side's sight: its own, the land's and the wild's always; another side's only when that side's eyes saw it at the last look, or the eye asking sees it now (range and line, QAL and QAM); the one check for the screen, the fight and the computers"},
 "E625": {"text": "a board at peace (Mid's 39-games, D322): the truce clock, the hidden age it opens, standing down, the chronicle; the deal of the peoples for the next match"},
 "E626": {"text": "a board truce: no two living sides at war and no notice running; how long it has held"},
 "E627": {"text": "the chronicle: the match's lines, kept to D322's chron, newest last"},
 "E628": {"text": "standing down (demobilisation, as every peace since Rome): the soldiers at home above the keep go home as villagers, one for one; yours to your gathering job when you ask, a computer's above the army it keeps at peace"},
 "E629": {"text": "once a second: the truce clock starts or stops; a year of it opens the hidden age for every side; after D322's stand.after the computers stand down"},
 "E630": {"text": "the three crowns and the overall (Mid's crownsOf): Wealth all a side gathered, War the cost of the enemy people and buildings it destroyed, Wellbeing its people in health, its places of care and its laurels; each crown gives a side a point for every side below it, the score breaks a tie"},
 "E631": {"text": "the last step of the hidden age ends the match for everyone: everyone wins, the crowns say who won what"},
 "E632": {"text": "a side's people: its civilisation, and the bonus row it holds from the start (Mid's CIVS fx, applied by QCA as research is)"},
 "E633": {"text": "the War crown's count (Mid's warCredit): a side destroying another side's unit or building is credited its cost; the wild cost nothing"},
 "E634": {"text": "a raid on yours: an enemy strikes or fells one of your things; told by the mail, by sight, by ear or by messenger (QCH)"},
 "E635": {"text": "the mail (Mid's say and tell, D323): a line shows a while unless it is quiet, the same line within merge is a count on the first, the newest kept; news out of sight comes by the post (QCH)"},
 "E636": {"text": "which way a place lies from your Town Center, of eight"},
 "E637": {"text": "how a line reaches you (QCH): in sight now; a fight in earshot by its way only; else by a messenger walking from your Town Center, if the Post serves that far"},
 "E638": {"text": "a line said: by messenger later, heard as a fight, or now; merged with its repeat, kept, shown"},
 "E639": {"text": "the messengers arrive"},
 "E640": {"text": "the world's news: a line of your age every while, none at first"},
 "E641": {"text": "the peoples on the Start card: the one you pick and its line (its own soldier, the one it replaces, its wonder, its bonus); the others are dealt at random"},
 "E642": {"text": "the milestones and tips (Mid's MS_TEST, advise): each milestone said once a match the first time it is true; a tip names what the town needs next until you have done it"},
 "E643": {"text": "a hint retires once learned: what you did, counted on this phone, to D325's learned"},
 "E644": {"text": "what each tap teaches: training a kind, a job, a building, the next age"},
 "E645": {"text": "the fourteen milestones' tests, and their numbers filled from the books"},
 "E646": {"text": "gold short while another store is full"},
 "E647": {"text": "what the town needs next, first that holds: room, villagers, wood, idle hands, a barracks, spearmen, the next age, food, gold, a fire, sickness, gold work"},
 "E648": {"text": "every lesson beat: a new tip is said, then the first milestone newly true, one a beat"},
 "E649": {"text": "a computer chases its crown (Mid's chaseCrown): the wellbeing chaser builds each place of care it lacks; every side takes the hidden age when it opens and runs its steps, the match a race to the last"},
 "E650": {"text": "The corners: the board's four, clockwise a quarter turn apart from the screen's top left; yours, the first, sits A6 round (the bottom left, Albert Nov 6), the computers' follow in turn"},
 "E652": {"text": "The way home (QCQ, Mid's openWays and wayHome): nothing is walled in; a find cut off by woods gets the fewest trees cleared between it and its Town Center, never across water; the pocket's grove is kept"},
 "E653": {"text": "Z3, laid by the Randomizer: each find of D65 at three pockets' worth, and the land's specialty once more at one pocket's, at a rolled spot in the ring, off the road; the same dice in every corner"},
 "E654": {"text": "The land's character (D329, Mid's LAND): past the pocket every find is worth its store's share"},
 "E655": {"text": "The save and the safety net (Mid's 34-save and 41-boot): the game saves itself on the save beat and on leaving, keeps the one before, waits out a fight; an error costs a frame, never the game"},
 "E656": {"text": "each kind of error logged once; a second kind holds the save (the last good one stands) and says so"},
 "E657": {"text": "the save: the seed (the map is laid again from it), the lists, the climate, the sides, what they know, and what differs from the fresh map; each module adds its own on the save hook; a thing or a unit is kept as its place in the lists"},
 "E658": {"text": "a save opened: the places turned back into the things and units, the Maps, Sets and Infinity by their tags (D331)"},
 "E659": {"text": "the save waits while you fight, at most D331's fight; a failed save says so once in D331's fail; the test field is never saved"},
 "E660": {"text": "saves roll through D331's slots, one set per build folder, so live and a preview never share one; when storage is full the oldest goes to make room; a save that will not open is skipped and the one before opens"},
 "E661": {"text": "the game opened from a save: the fresh map from its seed, then the lists, the sides and the changes laid back, then each module's own"},
 "E662": {"text": "The opening: the game opens where you left it, newest save first, saying so if it had to open an older one; the address never ends a match; ?test opens the test field on its own seed"},
 "E663": {"text": "New game (Mid's applyScenario and testField): the scenario's buildings and people placed by the placing rules nearest their spot"},
 "E664": {"text": "A scenario (D330): the age, the store and the research for you (or every court), the relations, the buildings and villagers, the length"},
 "E665": {"text": "The test field (D333): you and one rival at war, the other two gone, every store full, both armies down the road from your Town Center"},
 "E666": {"text": "the economy's part of the save: a finished game clears the save instead"},
 "E667": {"text": "the war's part of the save: the waves, the orders, the relations, the squads"},
 "E668": {"text": "the computers' part of the save: their clocks, plans and minds"},
 "E670": {"text": "The test tools (Mid's matchLog, copyLog, tapCount): the match log for Claude to read, tap counts kept on this phone"},
 "E671": {"text": "a row a minute (D335): each side's age, villagers, soldiers and stores, or none once it fell; and your own ledger so far, in and out by reason (led), and how many of your villagers are at each kind of work (vil: food, wood, stone, gold, iron, build, idle, wait, walk ...; Albert, Nov 13 20:56), so a jump in the stores names its source (Albert, Nov 4: the match-log additions; Nov 13: the runaway income)"},
 "E672": {"text": "copied to the clipboard, or through a hidden box where the clipboard is refused"},
 "E673": {"text": "the menu's part of the save: the mail, the news, the options, the match log"},
 "E674": {"text": "a guarded find stands in its own clearing, as Mid lays its guards on the ring round it (26 from home): it is laid only where the ring is open land, and the trees on the ring are cleared, as the pocket's grove is kept"},
 "E675": {"text": "The Guide, written from the books (Mid's guideModel): every building, unit, research step, age, people, find and rule, its numbers read from the tables, so it stays true as they change; an age is a building's or a kind's, or the first"},
 "E676": {"text": "a unit is trained at the first building that trains it (or the kind it replaces), as Mid gives each its one home; a history line sits under the shell's look unless the Guide's key says otherwise; a step's line under tech:key, else its key"},
 "E677": {"text": "a rule's numbers and names are filled from the books: {D:path} a measurement, {S:code} a shell's name, {J:key} a words entry, {fx:stat} the research that raises it"},
 "E678": {"text": "Mid's guideModel, field for field, on v100's tables (a building's menu is its Build tab, else why it is off the menu); no line of what a thing does yet: v100's books hold none"},
 "E679": {"text": "History (Mid's yearOf, histRows, histText): a step's date as a year (BC below none; an era by name; undated last), the dated steps in order, a row as text to copy"},
 "E681": {"text": "a plain record held in two places (a war order, a camp, an ambush) is saved once, tagged own, and its other places as same; opened, they are one record again (the save first walks what it holds and counts which records it meets twice; the things and units are walked by their fields, each once)"},
 "E682": {"text": "a computer's estimate of what one more worker earns on a yield is kept for the slow beat (D182: the computers' slow looks) and not worked out again each turn: the finds change slower than that; when they run out, one is worked out again a frame and the rest keep theirs till a later turn, so a turn never works them all at once"},
 "E683": {"text": "the computers' clocks start spread over one turn (react ÷ how many), so no two think on the same frame; each keeps its own turn"},
 "E684": {"text": "the work queue: slow jobs, each a generator that yields where it may stop; one job of a key at a time (a computer whose last turn is still running does not start another)"},
 "E685": {"text": "a frame runs the queue's jobs in turn, a slice each, up to D339's slices (QCR: counted, not timed, so the game does not depend on the machine); a job not done goes to the back and resumes next frame"},
 "E686": {"text": "a site the computer cannot pay for, or may not build, is not searched for; the search asks each tile only about the ground, and the build is asked with the search's own pass (apart), so the spot picked is one plan() takes (N422: N84 left plan() without it; a spot beside a Farm was refused every turn)"},
 "E680": {"text": "the Guide as Markdown (Mid's guideMd): one table a part, its headings from the words, a bar in a cell made a slash"},
 "E800": {"text": "made once a map: which tiles are grass, bare or other land; a micro-relief, and on it each tile's flow by the steepest of the eight ways, the area that drains through it and its wetness index ln(a ÷ tan β) (TOPMODEL); the snow's lognormal drift by the relief; the six layers' weights; the clusters of flowers and pebbles; and for each texel of the picture the tile under it, found by walking the height until the view and the land agree (a cliff face, where they never do, is left to the ground below)"},
 "E803": {"text": "the flowers and pebbles close up: each cluster's offspring from its own seed, as many open as its season allows, none under snow or on a trodden path; one path a colour, filled in layers"},
 "E804": {"text": "a tile's wetness by its wetness index and its snow by its drift: one home each for the step, the footing and the picture"},
 "E805": {"text": "a step's wear on the grass: the pressure of everything that walks there (body, mount, kit and the load carried) over its prints, past the soil's precompression stress (lower when wet), by the log of the ratio, in person-steps: a light step wears nothing, a laden villager a little more than an empty one, a knight or a ram several times"},
 "E806": {"text": "an order leaves its soldiers tired as a charge does (D247 slow, settling back with tired): give many orders and the army slows (Mid's ORDER.tired; Albert, Nov 8)"},
 "E807": {"text": "QCJ while two soldiers form up (D242): the one of lower precedence gives the whole way, softly (foot before archers before riders before engines; Mid's FORMING soft)"},
 "E808": {"text": "a side's exposure to cold and wet (D354): the air's cold and the ground's wetness, each cut by its research (Wool cloaks, Oiled cloaks, Chimneys); read by the meals, the sickness and the nerve"},
 "E809": {"text": "a soldier's nerve settles no higher than its full × (1 − D354 nerve × its side's exposure): cold and wet sap morale"},
 "E810": {"text": "familiarity (D355): a cell is known to a side from the last time one of its eyes stood in it; nothing is saved, so a reload forgets the scouted ground and keeps the own ground"},
 "E811": {"text": "a side's familiarity with a tile: one on its own ground (a finished building of its own within D355 home), the Natives' and the wild's everywhere, else the memory fading from the last look"},
 "E813": {"text": "a scout set to Stealth (its card) goes on foot at D224's sneak and takes the spy's veil (E472): unseen unless a foe's soldier is near or a shooting building watches"},
 "E815": {"text": "what a research does, in words from its effects; with no effects, why it is there. N62 (N385): each effect is said as the word, then the amount (\"Train time −25%\"); a cell shows the first, with a mark when there are more; a name too wide for a cell is shown by its short form (J58)"},
 "E816": {"text": "where the finger leaves the ghost: Mid's snap first; if nothing caught it and it stands on no guide, the nearest guide line within tol pulls it on (a light pull, as a PDF editor's), so what is drawn is what it snaps to"},
 "E817": {"text": "the small pop-ups on the map (a quick attack on bare ground, the ice's clear, the villager's square) stand a slot above the point, centred on it, never under it; where the top bar or the help line leaves no room, a slot below instead"},
 "E818": {"text": "the bottom bars' height, told by the menu when it changes (the top bar's is read as topOf)"},
 "E819": {"text": "the villager's square (Albert, Nov 8 21:35-21:46): a tap on your villager opens four boxes above its head, Build, Send to, Attack, More; More turns them to Garrison, Rally, Info, Focus; Send to and Attack wait for the next tap on the map; any other tap closes it and lets the villager go; it follows the villager as it walks"},
 "E820": {"text": "a villager told to take cover goes into the nearest building of yours with room, as fright sends it; like fright's, it comes out when no foe is near (so with none near, there is nothing to hide from)"},
 "E821": {"text": "one tap listener for the whole screen (Albert, Nov 9): every button with a verb answers wherever it sits; the pause panel lived outside the three listeners and its buttons never ran"},
 "E822": {"text": "the rate the frames run at, one home: at rest the idle rate, shedding frames the lower rate, otherwise the full rate; the loop paces by it and the shed budgets by it"},
 "E825": {"text": "every menu ends in the help line, always there (Info Help Ribbon 1): the latest message, and a tap opens Help; the same line under the top ribbon comes and goes on its own (Albert, Nov 9 12:29)"},
 "E828": {"text": "the ring's marker inside a box: its colour and its state (dim not chosen, lit chosen, run at work). N62 (N385): in the dock a ring is drawn only at work (run)"},
 "E829": {"text": "one colour a kind of work (Albert, Nov 9 12:03-12:19): the age-up white; soldiers red; scouts, envoys and spies blue; caravans gold; other people green; a research blue, green while it is being researched (Albert, Nov 14, N369: \"All tech should be blue. Not green and not red\"; was its family's colour)"},
 "E830": {"text": "dim is the colour mixed into the tray brown by one share, never picked by hand"},
 "E831": {"text": "the box's outline as one path from 12 o'clock, clockwise, round its corners"},
 "E832": {"text": "each ring drawn once its box has a size, and again only when its size, colour or state changes; measured by the box the ring is laid on (its padding box), so a ring in a split bar is whole on every side (N369: the new game's option rings were clipped on one side: a box in a split bar cut off whatever passed its own edge, and its ring lies on that edge, half outside, so a side went missing; the chosen box now shows all of its ring, above its neighbours)"},
 "E833": {"text": "how far the work is: a queue's first item by the time left on it; the help line by its time to read"},
 "E834": {"text": "every frame the running rings recede, pinned at 12, clockwise, gone when the work is done"},
 "E836": {"text": "MR title: every menu's title row ends in back, book and close, always in the same place (Albert, Nov 9 12:57)"},
 "E837": {"text": "a help line wider than its bar shows the chevron; the chevron opens it to two lines and closes it again"},
 "E838": {"text": "the chevron's tap: open or close the help lines"},
 "E839": {"text": "a font from the type rule: its weight and size, in the face named"},
 "E840": {"text": "Relations and Misfits in the dock (N385: tap, then choices): the peoples as cells, each with its standing in its colour; a tap on one shows it and its four choices (gift or bribe, war, terms, ally); Back returns to the peoples. The choices' coloured rings are not drawn in the dock, where a ring means work"},
 "E841": {"text": "the small cards are two columns of the mold wide: the width read from the bar's own width, set once a render"},
 "E843": {"text": "after a card is drawn: the mold's line and base put in and fitted, the dark patches laid (E1306), the map told how far up from the bottom the menus reach when that changed (FK.bars), the mini map's box let go; then Paused: its top line, then Speed and Sounds, each a row of tiles under its word; play or the X plays again"},
 "E845": {"text": "the book: Welcome back mid-match (Resume, New game), paused"},
 "E848": {"text": "a small card's title: the title on its own row, back, book and close beneath it"},
 "E850": {"text": "a ring is the box's outline: the box drops its own border so the ring sits on the edge, one line, never a second inside"},
 "E851": {"text": "what a side cannot build yet (age, research, a building it needs, a later age): the locks before the limit; the Build menu hides these"},
 "E852": {"text": "a building raised into another where it stands (the Gate's way over a wall): taken down, the new one's site laid in its place and paid; put back as it was when there is no room"},
 "E855": {"text": "a picked unit: the green ring at its feet, thick and glowing"},
 "E856": {"text": "a picked unit takes the next tap as its order, by the tap table (E1038, SN43). While the ice question is open the pick waits for its answer"},
 "E861": {"text": "a builder's next site: the first one laid, then the nearest (a wall line keeps to the nearest piece) (Albert, Nov 9: first placed, first built)"},
 "E862": {"text": "the year's clock: the game's time from a start late in spring (D359), for seasons, leaves, the meadow, the weather and the harvest"},
 "E863": {"text": "the woods: walkable for a person or a rider at the woods' pace (D360), never for engines or wagons; the path pays the time lost, so the edge wins unless the trees are much shorter"},
 "E864": {"text": "a tap anywhere on a building's drawn shape is the building: the front-most whose picture is solid under the finger (Albert, Nov 9 item 8.7)"},
 "E865": {"text": "a hold is only the box drag to pick many (Albert, Nov 9 item 8.5): nothing else listens for it"},
 "E866": {"text": "the menus' sizes, once: every px in the style read from the Screen book's css entry (SN35); a row word's tap area reaches up to the mold's slot from its 40 (N423)"},
 "E867": {"text": "words drawn on the map at the head type (SN20), never a size typed in the code"},
 "E868": {"text": "the sight map, per side: each tile counts the eyes on it (VIS), remembers being seen (EXPL); the buildings a side has seen stay as it saw them (MEM)"},
 "E869": {"text": "an eye's tiles: every tile in its reach whose ground, a body high, its line clears over the tops between (trees and buildings by height); cast again only when the eye steps to a new tile, its reach changes, or the tops change"},
 "E870": {"text": "seen now: a unit whose tile is in sight; a building any of whose corners is"},
 "E871": {"text": "the fog of war's veil: one pixel a tile, dark where never seen, dim where seen before, clear in sight, drawn over the land and smoothed"},
 "E872": {"text": "the Start page's Fog of war: off, every side sees all (one rule for all)"},
 "E873": {"text": "the fog drawn by Beer-Lambert: its veil 1 - e^(-beta x path), the path the fog layer or the camera's height inside it, the height read from the zoom"},
 "E874": {"text": "a crossing is ice or woods: the same modes for both (single file, thin out, one at a time, stick to edges, go around), chosen once on the crossing card"},
 "E875": {"text": "in the woods a missile is stopped by the trunks with chance 1 - e^(-stems x trunk x L), L the metres of wood the line runs through"},
 "E876": {"text": "in the woods the line breaks into one-on-one duels (Lanchester's ancient model, the Linear Law): a blow is shared among all who strike the same foe"},
 "E877": {"text": "an eye facing no fog: every point round its rim already seen by others, so it casts nothing; eyes in one cell share one cast"},
 "E878": {"text": "a sight cell's woods: how much of it is wood and its ground under the trees, so a ray through the trunks thins by e^(-n d L) and a ray over the canopy meets a wall"},
 "E879": {"text": "the fog of war is saved with the game: the ground each side has seen and the buildings it remembers, and whether fog is on; sight is cast again on load"},
 "E880": {"text": "the land kept while the camera holds still: one copy drawn back instead of the ground, the meadow, the scars and the skin each frame (SoRen's keyed layers)"},
 "E889": {"text": "the land sheet slid by the camera's move since it was drawn: a pan costs one copy, not a new land"},
 "E893": {"text": "a sheet (a cel of the old cartoon): a picture a margin larger than the screen, slid pixel for pixel with the camera, painted again only when it slides past its margin, the zoom or its key changes, or its time runs out; the land and the fog of war are each one"},
 "E894": {"text": "with ?test the frame meter shows from the start (its only door, the Yard, left the Paused card in N6)"},
 "E896": {"text": "the weather's fog as a sheet: each 5 m cell veiled by Beer-Lambert through the fog above it, the layer's top level over the lowest ground, so it pools in the hollows"},
 "E897": {"text": "your own people under the canopy drawn as a ring over the trees, so you see who is inside"},
 "E900": {"text": "the ground's soil and paper (N11): wet and snow on the ground for play, and the light, season, snow, flowers and glints over the paper sheets"},
 "E901": {"text": "over the baked ground: the hills' sun and shade and the meadow's soft patches as one small soft picture, then the snow sheet, then the flowers"},
 "E902": {"text": "grass is painted a light neutral and also on its own sheet; that sheet takes the season's one colour (multiplied), recoloured only when the colour moves a visible step, so the ground is never painted again for the season"},
 "E904": {"text": "a marsh is shallow water; reeds stand in it"},
 "E905": {"text": "each paper sheet casts a thin shadow on the sheet below, along its edge"},
 "E906": {"text": "the flowers come up in new places each year; the pebbles stay where they lie"},
 "E907": {"text": "snow is one more paper sheet, in six steps: it lies where play's drift would cover the ground, hollows first"},
 "E908": {"text": "glints on the water: a few short strokes that come and go"},
 "E909": {"text": "how far each water tile lies from its shore, in tiles (a chamfer distance in two passes); the water's three sheets follow it, so their edges are smooth"},
 "E910": {"text": "the blades fade in with the zoom, as v80's did: none from far away, full close up"},
"E911": {"text": "a path kept as lists of points, so a run of one colour can be joined into one shape"},
"E912": {"text": "the ground is recorded once per map as shapes, not painted into a picture: each run of one colour or line becomes one shape, every piece wound the same way so joined pieces never cut holes; replayed under the camera, sharp at every zoom (the paper ground mock, Albert Nov 10 08:38)"},
"E913": {"text": "the ground's shapes, the grass's one shape (the season's colour and the blades' bed), the water's fill level and its foam, the blade tiles and the cloud tile"},
"E914": {"text": "a blade tile drawn at the screen's own pixels for the zoom in hand, thin triangles in the two blade colours, wrapped at the tile's edges: always sharp; only its scale is on the pattern, the camera on the canvas (Safari)"},
"E915": {"text": "the blades' marks, made once per map from the seed: where in the tile, how long, how much lean, dark or light"},
"E916": {"text": "the cloud tile: soft noise that wraps, made once per map"},
"E917": {"text": "cloud shadows drift over the land each frame, the camera and the drift on the canvas (Safari); still when motion is reduced"},
"E918": {"text": "the water fills every cut up to one level just under the grass (the mock's 'high'): the banks below it are drawn as shallow water with foam at its edge; drawing only, the walking rules are unchanged"},
"E919": {"text": "the minimap's picture: the shapes replayed once, small"},
"E920": {"text": "the shapes are kept by layer (tiles, faces, reeds, then each band's contours) and by colour within a layer, so a whole map replays as a few dozen fills, in the order it was painted"},
"E921": {"text": "each water band gets its own layer, laid in order before the first contour: the shapes are kept by colour within a layer, so in one layer the shallow band's fills all drew after the deep band's and hid its smooth edge, leaving the tile squares (Albert, Nov 10: lakes look like Minecraft)"},
"E922": {"text": "the grass mask (where the season's colour and the blades go) is cut from the contour cells, not the tiles: a whole grass cell goes in, runs of flat cells merged into one shape; the shore and hill cells add only their grass part; so the tint and blades stop at the grass's smooth edge and never step over the dirt (Albert, Nov 10: odd slopes toward lakes)"},
"E923": {"text": "the water's distance from shore starts at the waterline itself: a water tile beside land takes the fraction of a tile to where the height crosses zero, and the distance spreads only through water; measured from the land tiles' middles it followed the turned grid's staircase, so the bands stepped (Albert, Nov 10, #5: the coast's sawtooth)"},
"E924": {"text": "the marsh: each marsh tile draws a number from the seed; where it is over D366's tussock the tile is water, else a tussock of grass; the water's edge runs between the tiles' middles (marching squares) and goes in with the shallows, drawn after the grass's colour and blades, with their foam on its edge; so the marsh is smooth and dotted with tussocks, never the tile staircase (Albert, Nov 10, #9)"},
 "E925": {"text": "the Daily challenge: when it is on, the civ, difficulty, length (Albert, Nov 10 11:51) and the dangers are drawn from the day's own dice at the lot's odds, shown picked and locked, the same for everyone that day (Albert, Nov 10, #14)"},
 "E926": {"text": "a price is one line in one colour, by the store you are shortest of: red when short, white at exactly enough, green past it (Ring red, white and green, three steps, no ramp); the stores you lack are underlined (Decisions Nov 11, #13: the fade on the whole line, the missing resource marked extra); the parts of a price sit a hair apart, with no space, so three fit a cell"},
 "E927": {"text": "the Top Info Ribbon's worked readings (SN5): the hour, the bell (a wonder's count, green if mine, red if theirs, else the time left when the match is timed), the people as count/cap, and the rank by score among the sides"},
 "E928": {"text": "the time of day as hours and minutes, one home for the clock and the ribbon"},
 "E929": {"text": "a villager walking home with a load carries it on the back, a bundle in its store's colour (Albert, Nov 10, #35)"},
 "E930": {"text": "every finished building has a torch by its door from the start, houses their hearth as well; a building two tiles wide or more has two (Albert, Nov 10, #26)"},
 "E931": {"text": "any queued item can be taken out, not only the last, and is paid back in full; taking out the first restarts the clock"},
 "E934": {"text": "an order's target answers: a unit glows, a thing ripples in the done colour (Albert, Nov 10, #31)"},
 "E935": {"text": "with someone picked, a tap near a resource takes it, so the target is bigger than its tile (Albert, Nov 10, #23)"},
 "E936": {"text": "your soldiers leave a wild animal alone unless it is after one of yours or you sent them at it (Albert, Nov 10, #32)"},
 "E937": {"text": "a beast that is not attacking your side is not a target for your soldiers"},
 "E938": {"text": "Lanterns (research) make the door torches brighter: light falls off as the square of distance (E = I / r^2), so a torch seen as far reaches sqrt(1 + gain) as far (Albert, Nov 10 11:51: the tech makes them brighter)"},
 "E940": {"text": "a leafy crown takes a warm gloss on its sun side, painted only over its own leaves, baked once with the tree so it costs nothing a frame (Albert, Nov 10, #22)"},
 "E941": {"text": "the pop-up over the map holds one thing, the ice's Clear button. The quick action (a tap on open ground opening Attack, Build, Rally and their steps) is cut (Albert, Nov 14 16:45, N369: \"That needs to be gone\"); logged in Parked"},
 "E943": {"text": "menus are not redrawn while a finger is down on a button (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #7: taps pressed but did nothing): a redraw replaced the button under the finger, so the click never came; the next frame after the lift draws again. The same finger drives the press (N445): the button under it is pressed the moment it lands, and let go when it leaves, but not before SCR.press.hold seconds"},
 "E944": {"text": "minus on a job acts at once: the villager drops what it carries and stands idle, so the count falls on the tap (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #10: plus already pulls someone off another job; minus did nothing while the one it picked walked its load home)"},
 "E945": {"text": "first placed, first built (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #4; AoE2's build queue): a site placed with a builder picked who is still raising another joins the end of his list; he finishes the one he is on, then walks to the next in the order they were placed. This was the cause of builders leaving a half-built site (#19, #27, #36)"},
 "E946": {"text": "an order you give marks each unit sent: its foot ring stays green from the order until its walk ends (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #9); soldiers sent to ground join a group of their own that is holding or marching only when the spot lands inside that group, within one ranks gap of one of its places; then they form up as one. Every other group keeps its own order (N423, N429)"},
 "E947": {"text": "your people under the canopy drawn as a flat ghost in your side's colour, the figure's outline only, with the ring at the feet (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #11); each figure's flat copy made once and kept"},
 "E949": {"text": "a flame's flicker by the real puffing rate (QCV, about 5 Hz for a torch), on the wall clock so game speed does not hurry it; the flame's height and its glow share one signal, so the light on the ground breathes with the flame (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #5)"},
 "E950": {"text": "campfires after dark (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #12): where two or more people stand or work together at night a campfire is lit among them, and stays where it was lit until dawn puts them all out; a light, not a building"},
 "E953": {"text": "a sound that will not come back (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #10 and #19): a phone call leaves iOS's audio interrupted and a resume that fails stays failed, so when the last resume did not bring the sound back the next tap closes the old player and makes a new one. Nov 13 (N349): still silent after a call until the page was reloaded, because a resume that never answers was never counted as failed; now the first tap after the page comes back, or after iOS reports the audio interrupted, makes a new player unless the old one is running and was never interrupted"},
 "E954": {"text": "note: a tap or an order's answer, filed in Mail as a letter, with its place if it has one (N377); War's title no longer reads it (N417)"},
 "E955": {"text": "the base and the rank row are drawn once a render and that one drawing is both compared and shown (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #11: People's ring did not recede: the second drawing numbered the Hall's queue 1 where the first had 0, and the ring read an empty slot)"},
 "E956": {"text": "a soldier trained while a rally flag stands joins the ones already marching to it or holding it, and they are dressed into one formation there (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #14 and his N13 call: soldiers arriving together take a formation, not a loose crowd; a muster forms in ranks at its rallying point); each new one re-dresses the block, which grows a rank at a time"},
 "E957": {"text": "a sprite is cached at the next size up the √2 ladder, never the one below: drawn smaller it stays sharp, drawn larger it went soft and blocky (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #21: rocks still pixelated; the nearest step could sit 19% under the zoom)"},
 "E958": {"text": "your people behind a tree or a building show through it as a silhouette, as Age of Empires II draws them (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #20): each of your people drawn this frame is kept with its box, and every tree or finished building drawn after it (so in front of it) whose box meets that box is paired with it"},
 "E960": {"text": "an army's standard groups the soldiers of one order, one rally or one march (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #8: an army out carries its torch; a dressed army gives each soldier its own spot, so grouping by spot never made a group)"},
 "E961": {"text": "the standards drawn this frame, kept so the lights put a torch on each after dark (v80's fire staff that walked with the army)"},
 "E962": {"text": "a campfire after dark by a drop-off where two or more of a side gather and bring their loads there, set just past the building's front corner, once a beat, never by a building that has its own hearth; out at dawn (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #8)"},
 "E963": {"text": "the lights add a torch on each army's standard, its glow at the standard's foot and its flame at the pole's top"},
 "E964": {"text": "an open flame's white-hot core: a bloom at its heart the flame's own height across, laid on with light (Albert, Nov 10 15:30, the fire mock)"},
 "E965": {"text": "one scratch canvas for the fire's highlights"},
 "E966": {"text": "firelight on the side that faces it (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #8, the mock): each person and finished building in view takes the nearest open flame's colour on its near half, from nothing at its middle to full at its near edge (Lambert's cosine law), as strong as that flame's glow is at its distance (the glow's own falloff) times the rim's gain, after dark only"},
 "E967": {"text": "the grass blades' tiles are made at the next step up the √2 ladder of the zoom and stretched to it, so a pinch makes a new one only when it crosses a step, not every frame (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #22)"},
 "E968": {"text": "while a pinch moves, the land sheet is stretched to the new zoom instead of drawn again; once the zoom has stood still a moment, has moved a whole √2 step, or the stretched sheet would leave a gap at the screen's edge, it is drawn fresh (D landCache.settle; Albert, Nov 10, N17 #22: zoom weird and sticky: every frame of a pinch redrew the whole ground)"},
 "E970": {"text": "a soldier whose rout has run its time comes back to the fight: he turns on the nearest foe he can see (within his sight; Nov 10: within the flee distance he often found none, having run past it), or else walks back to his place by his building (Albert, Nov 10 18:55: the rallied stood idle and a battle stalled with men left on both sides; in Age of Empires II a unit at rest takes on the enemy it sees)"},
 "E971": {"text": "the top row holds what two rows held (Albert, Nov 10 18:27): a cell named two keys joined by | shows each on its own line, a store with its icon and count, anything else from the ribbon's list; when is the season's icon with the clock over the time left, folk the people over idle and army with their icons"},
 "E972": {"text": "a tree deep in a forest is one with a tree in each of the eight directions a forest step away (the forest is planted on a grid of D forest.step, so trees never touch tile to tile); deep trees are drawn once into the woods' cached picture instead of one by one each frame (Albert, Nov 10 19:22, the speed audit: of 8,046 trees only 120 were deep, the rest drawn each frame); cutting one wakes those within a step"},
 "E973": {"text": "asking for a fresh picture marks the frame wanted; the loop draws every frame while the game runs, and while it rests (paused, a menu over it) only when something asked or the camera moved (Albert, Nov 10 19:22, the speed audit: each ask had queued a second full drawing in the same frame, so a pan or a pinch drew every frame twice, and a still, paused screen was redrawn sixty times a second)"},
 "E975": {"text": "the mist and the fog of war share one sheet, the mist painted under the fog, so the screen takes one large copy a frame for both instead of two (Albert, Nov 10 19:22, the speed audit; the land stays its own sheet, under the people, the mist and fog over them)"},
 "E976": {"text": "loading a save makes the ground's shape from its seed but does not draw it: load draws it once, with the save's things on it (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-04: the ground was drawn twice on every load)"},
 "E977": {"text": "a filled shape needs no closing stroke, a fill closes itself; only a stroked shape that was closed is closed (the ground's thousands of closings were most of drawing it: a load went from 11.7 s to 2.6 s headless, Nov 10)"},
 "E978": {"text": "a tile that opens (a tree felled, a rock mined out) joins each side's reach where it touches it, flooding on from there, instead of every side's reach being worked out again over the whole map (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-01)"},
 "E979": {"text": "a felled tree lowers the top of its own tile and its sight cell only, and the sight caches are told the view changed (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-02: one felled tree recomputed the tops of every tile on the map)"},
 "E980": {"text": "the map's tops are worked out again in full only when a building or a find goes, not a tree (cut one by one above) nor a person (never in the tops)"},
 "E981": {"text": "food in reach is food a side can carry home: a find or prey within the hunger book's reach of one of its own food drop-offs (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-06: any berry bush on the whole map kept a side from famine)"},
 "E982": {"text": "a healer heals everyone of its side within its reach, villagers too, as Age of Empires II's monks do (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-10: only troops were healed); the garrisoned heal when the building they shelter in heals"},
 "E983": {"text": "a bow's reach from a height: the arrow's flight (its drag and gravity, QAJ) at the speed that carries it its flat range, flown from the height the shooter stands above where the target stands, so a tower or archer on a hill shoots farther downhill (Gemini's audit, Nov 10, BUG-08: the hill was ignored); uphill it keeps its flat reach, since a real archer raises his aim, which one fixed angle cannot show"},
 "E984": {"text": "your hidden people, under the canopy or behind a tree or building drawn after them, show as their ring only, dashed and twice as thick, in your colour, on top of what hides them; an idle villager's ring glows and dims (Albert, Nov 10 20:03-20:06: no silhouettes)"},
 "E985": {"text": "a person counts as hidden by what is drawn in front of him only if that thing has ink at the middle of his figure, not merely a box that meets his: each sprite's ink is read once and kept"},
 "E986": {"text": "the picture's resolution steps down with the draw level, three quarters then half, and back up as frames come quickly again (Albert, Nov 10 22:47: lower resolution when the frame rate drops)"},
 "E987": {"text": "every untouched tree is baked into the woods' cached picture (Albert, Nov 10 21:08-21:10, option B); a tree leaves it at its first cut, so the cache never shows a tree smaller or gone; a tree with trees a forest step away all round is inner and casts no shadow of its own (the woods' own shade)"},
 "E988": {"text": "the trees standing in front of a person, a thing or a building this frame (lower on the screen, their pictures overlapping, looked for cover tiles all round its footprint, as the board is turned) are drawn again over it in their place in the order, so depth stays right while the rest of the forest comes from the cache; a burning tree is drawn live for its flames (N23: buildings had been left out, so a tree in front of the hall was drawn behind it)"},
 "E951": {"text": "a lightning flash is three to five return strokes about 60 ms apart (CIGR\u00c9 TB 549), each re-lighting the bolt and whiting the sky by its nearness; timed on the wall clock, so at triple speed it is as startling as at one (Albert, Nov 10, N17 #15)"},
 "E999": {"text": "one route for a whole order (Albert Nov 11, N325: 'clean up how army is controlled wholly'): a soldier told to march is set on a path it is handed, or waits a staggered moment (D372) and finds its own. Before N25 every soldier searched the whole map for itself on every tap: twenty soldiers were twenty searches, measured at up to 80 ms a tap and 215 ms on water"},
 "E1000": {"text": "the route of an order: the soldier nearest the middle of the group finds the way once; each other soldier walks a short way onto that route (within D372 near, a short search of D372 tries), follows it, and leaves it at the end for its own place in the formation. One long search an order, not one a soldier. The leader's search goes as far as it takes (findPath's far search, N447), so an order across a forest finds its way"},
 "E1001": {"text": "a tap the army cannot reach (water, a cliff top, inside a wall) is moved to the nearest ground it can reach within D372 snap tiles, so the order still means something; none that near, the order is refused and says so (J50 why.noWay)"},
 "E1002": {"text": "Defend (Albert Nov 11, N325: 'Defend goes right to the attack', no spot to pick): of the foes now striking what is mine, the one striking the dearest thing (D373: the hall, then people, then buildings, then soldiers), the nearer first; every picked soldier not already fighting is sent at it. Returns how many went and where, 0 if all are busy, nothing if no one is under attack. The order of worth is Claude's design, for Albert to play"},
 "E1003": {"text": "picking soldiers on the board (a tap, a second tap, a dragged box) opens the Controller with exactly those picked ('who' is 'picked'): Albert Nov 11, 'the drag a box is still kind of nice, so is the tap one and tap thing'"},
 "E1005": {"text": "what they do: Attack lights and waits for a spot on the map, then Execute; Retreat sends the picked home at once; Defend goes at once (E1002). Albert Nov 11: no more than two taps for the urgent ones"},
 "E1006": {"text": "a tap on the board while the War card is open: on my own soldier it picks or lets go; with soldiers picked (by hand, or All, a Class, a Squad, Idle) and Attack or Move armed, the tap is that order at once, at the thing tapped (or seen under the tap) when it is not mine, else at the spot, and the pick ends (endPick, N435; Albert, Nov 11 23:36: \"I don't have a way to move the army. I have to tap attack then execute then go\"); with nothing armed it only places the aim, and a second tap on the same aim takes it away"},
 "E1007": {"text": "the map's things that are not trees, kept as one list and remade only when a thing comes or goes (as E709 keeps the buildings): of 8,500 things about 8,150 are trees, and every question that cannot be about a tree asks this list. Measured Nov 11: the rules took 8.2 ms a step with 360 people, 3.0 after this and E1008 to E1014"},
 "E1008": {"text": "who works what, counted without walking the whole map: only the things worked last step are cleared, then each worker counts onto his own"},
 "E1010": {"text": "which villager a wild animal is fighting, gathered once a step; before, every villager searched every unit every step"},
 "E1011": {"text": "whether food is within reach of a hungry side, asked once a second, and everyone fed in one pass once a second (D-peaceBeat) with the seconds since the last meal"},
 "E1012": {"text": "the trees near a spot, by the buildings' grid (D186), remade at most once a second: a felled tree is skipped by its amount"},
 "E1013": {"text": "wood is searched for near the worker, not across the map: within his search circle, doubled until a tree is found; tree farms are always candidates"},
 "E1014": {"text": "what a side can walk to is kept through building changes for one slow beat (D-beats.slow): before, every building placed made each computer flood the whole map again, a step of 100 to 200 ms"},
 "E1015": {"text": "the fire-light rim of a figure or building, made once for its picture, the light's kind and one of dirs directions (D-light.rim), then stamped; before, each was tinted and masked again every frame"},
 "E1016": {"text": "a light's glow painted once a kind and stamped at its size and the night's strength; before, a fresh gradient for every light every frame"},
 "E1017": {"text": "ice-shy (Albert, Nov 11: \"They see their comrades fall through the ice and they just continue\"): when ice cracks under a side or one of its people drowns, everyone of that side on the ice walks to the nearest shore and, for a season, none of them steps on ice; a march under way is taken up again from the shore, by land or by a ford (E1018)"},
 "E1018": {"text": "every lake has a ford (D374): a shallow bed through its middle, toward the middle of the map, laid without the dice so a map's other rolls are unchanged"},
 "E1019": {"text": "a struck soldier is heard: his own within crowd tiles (D-nerve) who stand idle, hold, or march sent, with no foe and not told to hold, turn on the attacker, once a scan (Albert, Nov 11: 60 of 102 stood idle while \"Your spearman is attacked\"; N423: the sent too)"},
 "E1020": {"text": "my soldier left idle far from his post (past the yard, D-yard) holds where he stands and does not walk home alone (Albert, Nov 10: soldiers move only on his command, an enemy, or an animal attacking them; measured Nov 12: of 40 sent at a hall, 14 walked home across the map once it fell); Retreat still sends them home"},
 "E1021": {"text": "a computer thinks in slices across steps (E684): its hall can fall between two slices, and the next slice then asked a hall that was gone for its villager (a TypeError, found Nov 12 by sending 40 soldiers at a hall; in the match it stopped that step half done and counted toward Something broke). The thinking now ends the moment the side has no hall"},
 "E1022": {"text": "the Market sells and buys by the lot at the going price (D270, D271), the Workshop is set to cloth or beer, a mercenary camp is hired from its card: all were built in econ.js with no button (Audit D, Albert Nov 11: show it all; from the parked build 3, without the Mint's debasing, which he refused)"},
 "E1023": {"text": "a caravan takes a trade route two ways: Trade route on its card sends it to the nearest trade stop not held by a foe (the safest; measured Nov 12, the best-paying stop was 217 tiles off and the caravan died on the road), or pick it and tap any trade stop for a longer, richer run; its card says where it trades, or why it stands idle (Albert, Nov 11 22:48: only the computers could set a route)"},
 "E1024": {"text": "the Relations and Misfits rows work: each shows your stance (Foe red, Neutral white, Friend green); War, Terms and Ally go through setRel (a notice before war, an envoy for terms or alliance, a group by its regard); Bribe gives a group gold for regard (N24 #12, Albert: stances and envoys work; from the parked build 3). A side's Gift waits: there is no gift to a side in the rules yet"},
 "E1025": {"text": "no food for a villager: the People icon wears the cannot-afford fade, red at nothing to white as the food comes (Decisions Nov 11, #22: red fade, not greyed out)"},
 "E1026": {"text": "a tower, Town Center or castle shoots: its reach is measured from the tile it stands on. A building has no tile field, so its height over the target, and with it its hill reach, came out not-a-number and nothing was ever in reach. Found Nov 12 from Albert's \"tower not shooting\": no building in v100 had ever shot. (Its reload timer also starts from nothing now; that alone had not stopped it.)"},
 "E1027": {"text": "Focus (Decisions Nov 11, #17; Design 08, Nov 12): a villager is focused only when her Attention is Focus (E1053), never by a tap alone (the Nov 11 rule that every tap focused her was cut Nov 12: it took villagers out of the jobs row and tangled gathering). Focused: she does not move on to a richer find while it lasts, is the last picked to build or to leave a job by the jobs row, and after sheltering goes back to it. A new order from you, or the jobs row, ends it. Told (N437), apart from Focus: a tap that sends her to a find, or any post she is set to, is remembered; she does not move on from it at a drop-off, the danger map does not pull her off it, and after sheltering she goes back to it; unlike Focus it does not hold her out of the jobs row. A new order from you, or the jobs row, ends it"},
 "E1029": {"text": "a find you can gather that stands behind trees shows its ring through them, dashed like your hidden people's (E984) and in the find's own colour, once you have explored there (Decisions Nov 11, #9: an outline through the canopy for things you can act on). The gold-over-trees draw order was checked Nov 12 and is right: trees in front of a find are drawn after it (E-covers)"},
 "E1030": {"text": "one schedule for everything that waits its turn in a building (Decisions Nov 11, #19): for each item its time until it starts and until it is done, counted from the timer of the one running; the queue row, the tech tiles and (to come) a villager's stops read it. Tech has no queue row (#18): tap as many tiles as you like, each paid at the tap as before and run in tap order with no cap; a waiting tile is blue with the time until it starts, the running one green with a draining ring and the time until it is done, in the place of the cost; a tap on either cancels it and pays it back. The queue row keeps the people being trained and the age"},
 "E1031": {"text": "Protect's three (Decisions Nov 11; Albert: Protect is really a lure): each garrisons your villagers as Garrison does, and those the buildings cannot hold do the one you chose. Split: they scatter split tiles (D-alarm) across a fan (half a turn) away from the threat, each his own way, so a raiding band must break up to chase. Lure: they run to your nearest building that shoots. Seek: they run to your nearest building that trains soldiers. With none to run to, they wait behind the hall as before. Gather and All hands have no button on this page now (Parked)"},
 "E1032": {"text": "an order's food is charged by the ground marched, not by the tap (Decisions Nov 11, #4; Albert: \"moving everyone at once makes people hungry in real life\"): a soldier marching under an order eats his ration times Pandolf's walking power over his standing power, 1 + walk × v² / stand (D224, v his own pace in m/s): 3.3 times at 1.52 m/s, only while he walks; standing, holding or fighting he eats as before. (Nov 12, N29) The share is now a field day against a garrison day, 1.37 (D224 marchDay, Tharion 2005), not the walking minute's power against standing (3.3): a soldier at home eats one ration, on the march 1.37"},
 "E1033": {"text": "Prep (D375): one tap and every villager, working, idle or sheltered, stops and walks to the nearest of your buildings not yet boarded (two to a building, D-builders crew; walls, fields and traps are not boarded), pays its boards and hammers; boarded, the building holds add more health and the villager goes inside it, or on to the next building, or into any shelter, or waits behind the hall. Work takes the boards off and sends everyone back: before any attack has landed near the town (D-alarm home) each building is left short by back of what was added; after one, nothing is lost. No cooldown and no timer; boarding again is the same price and the same risk. On the Protect page Prep and Work share one cell: Prep in peace, Work while an alarm or Prep is on (Claude's placing)"},
 "E1034": {"text": "a boarded building shows its planks across its foot, one by one as they go on"},
 "E1035": {"text": "the pace meter's laps: with ?fps on, the time between one drawing layer's end and the next is averaged a layer, and shown as the meter's second line (Albert's number one, the freeze: nobody could say which layer heats his phone; now his own screenshot does)"},
 "E1036": {"text": "an idle soldier walks home once: if his home spot cannot be stood on (built over, a tree, water) he takes the free tile nearest it as home; if no way leads there he is home where he stands. Before, he searched the whole map for a way every second and failed every time: measured at minute 9 of a four-side match, 2,009 of 2,149 searches in two minutes failed, half of all the rules' time (10.7 ms a step); the freeze's largest single cause found so far (Albert's number one)"},
 "E1038": {"text": "the tap table (SN43, Albert Nov 12 08:12-08:15): with something picked, the next tap is its order. What was tapped is named (foe, prey, find, site, hurt, own, stop, mine, ground), each picked unit finds its row (villager, soldier, caravan, any) and the units of each action go together: gather, hunt, build, repair, work, attack and go through the war module's order; fight, garrison and route their own. After any row everything picked lets go, soldiers too, unless the ice question is waiting. A tap on another of your units while something is picked is item 2 (no row: nothing happens, the pick lets go); with several picked by a box or the Controller it still adds or removes"},
 "E1040": {"text": "what is under the finger while something is picked (E1038): another of your own units counts only if the finger is on it (D246 armed, not the wider hit), and a find nearer the finger wins. Before, four villagers on a bush made the bush untappable, and a tap beside the picked villager picked a neighbour: he stayed picked (Albert, Nov 12 08:05, his screenshot)"},
 "E1039": {"text": "garrison (the tap table's soldier + own building): each soldier goes inside up to the building's hold (D-hold by stat), the rest walk to it and are told how many found no room. Uses the shelter's own door (enter)"},
 "E1041": {"text": "the job door: every unit's job is one property with one setter, so all of the code's writes (75 in N29: econ 41, combat 31, menu, ai, the world) pass one place. It keeps the job before and when it changed (FK.jobWas), so a card or a test can say why a unit stopped, and it records any job not in the list (D jobs, FK.jobOdd). Units from a save get the same door when they load. Plan P2 (Nov 12): the first step; the rules for what comes after a job stay where they are until each has its test"},
 "E1042": {"text": "the health door: every loss of health (a blow, fire, sabotage, a charge's trample, a flood, a sinkhole, a stampede) passes one function that lowers it and records who or what did it and when (t.hitBy, t.hitT). Plan P3 (Nov 12)"},
 "E1043": {"text": "one health bar: the war module draws its bars with the world's own (index.html bar), not a line-for-line copy (Repeated names - Nov 12, merge 1); the menu asks the war module whether a tech is known (merge 2)"},
 "E1044": {"text": "a world event's walker goes in legs (D events leg): each leg is a short search toward the far side, and the next is found when the last ends; it leaves the board when it reaches its goal or no leg can be found"},
 "E1045": {"text": "a caravan's escort (Albert, Oct 27): its card has Escort +4 (the nearest idle soldiers of yours, up to the trade book's guard of 12) and Release. An escort follows the caravan; robbers leave alone a caravan with one of its soldiers near (D-trade near)"},
 "E1046": {"text": "the convoy: an escort that falls behind walks back to its caravan, and the caravan waits while any of its escort is too far (D-trade keepUp, wait; pace state convoy). Measured before (N30): escorts trailed 14 to 21 tiles behind, outside the 6 tiles that keep robbers off, and all three caravans died"},
 "E1047": {"text": "one tap rule on the war page too: a tap on a villager (or any of yours that is not a soldier) picks it, and its next tap is its order by the tap table, as on the jobs page. Before, the war page swallowed it as an aim (found by the N30 test)"},
 "E1050": {"text": "one place lets the pick go (letGo), and endPick uses it after every order: soldiers and villagers alike, from the map, a card or the War card (Albert, Nov 12 11:32-11:33: \"Touch a villager. Touch a thing. DESELECT.\"; Nov 21, N435: \"When I send anyone to do anything the selection of it should end\"). Placing a building sends every picked villager to build it by the tap table's site row. A building placed with nobody picked goes to the villager already building, at the end of his list (ECON.builder; Albert, Nov 14, N369: one villager, site to site); with no builder yet, autoBuilder picks one"},
 "E1051": {"text": "the call (Design 08, N331): with no New Group, a tap on the unit you called hangs up (the pick ends, it carries on); a tap on another of yours moves the call to it; with New Group (More) a tap adds or drops one"},
 "E1052": {"text": "the call's refusals (Design 08): a soldier sent to a site or a find gets a toast and stays where he is; villagers sent to a find with no free spot go to the nearest find of the same kind (gatherAt) and the toast says so; the pick ends either way (N435)"},
 "E1053": {"text": "Attention (Design 08): Normal is the default and no tap focuses; Focus pins a villager to the find or post you send her to and, when it runs out, sends her to the Town Center to wait; Mobile is first picked by + and by a site needing a builder, Focus last; a tap that sends her to a find tells her (N437): she keeps to it at each drop-off until it runs out, whatever her Attention"},
 "E1054": {"text": "the load rule (Albert, Nov 13, N335): a villager sent to another kind of work while carrying takes the load home first only when its drop-off lies on her way (nearer to her than the new work, and nearer to the new work than she is); otherwise she drops it and goes. No number: the geometry decides. Destroy (her setting) still drops at once. Before Nov 13 the load always went home first (Drop) unless Destroy was set (E1054, Nov 12)"},
 "E1055": {"text": "the unit card of the call (Design 08, P2b): a called unit's card opens with its status and how many of yours do the same (Select the rest), Add task, Build and Cancel; under them folded rows Orders, Attention, Load (villagers), Group, History, Statistics and Exit. A chevron opens one row, a minus closes it; one open at a time, all closed when the card opens (Albert, Nov 12 17:52) Exit kills through WAR.die, the one death path: the unit falls, leaves the board and frees its place in the head count (Albert, Nov 14 22:05, N371).. N62 (N385: \"Kill the villager cards for now. We only need: select, kill, hold, go\"): the unit card's rows and lists are cut (Parked); a lone unit of yours that is neither villager nor soldier opens its card in the dock (Manage), as does a double tap on any unit; Exit stays there"},
 "E1056": {"text": "Add task (Design 08): the card asks for the next task; taps on the map are queued on the unit (plan) until Done; when the unit's task ends (idle, or a build done) the next queued task is given through the tap table"},
 "E1057": {"text": "a unit's record for its card (Design 08): spans of what it gathered (merged while the kind stays the same), builds and idle spells, the total it gathered, what it ate, and when it came"},
 "E1058": {"text": "the villager Controller (Design 08 section 8, N333): a called villager (or a group of them) takes the war Controller's mold. Pads read clockwise for one thumb (top left, top right, bottom right, bottom left; the grid lays them out row by row, so the 3rd and 4th trade places in code). Brown: People, Garrison (into the nearest of your buildings with room), Log (her card with History open), Build. Blue only picks: Deposit or Drop (her load), Focus or Mobile (her attention; tap a lit one to go back to Normal). Red: Group (everyone on that same spot; the counter says how many), Stop, Jobs (opens Gather, Help build, Hunt, Repair in the middle pad), Order (the next tap is queued). Top: Home, Exit (skull, two taps), Restart (puts back what she had when called), the pill, Hide, ✕ (back a page, else hang up), War Exit kills through WAR.die, the one death path: the unit falls, leaves the board and frees its place in the head count (Albert, Nov 14 22:05, N371).. N62 (N385): Log is cut with the unit card; the brown pad holds three"},
 "E1060": {"text": "Jobs fine-tunes the next tap (Albert: \"the village control is meant to fine tune\"): with Hunt picked, a tap on a tree is refused with a toast and she stays called; tapping without a job picked works as before"},
 "E1061": {"text": "the ground picture repaints when what is on it changes (Albert's freeze fix, Nov 13, N334): the season colour, the snow step, the blooms, the camera, or a new scar (SCARV counts them); the timer only catches slow things the key does not see (flowers trodden, every 10 s, not every second). With snow on the ground one repaint costs a lot, so a repaint every second cost frames"},
 "E1065": {"text": "who gives way (D377 priority, Albert Nov 13 09:39, N339): each of two who meet has a level by what it is doing (at work 3, on the move 2, at rest 1); the lower takes the whole push and the higher stays; equals part by mass as before. If the lower cannot be moved (the ground behind it cannot be walked: a building, a wall, water, trees, a find), its level is added to the press on the higher, with the push it would have given"},
 "E1066": {"text": "the exception to the levels (N339): after every pair is settled, anyone whose press (the summed levels of those she blocks who could not be moved) passes her own level gives way by their summed push; the press is counted fresh each step"},
 "E1067": {"text": "fish along every river and stream (N341): the lakes' own spacing along the bank (2π × D218 per), alternate banks, walked out from the middle to the bank and set inset back into the water as on a lake; each holds 4 × the half-width × amt ÷ r0, the lakes' fish per area of water; laid with the finds' own dice so the rest of the map does not move"},
 "E1068": {"text": "by water (N341): any water or marsh tile within r tiles of a footprint; a Shore building needs it, stands on the beach or in the shallows (no tile deeper than half a wade) and is spared the flat-ground rule"},
 "E1069": {"text": "a Shore building (the dock) is laid on the beach or in the shallows: the board spares it the flat-ground rule too, as placing does (E1068). Nov 13, N348: placing said yes and the board said no, so no dock could be built at the water's edge"},
 "E1070": {"text": "a bulk sale at the Market (N350): bulk lots sold one after another in one tap, each at the price the lot before it left, so 1,000 pays less a lot than 100 (the going price, QAE); the cell shows the whole sum before the tap by walking the same lots on a copy of the stock"},
 "E1071": {"text": "the standing wonder nearest its win (N351): one home for the judge and for the countdown under the clock, gold for yours and red for a rival's; the clock's second line counts a timed game down from the game's own length, not the book's default (it read -0:00 in every untimed game after minute 15)"},
 "E1072": {"text": "what grows back (the Regrow tick, D378, N353): the law is written once for the tick, not for fish by name; a find with a root is never taken off the board: emptied, it keeps its root, stands bare (not a find to anyone) and comes back at the turn of spring"},
 "E1074": {"text": "a building going up, as in real life (Albert, Nov 13 22:51, N355: \"Foundation, frame, finishing\"): first the foundation, a stone slab laid over the staked plot; then the timber frame, posts and rails rising to the wall plate and rafters to the ridge; then the finishing, the building itself filling the frame from the ground up. A plot too low for a frame (a field, a trap) goes from slab to finish. Everything is drawn on the building's own axes (Albert, 22:54: the scaffold stood on different axes from the building): the frame's posts stand on the four corners of the plot as the board projects them, its rails and wall plate are the plot lifted, its ridge runs between the middles of two sides; the finished part is cut along the plot's near edges lifted to the height built (E1076), not at a line across the glass. The bar and the idle mark ride the top of whatever stands"},
 "E1076": {"text": "the finished part of a rising building is cut along the plot's two near edges lifted to the height built, so the top of the walls runs on the building's own axes, not straight across the glass (E1074)"},
 "E1077": {"text": "fish in the sea (N357): along each of the four coasts, every sea spacings, the walk goes from the beach out to the first water and lays a spot one step past it; a dock on the shore works them as it works a lake's"},
 "E1083": {"text": "a sea fish is laid only where someone can stand to catch it (N361): of the spot one step past the first water and the first water itself, the first whose ring of standing places (E2) touches ground shallow enough to walk; where neither does, that stretch of coast gets none"},
 "E1084": {"text": "the woods' field reads the board's own coordinates (N362): one field over the whole land, so no two corners grow the same woods; only the thickening away from home is still measured from each corner's own Town Center"},
 "E1085": {"text": "a clearing, one randomized element of Z4 (N362, N363): a disc of flat land kept free of trees, laid by the dice, apart from the others; a rich one is laid for every pair of homes, six with four players, where both homes of the pair are about as near as the nearest home, so each side has three and shares each with one rival"},
 "E1086": {"text": "a path, the other randomized element (N362, N363): a winding line kept free of trees, from clearing to clearing along the shortest tree that joins them all, a few more links for a second way round, and one from every home to its nearest clearing; the middle is one of the clearings; none runs straight and none points at a rival (the bare lanes from each corner to the middle, which read as trails to every side, are grown over)"},
 "E1087": {"text": "a rich clearing's deposits (N362): what the home pocket holds, without the trees (berries, gold, stone, iron, the pocket's own counts and richness, D62), each kind a cluster a quarter turn from the last around the centre, leaving the middle and the rim open to build on"},
 "E1088": {"text": "dock + fish, one element (N365): the dock is worked like a farm (the Field tick: one worker, its builder takes it up, the catch landed on its own boards); its fish are its own stock, set when it is laid from the wild spots in its reach, each counted for one dock only; a wild spot is never worked directly, and a villager sent to one goes to the least busy dock of her side that reaches it; fished out, the dock keeps its root, rests bare and comes back at the turn of spring (Regrow)"},
 "E1089": {"text": "the focus rule in one home (Albert, Nov 11: a focused unit stays on its job; its find gone, it walks to the Town Center): it held only when she emptied the find herself and banked the load; with four to a tree (N364) another villager can finish her tree under her, and empty-handed she went looking for another. Now both ways end at home"},
 "E1090": {"text": "the mine shaft (N366): once a side has Blasting, its Mining camps are worked in place for gold, one miner each, straight to the stores (the Quarry's way: the Store tick), with a stock like a field's that is sunk again for a share of the camp's price; before the research a camp is only a drop-off, as it was"},
 "E1091": {"text": "the Pioneer (N367): a unit that carries the Fell tick walks into the woods though its body is an engine's, at the woods' own pace, and fells what stands within its lane; a felled tree is the same tree (one thing, its wood kept), taken out of the woods' mask and the baked picture, so engines and wagons follow where it went and villagers gather the logs; nothing regrows (Albert: \"Permanent. This is the point\")"},
 "E1092": {"text": "an order to ground is obeyed (N368): a soldier sent to a spot looks for no foe while he marches there; the mark is cleared when he arrives and holds. Struck on the way, he and his own nearby kill the one who struck (E1019), look for no other, and march on (Albert, Nov 20 05:01, N423)"},
 "E1094": {"text": "the side's builder: a villager raising (or walking to raise) a building that is not a wall. The menu hands him the next site placed, so one villager goes site to site, first placed first built (E945), unless the player sends another (+ Villager, or a villager tapped onto the site)"},
 "E1095": {"text": "the trade roads: each route one road from the last open land of the main land (E1111) on its coast, through the open tile nearest each stop's fixed place, to the other coast, each leg the cheapest way (E1109), the whole rounded (E1110); a place with no way to it is passed by; the two routes cross the board, so their roads cross (Albert, Nov 15 12:32: coast to coast, cross somewhere, never in water; N383)"},
 "E1096": {"text": "one ground law: a tile's top layer is its stratum, except that worn road shows dirt where grass would grow (a road is a cut through the grass, as a lake is a cut through the land)"},
 "E1097": {"text": "the trees are set, every tile of woods one tree: wood by size, and a tree laid by amount (a cluster's) is a broad old tree (D345, N398); the road's strip fells none (N374)"},
 "E1098": {"text": "the trade booth, one frame in two states: the stop's empty booth (plain canvas, its wanted ware on the sign and the counter, stock around it) and, built on it, the Trade post: the same booth held (the holder's stripes, bunting and three pennants, every ware on the counter, cloth hanging, a scale and coins, a handcart, the trader, a ring); drawn with the building brushes so it sits in the game's own light and line (N375)"},
 "E1099": {"text": "a stop draws its empty booth from the Trade post's own art, with its wanted ware; once a post stands on it and holds it, the post is drawn instead (Base's and v80's rule)"},
 "E1100": {"text": "one home for messages: a letter is filed in Mail (merged with the same letter of the last moments, the oldest dropped past the keep); say files what the world tells, note files what a tap or an order says back (N377)"},
 "E1101": {"text": "what of mine is under attack: every hostile whose target is mine and alive (one finder for Defend and the alert button, N378)"},
 "E1102": {"text": "the army's fronts: my soldiers and support grouped by their order, with those outside the home zone (Z1) and on no order as one more group; each front is its centre (N378)"},
 "E1103": {"text": "look: the camera jumps to the next spot of its kind, alert or army; the same button again goes to the next, round and back to the first (N378)"},
 "E1104": {"text": "the two look buttons beside Home on the top row: the alert red while something is under attack, the banner dim when no army is out (N378); the yellow circle's spots are mine who are sick (N397, Design 20 B)"},
 "E1105": {"text": "the trade roads drawn into the ground once: one smooth round stroke per road, a sand verge under a dirt track, following the land's height (N379); every point is on open land (N383)"},
 "E1106": {"text": "the research tab: a parchment pill in red ink with a red open book, and the count of what can be started when more than one (v80's badge, N380)"},
 "E1107": {"text": "a trade stop's seat: the nearest free road tile to its fixed place with no find within room tiles and no stop within apart tiles, looked for within find tiles, then twice that (N382)"},
 "E1108": {"text": "where a road may not go: water and the shallows (under the sand's top) and, by the road's width and verge, the land beside them and round every find but the trees it clears (N383)"},
 "E1109": {"text": "a road's leg: the cheapest way from tile to tile over open land (A*, eight ways, octile distance to guide it), each step costing its length times the tile's ground (1 to 1 + cost by the map's fractal) (N383)"},
 "E1110": {"text": "a road rounded by Chaikin's corner cutting, soft passes, kept only if every rounded point is still on open land (N383)"},
 "E1111": {"text": "the main land: the open land (clear of water and finds by the road's width and verge) split into pieces joined by the eight ways, the largest kept, so a road's ends and stops all lie where it can reach them (flood fill)"},
 "E1112": {"text": "Back, the circle beside Close: on a card with a people chosen it steps back to the peoples; with units queued in the card's building it cancels the last unit queued and says so, its price paid back (a tap on a queued research cancels that one); else it goes back a page, or shuts the card (N385)"},
 "E1113": {"text": "a card's tab: choosing one shows its cells from the first page and lets go of a chosen people (N385)"},
 "E1114": {"text": "the More cell, in the sixth place only when a tab holds more than six: it says how many more than six, and which page; a tap turns the page (N385)"},
 "E1115": {"text": "a people's cell on Relations or Misfits: a tap chooses it, and the row then shows that people and its choices (N385)"},
 "E1116": {"text": "the card's helpers: up, your building and finished; info, a cell that only tells; docked, the thing whose card is in the dock (none under a page, the place bar, War or the villager's pads); atWork, how many of a kind a building has queued and their ring: receding on the one in hand, full on those that wait (N385)"},
 "E1120": {"text": "the fit law: a line of a dock cell, a tab or the name pill that is wider than its box is drawn narrower to fit, never under the book's share; bare words are wrapped so that they can be (N385)"},
 "E1121": {"text": "what to build, told on the cell (N386): top, the trained kind of your side that scores highest over one (none if none does); beats, the symbol of the class a kind hits hardest by combat's own vs (E282), or Buildings when it strikes only them or strikes them harder; unit, a soldier's two lines: its name, a red > and that symbol, then the book's three numbers (SN45) read from its row, a number from the book's whole up shown whole; both are worked out once for a row of numbers and kept until research makes a new row; loses, a cell naming the kind of yours that hits a thing hardest"},
 "E1122": {"text": "Help, a card in the dock (N387, mock 7): one function a tab, each giving its body and what the reading box says of the chosen cell; a cell of Help is the game's own cell (the Train tab's for a unit, the Build page's for a place, the Learn tab's for a step) under the help verb, so a tap there only chooses what to read and never buys; stepsAt, a building's research for your people; Research shows the buildings that research with learned over all, then (sub) one building's every step, a group a line in age order, a learned step saying so and a later age's dimmed; Ages leads with what your people eat a minute and the next age; the Guide is read once a tap and kept (the game is paused behind it)"},
 "E1123": {"text": "Help's verb (N387): with no word it opens Help on its first tab, from the pause drop, the game left paused; with one it sets that part of Help's state (tab, grp, sub, sel) and clears the chosen cell, a new tab also leaving a building's tree; sub, the building whose tree Help shows (the pill names it, and Back leaves it before it leaves Help)"},
 "E1125": {"text": "the button on a unit at work: it takes the last one of that kind out of the line and says so (E1112's words)"},
 "E1127": {"text": "Repair (N390): no villager need be picked: the picked one if there is one, else autoBuilder's own choice (the nearest free hand), for a site and for a hurt building alike; so Helpers is folded into it (SN47 hide)"},
 "E1128": {"text": "Demolish (N390: \"tap the icon once, red fill, tap again\"): the first tap arms it (S.dm), the second takes the building down; a second tap sooner than a double tap (D touch dbl) does not count, any other verb disarms it (act), and it lets go by itself after SN47's disarm"},
 "E1129": {"text": "a cell made while the card's model is being built (K): its verb is noted, the chosen one (S.cs is its data-v) keeps what the bar reads (its label, why not, its row), and it wears its unit's picture; its text stays white, only the cost is coloured (N397; a locked cell alone is dim)"},
 "E1130": {"text": "the building card's parts (Design 13, N390): KB its numbers and lists (SN47), KW its words (J60), KP the unit pictures drawn once, kOf a building of yours, K the model being built, KM the model of this render"},
 "E1131": {"text": "a walker's picture for a cell: its figure at SN47's fig, in your colour, drawn once a kind"},
 "E1136": {"text": "the first tap on a cell of the box selects it (the bar reads it); the same cell tapped again goes on to its verb; SN47's direct verbs act at once"},
 "E1200": {"text": "the mold (Design 14): every screen in play is one fixed line (Home, the path and name, a card's buttons, the alert, War), a control row and a tile row; Home and War never move"},
 "E1201": {"text": "who the mold is for: the army is the picked soldiers less support (priest, medic, spy); the crew is any picked walker of mine that is not army (villagers, support, carts): they get the villager card"},
 "E1202": {"text": "a building's Build group is where it sits in the tabs; a tile may wear a short name from the screen book"},
 "E1203": {"text": "a pill is a word button drawn small with a 44 tap area; a toggle is the pill track whose lit thumb is the side shown"},
 "E1205": {"text": "a tile row: six at most; over six the sixth is More and pages the rest; fewer than six sit at the right (the card shrinks right)"},
 "E1206": {"text": "a card's sides are its ticks' rows in the screen book's order; a side that plants or builds from the card reads Plant when all it makes are fields, else Build"},
 "E1207": {"text": "the reading on the line: health when hurt, a site's percent, what is left of a find, sheep, and for a foe what the spies saw"},
 "E1208": {"text": "ice by Gold's formula: a load of P kg on h cm of ice is safe under A_safe·h², maybe under A_fail·h², unsafe over it (D350 load); P the asked units' own masses (E788), as the walking rule weighs them"},
 "E1209": {"text": "the six cards the mold draws: Jobs, Build, a building, a crew, a find, ice and the Controller"},
 "E1210": {"text": "the saved group still alive; Custom+ saves a pick made by hand or trimmed with minus and plus (or any pick while nothing is saved), and otherwise picks the saved group again, until Custom+ gets its own step (N433)"},
 "E1211": {"text": "which card shows: ice, war, a crew, my building, any other subject, then Build or Jobs"},
 "E1212": {"text": "the fixed line: Home at the left; the alert circle when something of mine is attacked; War at the right (red, an X while the Controller is open); the same circle is yellow while any of mine is sick and nothing is attacked: one circle, the highest alert (N397)"},
 "E1213": {"text": "under the line the control row and the tile row; empty rows keep their height so Home and War never move"},
 "E1214": {"text": "a Jobs tile: People or a resource. People trains a villager at the hall (its tile shows the head count over the cap and the price); a resource with villagers picked sends them to that work; with none picked it rings it and makes it the rally (new villagers go there), and a second tap takes the rally off"},
 "E1216": {"text": "the Jobs | Build toggle; with a card open it closes the card and opens the page; Jobs lets the picked go and is always the Jobs page, Build keeps the picked villagers as its builders (N396, N414)"},
 "E1218": {"text": "Home: closes whatever is open; with nothing open it takes the camera home"},
 "E1219": {"text": "Cancel on a one-line card: let go of the pick and close"},
 "E1220": {"text": "Gather on a find: the nearest idle villager goes"},
 "E1221": {"text": "remember the ice answer this winter or this game"},
 "E1222": {"text": "the troop words: All clears every class, Idle and both screen boxes; Idle narrows or widens; a class word boxes or unboxes that class and adds or takes only its soldiers, so a count trimmed with minus survives adding another class; after an order has gone out the next class word starts a new pick, so two groups can be given two orders in a row (N433)"},
 "E1224": {"text": "the six orders: Hold, Defend and Retreat go on the tap; Attack and Move go on the map tap before or after them; Squad saves or picks the squad; an order taken (Hold, Retreat, Defend when someone went) lights its tile until the next tap (S.ro; N396, Design 19 B)"},
 "E1226": {"text": "send: Attack goes through the tap rows (a foe is fought, the ground marched to); Move marches to the spot whatever is there"},
 "E1227": {"text": "the Normal | Daily toggle on the new-game sheet"},
 "E1228": {"text": "a scenario is optional: a tap lights one, a second tap clears it (a normal game)"},
 "E1229": {"text": "the Rules pads: War Fog, Allies (today's Diplomacy) and Random (hazards rolled at random) each tap on and off"},
 "E1230": {"text": "whether a Rules pad is lit"},
 "E1231": {"text": "Albert, Nov 17 15:36 (The List 26 item 7): when a side reaches an age, every unit of its line upgrades to the next kind that age opens (AoE II's line upgrade), keeping its share of health and its job; the School's Teach is cut from the player's menus"},
 "E1234": {"text": "a tap on a ready book opens that building's card on Learn (Design 15 E): the book wins over what is under it, its tap area the slot; the book of the open card is gold with a white edge for as long as the card is open (N420)"},
 "E1235": {"text": "a picked building glows faintly gold from behind (Design 15 F): drawn on the back hook, before the building"},
 "E1236": {"text": "a picked villager: his name, state and actions in row 2; his job tiles at once, Build's tiles on Build (N410, N414)"},
 "E1237": {"text": "one home for sending a villager to a job: the best find of that kind (Jobs' +, and a Jobs tile with villagers picked); the jobs row ends what she was told (N437)"},
 "E1238": {"text": "a floating action word (Design 16): dim when it cannot run"},
 "E1239": {"text": "the line's parts (Design 16): Jobs | Build, the group words split by bars, the italic hint centred in the free span"},
 "E1240": {"text": "the crumb row (Design 16): crumbs, the first large, each tappable back to it; a quiet note in the middle; the actions with pipes"},
 "E1241": {"text": "a unit's state word for the crumb; finish: the crumb reads Going or Building, then after settle the menu closes, or goes to the page named (Build stays Build, N418)"},
 "E1242": {"text": "Jobs (Design 16): floating − + over each job, a + alone over People; nothing open shows only the line"},
 "E1243": {"text": "Build (Design 16): the group words on the line, Build → group → building in the crumb row, Build and Cancel"},
 "E1244": {"text": "one job's − or + from the floating row (People: + trains a villager)"},
 "E1245": {"text": "a picked villager's job tile: tap to pick, tap again to drop"},
 "E1246": {"text": "Go: the picked villagers go to the picked job, then the menu closes"},
 "E1247": {"text": "the one Cancel (Design 16): drops the last crumb; a crumb tapped drops all after it"},
 "E1248": {"text": "Build placed: the crumb reads Building, then the Build page stays open for the next building (N418); the ghost waits on a next spot for the Repeat ones (N409)"},
 "E1249": {"text": "the idle villagers (idle or waiting, not inside); Idle n over People: a tap jumps the camera to the next and picks it (Design 17, 27)"},
 "E1250": {"text": "the − above the line hides Jobs | Build and closes the rows; the + after Home brings them back (Design 17, 11)"},
 "E1251": {"text": "at the drop a villager sent to a find of another kind takes that kind (Design 17, 3: sent to wood from gathering food, it went back to food)"},
 "E1252": {"text": "placing: a still tap on the green ghost builds it; a tap elsewhere moves it (Design 17, 4, 16)"},
 "E1253": {"text": "a site of one's own: a tap only picks it and opens its card; a second tap does nothing more; Delete is on the card (N434, which overrules Design 16 to 18: no trash by the finger, no second tap that takes the site down)"},
 "E1254": {"text": "the building card under the law: Train | Learn | Talk on the line; the crumb row with the queue, Stop, Repair, Demolish and Cancel; a unit tile tapped trains one (Design 17, 26, 19)"},
 "E1255": {"text": "every villager inside or sheltering comes out to its work"},
 "E1256": {"text": "War: Shelter, Work and Out (Design 17, 5, 6)"},
 "E1258": {"text": "the road's strip: every tile within the road book's clear of a road tile, by one two-way distance sweep (a chamfer); woods there give no cover (N374, N398)"},
 "E1259": {"text": "the smallest-first queue, one home: the roads' search and the water's flood"},
 "E1260": {"text": "distance over the tiles from where src holds, out to lim"},
 "E27": {"text": "a wandering line (QAZ) from a to b, pinned at both ends; null when any point fails ok"},
 "E1262": {"text": "the item card's −: the last villager working this find goes idle (N410)"},
 "E1263": {"text": "a new game owes no upkeep and remembers no reach: the last game's unpaid seconds and its reach are dropped (Nov 20: a restart paid the last game's unpaid upkeep in its first beat, so one seed played two ways)"},
 "E1264": {"text": "the facts a row of the book may ask for, each about the mold's subject (the thing or the unit the mold is showing): the book says which facts, this says how each is told"},
 "E1265": {"text": "where a row's arg comes from: the thing's key, the unit's key, whichever of the two the subject is, or the last item queued"},
 "E1266": {"text": "the control row's actions for a state of the mold, read from the Screen book's acts list: the rows whose facts all hold, each made by the one button maker (ab, or dot for a round one), its word found in the Words book by its place"},
 "E1267": {"text": "the lists the game gives a row of tiles: the six jobs, the jobs a villager can be sent to, the buildings of the open group that this side may still raise, the ways across ice"},
 "E1268": {"text": "a state's tile row, read from the Screen book's tiles list: a row shows when its facts hold, makes one tile a thing in its list (or one tile alone), and takes the look of the first fact in clsIf that holds for that thing; blank is the empty place kept so the row does not shift"},
 "E1269": {"text": "a card section's tiles for a finished building of one's own, read from the Screen book's cardRows list; the sections and the tick each needs are the book's card list"},
 "E1270": {"text": "the one part of a card kept as code: the people a seat can talk to (the three rivals and the four groups of misfits), or one of them with the stances to choose"},
 "E1271": {"text": "a cell of the single strip is thinner than a finger, so each cell that can be tapped takes taps a full slot tall, reaching below the strip (Albert, Nov 20: the top bar back to a single strip; his 44 tap size)"},
 "E1272": {"text": "the top corners carry two round controls under the bar at the right, pause then Mail, clear with only the icon drawn: circles are controls, the bar is readings (Albert, Nov 20 17:17 and 17:19: both on the right, clear, just the icon)"},
 "E1273": {"text": "the sheets as shells: each sheet is a list of parts in the Screen book (SN56), and SHEET holds one maker for each kind of part: welcome, toggle, pair of pads, cells, head, table, blurb, list, wide, part"},
 "E1274": {"text": "the two tables a sheet can hold, Stores and Score: the columns are worked out here, the words come from the Words book"},
 "E1275": {"text": "the screen is updated in place: put() compares the new markup with what each part was last built from and swaps only the parts that changed; a part with text of its own, a ring or a button is swapped whole, a plain holder is kept and its children compared in turn, so a button that did not change stays the same button under the finger; a pressed button that was swapped gets its press back (repress), so it still springs back"},
 "E1276": {"text": "Stand: the picked foot and archers lock into a line where they are, foot in front and archers behind, facing the foe near them or the spot tapped, and hold it until the next order or a second tap (Albert, Nov 20 22:14: the hold stays until I remove it, and the archers hold too); a standing drill has no end time"},
 "E1277": {"text": "the log's extra rows, for Claude to read a match Albert played: each side's soldiers by kind, its people against its room, and for a rival its army aim, its goal and any attack it launched; who was lost that minute and to whom; Albert's own orders (when, what, who by kind, where); taps refused and why; the news with repeats folded; how it ended; errors and the slowest frame each minute (those two are not saved: they differ from phone to phone)"},
 "E1278": {"text": "a soldier told to attack a foe that walks out of sight goes on to where it was last seen, and does not stop where he stands (measured Nov 21: archers sent at a chariot 140 tiles off stopped after 8 s and were told they had arrived)"},
 "E1279": {"text": "a soldier who broke and ran does not walk back into a building on his own: until his next order he picks no building to attack, so a routed band no longer returns to a tower one man at a time to be shot (measured Nov 21: ten spearmen sent at a tower broke at three dead with the tower at 588 of 1020, then went back singly and all died) (N432)"},
 "E1280": {"text": "a band told to bring a building down keeps its nerve while it is winning: a loss beside him shakes a soldier only if his band has lost a larger share of its men than the building has of its health (Albert, Nov 21: had they stayed, the tower would have fallen; measured, ten spearmen at a tower: breaking at three dead left the tower at 588 of 1020, staying brought it down with five alive) (N432)"},
 "E1281": {"text": "entering War with nobody picked picks the whole army, both screen boxes lit and the mission tiles showing; leaving puts the troop words back to All (N433)"},
 "E1282": {"text": "the On Screen and Off Screen boxes: a lit box means those soldiers are included; the last lit box cannot be put out (the other lights instead); putting a box out narrows the pick in hand, lighting one pulls the troop words again (N433)"},
 "E1283": {"text": "the three words on the War card's top line choose what the six tiles show: Troops the kinds, Mission the orders; Mode answers that it is not built yet (N433)"},
 "E1284": {"text": "the minus and plus inside a troop tile: minus drops one of that kind, a busy soldier before an idle one and the farthest from the middle of the map in view first; plus adds one, idle before busy and the nearest first; both refuse with a word when there is nobody to drop or add (N433)"},
 "E1285": {"text": "where a soldier stands on the glass, and whether that is in view (framer: the edges of the view, the top strip and the card, read once for a whole count, N442); the middle of that view is what nearest and farthest are measured from (N433)"},
 "E1286": {"text": "the soldiers the troop words may draw on (the army less healers, priests and spies, cut by Idle and by the two screen boxes), whether one is of a kind or class, and the pull itself: everyone in the boxed classes, or the whole army when none is boxed (N433)"},
 "E1287": {"text": "in War the top line reads Troops | Mode | Mission in place of Home | Jobs | Build, a red box on Troops while soldiers are picked and on Mission while an order is armed, with the On Screen and Off Screen boxes beside the W (N433)"},
 "E1288": {"text": "the War card's control line: All | Idle | Foot | Bow | Cav | Siege | Custom+ and nothing else (the Wall button left it, N442), each word with how many it would pick now, after Idle and the screen boxes (N442); a red box on each chosen word and an unseen box on the rest so no word moves when another is boxed; Custom+ is boxed for a pick made by hand or a saved group (N433)"},
 "E1289": {"text": "the troop tiles: one for each kind he owns in the boxed classes, or the four classes when none is boxed or the kinds pass six; each reads picked/available over its name (N560), dim when there are none (N433)"},
 "E1290": {"text": "one place ends the pick after an order (endPick): whatever was picked is let go and the War card's troop words, Idle, armed order and spot are cleared, so a second tap cannot change or undo the order just given; it runs after any tap that gave an order, on the card or on the map (N435)"},
 "E1291": {"text": "an order at a foe (a unit, building or wild thing not one's own) is marked foe: its band draws no dashed ring or line where the target stood, since the target moves and the ring would be left behind on empty ground; the short aim flash on the target is all it shows (N436)"},
 "E1292": {"text": "an order marked foe has no ring on the map, so a tap there cannot pick its band either (N436)"},
 "E1293": {"text": "villagers sent to a find no path reaches within the search (D230) are told so at once, rather than going quietly to another find (N437)"},
 "E1294": {"text": "how far apart two buildings stand: the wider of their two lanes (D206 lanes, else lane), or none between two that may touch (D206 touch); one rule for every side (N438)"},
 "E1295": {"text": "your own workplaces show whether anyone works them (N439): a worked farm, pasture, tree farm, quarry, mint or foundry flies a flag in its colour (farm and pasture green, the rest what they yield), a worked mint or foundry glows as if lit within, and an empty one shows the idle z"},
 "E1296": {"text": "what befalls a band under an order is counted on the order (foe dead, lost sight, no way, broke, new order, dead); what D335 say names is logged at once, once an order (N440)"},
 "E1297": {"text": "the copy log counts each side's losses, villagers and soldiers: by the killer's side, or with no killer by the cause the death named (removed by you, drowned, sickness, stampede, trap, rebelled, fell with its side, stood down, sabotage; N440)"},
 "E1298": {"text": "the copy log writes what befalls a band the moment it matters (D335 say), and each band order's end: how long it ran, when it arrived, and what happened to it (N440)"},
 "E1299": {"text": "a find nobody can have (all run out, full or out of reach) leaves the villager idle, where you can see her, instead of waiting at the drop-off for ever (Albert, Nov 21, N441)"},
 "E1300": {"text": "idle villagers go home: idle a minute (D382 home), a villager walks to the nearest town center of her side and stands beside it; one you walked to a spot stays while she is there; a worker set to a farm, quarry, mint or the like never comes here, she waits at it (N441)"},
 "E1301": {"text": "a villager you walk to a spot yourself remembers it (park), so she is not sent home from it when idle (N441)"},
 "E1302": {"text": "FK.lum: how bright the map's picture is inside each screen box, 0 dark to 1 white, by Rec. 709 luma (N444). Each box is shrunk into its own rows of one small probe picture (one sample per D.luma.probe px) and the probe is read back once, so a look costs one read however many boxes. A box's brightness is the mean of its brightest D.luma.top share of samples, so a word half over snow counts as over snow; a box off the map reads as dark"},
 "E1303": {"text": "the dark patch's look (SN57): the red ring's box, filled with the cards' dark (b1) at SCR.patch.most, always on; a clear icon's patch is round. No glow and no easing: it costs nothing per frame"},
 "E1304": {"text": "the patch layer (Albert, Nov 21, N443): one layer between the map and the menus, one patch per floating word or clear icon. What floats: the card's top line and control line, and the clear icons under the top bar; what is filled is skipped (the circles, the screen boxes, the Idle box, the tiles, a word set to gone)"},
 "E1305": {"text": "floaters: every floating word and clear icon now on screen, keyed by its button's code and its text so a redrawn card finds its old patch. A word inside a ring box (.bx) or the title box takes the box; a bare word takes its letters plus the box's padding and edge, so every patch is the size a ring would be"},
 "E1306": {"text": "patches: lays a patch under each floater and drops the patches of words that went; run after every card is drawn, so a patch never lags its word. Nothing reads the screen (the per-word brightness look cost frames on his phone, Nov 21)"},
 "E1307": {"text": "the press's look (SN58): every button grows and brightens while pressed and springs back when let go; growing is quick (down), the way back slower on the spring curve (up)"},
 "E1308": {"text": "the press (N445): lift lets the pressed button go, but only the press it was set for, so a newer tap is never cut short; repress puts a press back on a button the card just redrew (put), so the spring back still shows when the tap changed the button"},
 "E1309": {"text": "findPath, the way for everyone (Albert, Nov 21, N447): a caller that names a budget gets exactly that search (a soldier's short chase, the seal test of a wall ring); every other way is searched as far as D.tries.far, so a long way round a forest or a lake is still found, and the search stops as soon as it finds it, so near ways cost no more. A way found not to exist is remembered for D.tries.forget seconds for that side, kind, start area (D.tries.cell tiles square) and goal, so a band of fifty does not search fifty times for a town behind walls; past D.tries.keep remembered ways the memory starts over The memory of a way not found is kept per side, kind, crossing mode and ice-shyness (so one unit's failure does not stop another that may cross), and a remembered failure counts only while it is due within D.tries.forget, so a new match or a loaded game (game time starting again) never inherits one."},
 "E1310": {"text": "the small card (Mail; SN33) keeps Albert's width, and its rows wrap their words onto more lines instead of cutting them off mid-word (the design pass, Nov 21: every Mail message was cut off, 95 px of row for 173 to 289 px of text)"},
 "E2280": {"text": "the season names the clock shows, read once from the words book (J62) instead of typed here"},
 "E1560": {"text": "attacking a group by its front line (N490, D420): a tap on one foe who stands in a group makes the group the target; the soldiers fight its front, not the man tapped; one rule for every side"},
 "E1561": {"text": "the group of a tapped foe: every live foe of his side within front.group tiles of him that the band can see as an enemy; one man alone is no group (null), so all go at him as before; it starts not closing, its middle noted now"},
 "E1562": {"text": "the band and its group, once a tick: the band is everyone still alive on the order, the group whoever of it still lives on its side; with either gone there is no front (c null)"},
 "E1563": {"text": "the group is closing when its middle moved toward the band's middle faster than front.come tiles a second over the last front.span seconds; the front is measured from the band's middle (c) and its nearest man (near)"},
 "E1564": {"text": "a soldier's man: the one nearest him on the group's front, never one deeper than front.deep past its nearest; between looks he keeps his man while that man is still on the front"},
 "E1565": {"text": "a soldier on an order at a group fights his man on its front (E1564) in place of the one tapped; with no front left he falls back to the order's own target and the usual checks"},
 "E1566": {"text": "while the group closes, the band holds its ground and lets it come: a soldier whose man is out of reach does not walk (no path, his path check waits) but still strikes or shoots once the man is in reach; an archer stepping back from foot (kite) is let be; when the group stops or pulls back, he walks to his man as usual"},
 "E1567": {"text": "the order is marked; an order at a foe is marked foe (E1291) and, when the foe is a unit in a group, carries the group (band, E1561) that its soldiers fight by the front"},
 "E1520": {"text": "the line a train order goes to (N480): the tapped building's own while it has room, else the least busy building of the same kind standing for that side with room that trains the unit; none when every such line is full; the same for every side"},
 "E1521": {"text": "a train order queues at the line with room (E1520) and pays that line's price; it gives back the building it went to, or false when refused"},
 "E1522": {"text": "lineAt shared with the menu, so a Train tap is refused only when the order itself would be"},
 "E1523": {"text": "Train (N480): refused as That line is full only when every line of that building's kind is full, the price read at the line it would go to; the card stays on the tapped building, and when the unit goes to another one a note says so and points at it"},
 "E1524": {"text": "the people button trains through the Train verb, so it gets the same lines and the same note"},
 "E1540": {"text": "who may step on ice (Albert's log, Nov 21: soldiers drowned marching on seed 3382234986, as a crossing mode let a walker onto any ice that held a person at failure, even ice too thin to bear one soldier): every walker of every side steps on only where the ice holds it at the safe load (Gold, D350), the computer and the wild only where it holds ai of them (D351), a way asked for no one in particular only where it holds a person; one already standing on the ice, as when it thins under him or cracks and he is sent ashore (E789), may walk on where it holds him at the failing load, so the way off is never shut; never a cracked tile, never while ice-shy (E1017), never when told to go around; a crossing mode then only spaces the walkers out"},
 "E1541": {"text": "a bowman stepping back from a foe (D-kite) walks there in a straight line, not by a found way, so every tile he crosses, a tile apart or less, must be walkable, not only the one he ends on: a line across a river or a lake's deep edge would leave him in water too deep to wade, where a beat finds him and the water takes him (E1540)"},
 "E1500": {"text": "a trip runs toward the danger (Albert's alarm fix, Nov 21): the straight way from a villager to a building comes nearer a threat than she stands now, and within the danger map's near (D253) of it; running away from a robber is never toward him"},
 "E1501": {"text": "shelter: a villager goes into the nearest building of her side that still has room and whose trip does not run toward the danger (E1500), else her Town Center if it has room, whatever the trip, since that is where she would gather anyway; no room, or she cannot reach it, and she is not sheltered"},
 "E1502": {"text": "the town centre gathering: a villager with no shelter walks to her side's Town Center and stands beside it, under its arrows; one already beside it, or who cannot get there, stays put"},
 "E1503": {"text": "during the Alarm, a villager left idle outside (her walk failed, her building fell, she reached the Town Center) looks again: into the nearest building with room, else beside the Town Center; nobody stands idle in the open while it rings, on every side"},
 "E1504": {"text": "the Alarm's villagers each take the nearest building with room whose trip is clear (E1501), not the sturdiest building's nearest, so a far or full shelter never sends her across the map or through the raid"},
 "E1505": {"text": "the Alarm's villagers with no room anywhere (Garrison, Shelter) gather beside the Town Center (E1502), not on a spot behind it that may be blocked or out of its arrows"},
 "E1430": {"text": "Fall back (N465): the picked soldiers that fight find the nearest enemy within look tiles of their middle, and the enemies grouped round it; none near, nothing happens"},
 "E1431": {"text": "Fall back: the spot is straight away from that enemy, past the farthest reach among them plus ranks rank spacings; the soldiers re-form there (dress), or nothing happens when they cannot get there"},
 "E1432": {"text": "Fall back: each soldier remembers the enemies it left (one shared list, so the group is known), falls back in order until it arrives (fb: fewer blows, no rout) and drops any squad order"},
 "E1433": {"text": "Fall back's beat: the soldiers falling back, grouped by the enemies they left"},
 "E1434": {"text": "Fall back's beat: once none of a group is still marching they have re-formed, so each goes back in at the nearest of the enemies they left still alive; the same rule for every side"},
 "E1435": {"text": "the war beat: squad orders, then those falling back"},
 "E1436": {"text": "the War card's missions that act at once (Defend, Fall back, Retreat, and Attack's arming): Fall back says how many fall back, or that no enemy is near"},
 "E1438": {"text": "a row of tiles, paged when it has more than six; a narrow tail tile (the War card's bell) comes after, not counted"},
 "E1439": {"text": "the War card's mission row (N465): the six missions in order with their icons, then the alarm as a narrow tile showing only the bell, green when on"},
 "E1440": {"text": "the War card's top line Troops | Mode | Mission: the open controller at full strength, the others' letters dimmed, the red box meaning set; the eye (N465) in place of the two screen boxes: plain, all troops count, tapped (red ring), only those on screen; the hint over the top line says the next step"},
 "E1441": {"text": "the mold's top line: the home circle, the hint and the top line (War: Troops | Mode | Mission and the eye), the alert, the War button"},
 "E1442": {"text": "what floats over the map gets a dark patch: the rank and the card's words, the War hint; the clear icons (pause, mail, the eye) a round one"},
 "E1443": {"text": "the War card's look (N465): the mission row six tiles and a half-wide bell; the eye a clear round icon like pause and mail, red ring when set; the hint in the italic hint style above the top line; a closed controller dims its letters, not its box"},
 "E1444": {"text": "a mission tile (N465): tapped with nobody picked it first picks All, as the All word does (the War card's opening default), then acts: Squad saves or picks the squad, Hold holds, Defend, Fall back and Retreat act at once, Attack and Move arm and wait for the map; refused only with no soldiers at all"},
 "E1400": {"text": "each match deals every computer its plan from the match seed (D390, N460): a number stream of its own, so the game's own stream is untouched; its personality drawn from the set, its numbers each times a drawn share (a count stays whole, a list item by item), its yes-or-no's turned over at their chance, its goals' order shuffled at a chance, the class it likes and the side it bears a grudge against; every computer side by the same rules"},
 "E1401": {"text": "a computer's personality is the one dealt for this match's seed, dealt once a seed and kept, so a save loads the same plan and the same seed replays the same match; yours has none"},
 "E1402": {"text": "an aim put aside (D391) is passed over for its time: the age, the army, the place that trains the army's kind, a building of its list; the next aim is taken"},
 "E1403": {"text": "an aim that has not moved for stall s (the same aim with the same age, the same soldiers or the same count of that building) is put aside for skip s (D391, N460: a second Town Center aimed at for 106 minutes)"},
 "E1404": {"text": "villagers stop at the personality's cap times its match share, and never past the room the army aim needs under the most people, so a full town still has room for soldiers (D391, N460: 146 villagers at 180 people with an army aim)"},
 "E1405": {"text": "the class it likes this match (D390): with no foe in sight every other soldier is of it, and with foes its kinds are scored liking times higher"},
 "E1406": {"text": "the side it bears a grudge against this match (D390): its odds on that side read grudge times higher, so which side it marches on differs from game to game"},
 "E1407": {"text": "the brewer is the personality dealt for this match (D390), not a fixed side"},
 "E1590": {"text": "a stat is looked up by its unit and then its name, two steps, not by a name strung together each time: in a big battle the joined name was built and hashed on every blow (5.8% of a heavy late-game step, Nov 21); same numbers, same memo, cleared the same way"},
 "E1591": {"text": "one side's remembered stats, one row a unit: stat keeps each number under its name, statRow keeps the whole row under *"},
 "E2400": {"text": "fromKnown(make, code, side) remembers anything worked out from what a side has learned, in that side's row for the code, under the maker itself (no name can clash with a stat's); learn() drops the side's rows, a new match or a loaded game drops all, so a kept value is never stale"},
 "E1480": {"text": "a soldier with no way to its foe (N470), its numbers (D400)"},
 "E1481": {"text": "what is in a soldier's way to its foe: the tiles on the straight line from it to the foe, one by one"},
 "E1482": {"text": "on each tile, the enemy building standing there (not the foe itself); the first wall or gate wins, else the first other building"},
 "E1483": {"text": "the enemy shooters (Shoot, built) within look tiles whose reach covers the soldier where it stands"},
 "E1484": {"text": "backing off: away from the middle of the shooters that reach it, spare tiles past the deepest of their reaches; none reach it, it stays"},
 "E1485": {"text": "no way to the foe (N470): strike what is in the way (E1481), keeping the first foe and whether it was told, to go back to (E1486)"},
 "E1486": {"text": "a building falls: everyone breaking a building of that side goes back to the foe it was cut off from, as told before; the way may be open now, and if not it strikes the next thing in the way"},
 "E1487": {"text": "out of reach and no path: look for one; none, the soldier breaches (E1485)"},
 "E1488": {"text": "the wall or gate first; no wall or gate on the line, the first other enemy building; nothing, none"},
 "E1489": {"text": "nothing to break: the old no way (logged, foe dropped, the told foe kept so it does not pick it again and again, waits wait path checks), then out of shooters' reach (E1484) or, out of reach already, it strikes an enemy building beside it"},
 "E2080": {"text": "stepOk: may a walker step from a tile of height h (its hAt, which around reads once for all eight ways instead of once per way) to tile b: b is walkable and the rise is within the slope of repose (REPOSE, E7)"},
 "E2060": {"text": "the mini map: drawn into the box a card sets (FK.miniBox), a square of the box's shorter side centred in it with the whole land fitted inside; MINI keeps the fit so a tap on it reads back to the map (miniAt); a blizzard whites it out"},
 "E2061": {"text": "a kind's limit for a side: its limit stat, one number an age, read at the side's age (the last when the side's age runs past the list); none when the kind has no limit"},
 "E2062": {"text": "the icons, each made once at load from the Screen book's icons (SN19)"},
 "E2063": {"text": "a dock's stock, laid at its site (the Shore tick): D218's amt × dock of its own, plus the amount of every fish find (the Catch tick) in its reach that no dock has claimed; each one counted is marked (shoal), so a shoal feeds one dock only"},
 "E2064": {"text": "a side's head count of the kinds asked (all by default): its units plus everyone waiting in its buildings' queues, a muster's plan counted one by one, so one queued already holds a place"},
 "E1445": {"text": "the War button: opening the War card (his call 9, Nov 21 18:22) picks All when no soldier is picked, as the All word and a mission tapped with nobody picked do, and arms Attack when there are soldiers, so Attack glows and the hint says to tap the map; closing it drops the soldiers from the pick and resets the who-line"}
});
